__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"LAGNA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MOON_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MOON_NAKSHATRA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"LAGNA_NAKSHATRA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return h}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLANET_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return u}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DIGNITY",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ATMAKARAKA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return c}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DARAKARAKA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return y}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"LORD_SAME_AS_TENTH",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return f}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SAV_STRONG_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return p}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SAV_WEAK_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return w}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"LOW_BINDU_PLANET",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return b}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DASHA_LORD",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return v}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TARA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return k}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"GLOSSARY",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return _}});var t=r(d[0]);const o={Aries:{themes:['identity_core','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You go at things head first, and you come across as impatient. Starting is easy for you. Finishing is where your chart makes you pay.",detail:"Aries is the moment a seed cracks open. It doesn't ask permission and it doesn't plan three steps ahead. It acts, then works out what happened. Ruled by Mars, it's the part of a chart that wants to be first: first to speak, first to start, first through the door. Its gift is courage that doesn't wait to feel ready. Its cost is a short attention span for anything that needs patience once the first thrill wears off. It also has a habit of starting fights it didn't need, just to feel alive. Anything in Aries in your chart wants to move now, not later."},Taurus:{themes:['identity_core','money_perception'],text:"You move at one speed, and people see it as calm. What looks like patience is often a refusal to be moved. That same refusal keeps you in situations after they have stopped being useful.",detail:"Taurus is what happens after the seed cracks open and has to survive. It's slow, physical and led by the senses. It's the sign of the body knowing what it needs before the mind has an opinion. Ruled by Venus, it wants beauty, comfort and things that last: good food, a stable home, money in the bank, a person who won't leave. Its gift is endurance. It can carry weight for years without complaining. Its cost is that it holds on too long, whether to a relationship, a possession or a grudge. Anything in Taurus wants to be built once and never rebuilt."},Gemini:{themes:['identity_core','mind_as_instrument','under_producing'],text:"People see you as quick, curious and a little hard to pin down. Your mind is your main tool. The cost is a habit of learning one more thing instead of finishing this one.",detail:"Gemini is the sign of the in-between: not the seed, not the fruit, but the messenger running between them. Ruled by Mercury, it's curious, quick and happiest with two things going on at once. Its gift is translating. It can take a complicated thing and make it clear to someone else, right now, in conversation. Its cost is restlessness that passes for being versatile. It can know a little about everything and struggle to go deep on one thing. It can also say one thing is true today and something different tomorrow without noticing. Anything in Gemini wants to be talked about, not just felt."},Cancer:{themes:['identity_core','emotional_pattern'],text:"You lead with feeling, and people pick up your mood before your argument. Your shell really does protect you. It also keeps out the advice you asked for.",detail:"Cancer is what protects the soft thing inside. Ruled by the Moon, it's the sign best at reading feelings. It reads a room before a word is said. It remembers how something felt long after everyone else has forgotten what happened. Its gift is real care: it can make people feel safe just by being there. Its cost is that the shell that protects can also trap. It can pull back into old hurts and drag the people it loves in with it. It can also mistake holding on tight for loving well. Anything in Cancer wants to feel safe before it will do anything else."},Leo:{themes:['identity_core','leadership'],text:"People see you before they hear you, and the room arranges itself around you whether you want it or not. The cost is that praise becomes the way you measure yourself.",detail:"Leo is the sign of the sun at its peak. It is not subtle, not modest, and not interested in being either. Ruled by the Sun itself, it wants to be seen. It has the natural warmth to make that feel good for everyone around it, not just for itself. Its gift is a generous spirit: real Leo lifts a room instead of just taking it over. Its cost is that the need to be central can turn into needing to be the only thing that matters. The pride that draws people in can also make it brittle when it's criticised. Anything in Leo wants an audience, even if it says it doesn't."},Virgo:{themes:['identity_core','service','under_producing'],text:"You come across as precise and useful, so people give you the work that needs care. The high standard that makes you good at it is the same one that stops you from finishing and handing it over.",detail:"Virgo is the harvest being sorted: what's useful from what isn't, what's ready from what needs more time. Ruled by Mercury, it's the sign of the working mind. It is precise, observant and always able to improve whatever is in front of it. Its gift is real usefulness. Virgo fixes things that were actually broken. Its cost is that the same sharp eye turned inward becomes anxiety, and turned on others becomes criticism nobody asked for. It can mistake \"not perfect yet\" for \"not good enough\", and that stalls the very work it's trying to improve. Anything in Virgo wants to be correct before it wants to be seen."},Libra:{themes:['identity_core','marriage_as_engine'],text:"People find you reasonable and easy to be around. Keeping things balanced is real work for you. It can slide into deciding by what keeps the peace instead of what is true.",detail:"Libra is the moment after the harvest when everything is weighed and shared out fairly. Ruled by Venus, it's the sign of relationship itself. It doesn't fully know who it is except next to, or in partnership with, someone else. Its gift is a real talent for fairness, tact and making people feel heard. Its cost is indecision that can look like people-pleasing. It can avoid a needed argument for so long that the resentment does more damage than the argument would have. Anything in Libra wants agreement more than it wants to be right."},Scorpio:{themes:['identity_core','depth_over_breadth','power_and_control'],text:"You give little away, and people fill the silence with their own guesses. Depth is your advantage. Secrecy is the price you pay for it.",detail:"Scorpio is what's underground: the roots, the rot, the process nobody wants to look at but that makes new growth possible. Ruled by Mars (and, in modern systems, Pluto), it doesn't do anything on the surface: not conversation, not love, not work. Its gift is being able to face what other people look away from, like grief, power, death and obsession, and come out changed. Its cost is a pull toward control, secrecy and testing the people it loves to see if they'll stay. Anything in Scorpio wants the truth, even the truth that hurts."},Sagittarius:{themes:['identity_core','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"People see you as open, full of opinions and on your way somewhere. Your range is real. That same range makes it easy to leave things ninety percent done.",detail:"Sagittarius is the seed's story turning into a belief: the meaning it takes from everything it has lived through. Ruled by Jupiter, it's the philosopher, the traveller, the person who needs a \"why\" behind everything they do. Its gift is real optimism, and a way of making people feel the world is bigger and more possible than they thought. Its cost is preaching instead of teaching and promising more than it can deliver. It also leaves before the hard, dull middle part is finished. Anything in Sagittarius wants meaning more than it wants comfort."},Capricorn:{themes:['identity_core','late_recognition'],text:"You look older than you are, and you are given responsibility early. Your chart rewards the long game, and the first half of your life pays for it.",detail:"Capricorn is the long climb: the part of the story where the excitement has gone and what's left is the work. Ruled by Saturn, it's patient, disciplined and quietly ambitious. It doesn't need applause along the way, only results at the end. Its gift is that it actually finishes what it starts, on a timeline most signs would give up on. Its cost is that it can mistake achievement for worth and work past the point of health. It also struggles to let anyone see it before it's \"ready\", which for Capricorn is rarely soon enough. Anything in Capricorn wants to have earned it."},Aquarius:{themes:['identity_core','isolation_risk'],text:"You stand a little outside the group, even when you are part of it. That distance gives you your view. It is also a loneliness other people do not see.",detail:"Aquarius is what happens once the mountain has been climbed and the view changes everything. It's the sign of the idea that's bigger than any one person. Ruled by Saturn (and, in modern systems, Uranus), it thinks in systems and futures, not in single people and the present moment. Its gift is real originality and a real commitment to fairness for the group, not just the self. Its cost is emotional distance. It can care about humanity in general while struggling to be present with the one person in front of it. It can also rebel just to be different, not because the rebellion means something. Anything in Aquarius wants to matter to everyone, which sometimes gets in the way of mattering to one person."},Pisces:{themes:['identity_core','emotional_pattern'],text:"You sense how a room feels before you size it up. Soaking things in is your gift. It means you have to build boundaries on purpose.",detail:"Pisces is the ocean everything returns to in the end. It's the close of the cycle, where the lessons of all twelve signs dissolve back into one whole. Ruled by Jupiter (and, in modern systems, Neptune), it's the sign that soaks up the most. It takes in what's around it, feels what other people feel, and struggles to know where it ends and someone else begins. Its gift is endless compassion and imagination. Its cost is escaping. It can drift, go numb or get lost in a fantasy instead of facing something painful. It can also let people take advantage of a kindness it doesn't know how to hold back. Anything in Pisces wants to merge with something bigger than itself."}},n={Aries:{themes:['emotional_pattern','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your feelings come fast and hot and are usually over before anyone else catches up. You react fast and rarely hold grudges. The cost is the things you say first.",detail:"Your feelings come fast, hot and honest. You react before you've decided to. Gift: emotional courage, because you say the thing. Cost: a temper that flares and is gone before you think to apologise. You also need to feel safe by doing something, not by being held. For you, feeling safe means moving."},Taurus:{themes:['emotional_pattern','home_foundation'],text:"You settle when your surroundings are steady. Comfort really does calm your system; it isn't just indulgence. The same need makes you slow to leave what has stopped working.",detail:"The Moon at its steadiest: you feel safe through comfort, routine, touch and things that don't change. Gift: a calm that others lean on. Cost: holding on to people, habits and grudges, because letting go feels dangerous. Your calm is real. Being inflexible is its downside."},Gemini:{themes:['emotional_pattern','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You talk your way into knowing what you feel. Silence leaves the feeling stuck. The risk is treating an explanation as if it solved the problem.",detail:"You work through feelings by talking about them. You need to name a mood to know you're in it. Gift: you can put feelings into words, and your lightness helps others breathe. Cost: thinking a feeling instead of feeling it, and restlessness when things go quiet. For you, feeling safe means conversation."},Cancer:{themes:['emotional_pattern','home_foundation','family_conditioning'],text:"Your feelings sit close to the surface, and the home you grew up in still sets your weather. You look after people partly to keep the mood safe.",detail:"The Moon at home: deep, protective, full of memory. You feel everything and forget nothing. Gift: the most instinctive caring of any sign. Cost: moods that come and go like the tide, and a habit of pulling back into your shell and dragging loved ones in with you. Feeling safe means family. The risk is never leaving it."},Leo:{themes:['emotional_pattern','creativity'],text:"You need to be seen by the few people who matter. Being overlooked hurts more than being criticised. Your warmth is real, and so is the cost of needing it back.",detail:"Your feelings need to be seen to feel real. You are warm and generous, and quietly hurt when nobody notices. Gift: emotional generosity and loyalty. Cost: needing praise the way others need air, and a pride that hides hurt until it bursts out. For you, feeling safe means being valued out loud."},Virgo:{themes:['emotional_pattern','health_discipline','service'],text:"You handle feelings by fixing something, and tidying up really does work. The cost is an inner voice that grades you on days that don't need grading.",detail:"Your feelings are sorted, analysed and quietly managed. You feel safe when things are in order. Gift: practical care, because you show love by fixing. Cost: worry as your default, and criticism of yourself and others when things slip. Feeling safe means being useful. The trap is never feeling useful enough."},Libra:{themes:['emotional_pattern','marriage_as_engine'],text:"You steady yourself through other people, so the mood of a relationship becomes your mood. Your habit of fitting in with others is older than any of your relationships.",detail:"Your feelings are tuned to the other person. You feel what the room feels first. Gift: tact and real emotional fairness. Cost: not knowing your own mood until someone else leaves, and swallowing anger to keep the peace. For you, feeling safe means harmony. The cost is the harmony you fake."},Scorpio:{themes:['emotional_pattern','depth_over_breadth','power_and_control'],text:"Your feelings are deep, private and slow to move. What you bury keeps working underground. Your strength is that nothing surprises you twice.",detail:"Your feelings run at full strength and in full privacy. You feel everything and show almost none of it. Gift: emotional depth and loyalty that survives anything. Cost: suspicion, control and holding on to a hurt for years. Here the Moon is debilitated (in its weakest sign), but that isn't weakness. It's a Moon that never learned to be casual. Feeling safe means trust, and trust costs a lot."},Sagittarius:{themes:['emotional_pattern','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"You need somewhere to go when your mood turns, and moving really does reset you. The same reflex lets you run away from conversations that needed finishing.",detail:"Your feelings need room. You feel safe when you know you can leave. Gift: emotional optimism and faith that things work out. Cost: restlessness that passes for freedom, and a habit of turning a feeling into a big idea instead of sitting with it. Feeling safe means the open road. The risk is never unpacking."},Capricorn:{themes:['emotional_pattern','childhood_weight'],text:"You handle feelings by handling the task. You were capable before anyone comforted you. The discipline is real, but it puts off grief instead of ending it.",detail:"Your feelings are held to a standard. You feel safe when you've earned it. Gift: emotional discipline and a steadiness under pressure that others rely on. Cost: a nervous system that never feels done, and trouble accepting care because you haven't \"earned\" it. Feeling safe means being capable. Let someone hold you anyway."},Aquarius:{themes:['emotional_pattern','isolation_risk'],text:"You deal with feelings from a step away, which keeps you steady in a crisis. The same distance can mean a feeling shows up months later that you never quite felt at the time.",detail:"You watch your feelings from a little distance. You feel safe when you understand what you feel. Gift: you can see feelings clearly, and you really care for the group. Cost: a detachment that comes across as cold, and surprise when your own emotions finally arrive. Feeling safe means perspective. The risk is watching your own life from outside it."},Pisces:{themes:['emotional_pattern','family_conditioning'],text:"You soak up the room and then carry moods that were never yours. The sensitivity is useful, but it means you have to keep asking whose feeling this really is.",detail:"Your feelings have no walls. Yours, theirs and the room's all arrive at once. Gift: compassion and intuition that can feel almost psychic. Cost: soaking up other people's pain and calling it yours, and escaping into fantasy when real life gets too loud. Feeling safe means pulling back. The work is pulling back and then coming back."}},s={Ashwini:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','gifts'],text:"You start fast and bounce back fast, and impatience is your normal setting. That speed often puts you three steps in before you've asked where this is going.",detail:"the healer's speed. You are fast, driven by instinct and first on the scene. You want to fix things straight away and move on before anyone can say thank you."},Bharani:{themes:['emotional_pattern','service'],text:"You carry things through to the end, including things other people drop. You really can carry a lot. The cost is a life that keeps taking on weight it didn't choose.",detail:"the one who carries what others can't. You are intense and private, and you can hold extremes like birth, death and heavy loads without flinching. But the weight builds up if you never put it down."},Krittika:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You cut through, and people feel the sharpness before they notice you're right. That sharpness is a tool, and it isn't always the one the moment needed.",detail:"the cutting truth. You are sharp and cleansing, and you can't stand padding or pretending. You say what needed saying, sometimes before checking whether the room was ready to hear it."},Rohini:{themes:['gifts','money_perception'],text:"You help things grow and you draw people in. Comfort matters more to you than you admit. That pull toward the pleasant also makes you slow to leave a situation that is only good enough.",detail:"beauty that draws people in and keeps them. You are sensual, magnetic and focused on growth, and strongly attached to what you love. The downside is that you can get possessive of the very things your charm attracts."},Mrigashira:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"You are always looking for the next thing worth having, and you rarely settle for the first. The searching is real, and it can quietly take the place of ever arriving.",detail:"the searcher who never quite arrives. You are curious and gentle, always chasing something just out of reach. The searching becomes who you are, and sometimes it keeps you from settling into what you already have."},Ardra:{themes:['emotional_pattern','reinvention'],text:"In your life things tend to break before they clear up, and you've been through that more than most. It gives you nerve. It also costs you the belief that life is normally stable.",detail:"the storm that clears the air. You are turbulent, and you bring the kind of change that alters a life. You are drawn to breaking things open to see what's really inside, including yourself. You need outside guidance more than most people do. Your urge to tear things down is hard to control on your own."},Punarvasu:{themes:['home_foundation','letting_go'],text:"You come back: to places, to people, to work you had left. The ability to rebuild after loss is built into you. That isn't the same as being spared the loss.",detail:"the return after the loss. You have renewal and resilience: the ability to rebuild cleaner each time something falls apart. You are hopeful in a way that has actually been tested."},Pushya:{themes:['service','spiritual_path'],text:"You feed and steady other people, and they trust you with it early. Your standing comes from being useful. Being needed can become the only way you let yourself rest.",detail:"the nourisher. You are protective and giving, and most at ease when you provide for others. You are often the last to let yourself be looked after in return."},Ashlesha:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','power_and_control'],text:"You read people well, including what they aren't saying, and that can slide into managing them. Your perception is a fine tool that works least well on yourself.",detail:"the one who sees beneath the surface. You are so perceptive it can be unsettling, and you can read what someone is hiding. The real question is always what you do with what you see."},Magha:{themes:['family_conditioning','leadership'],text:"You inherit standing and expectations from your family line, and the past still has a seat in the room. Authority comes easily. The question of what you did with it stays open.",detail:"the throne of the ancestors. You are proud and commanding, and you carry a family line whether you want to or not. Its duties and honour were handed down to you, not chosen."},'Purva Phalguni':{themes:['creativity','gifts'],text:"You make things and you know how to enjoy them. Rest is a real need for you, not a slip. The ease that draws people in can also put off the harder work.",detail:"pleasure as a birthright. You are relaxed and artistic, and really good at enjoying life. The risk is mistaking ease for fulfilment and never testing yourself against anything harder."},'Uttara Phalguni':{themes:['service','marriage_as_engine'],text:"You keep your word and help in specific, useful ways. Your reliability builds slowly, and people can use it up without ever noticing.",detail:"the loyal patron. You are generous inside a bond, you keep promises, and your relationships work like contracts. You are reliable, and sometimes slow to open up to someone new."},Hasta:{themes:['gifts','creativity'],text:"Your skill is in your hands, and with practice you can make what you imagine. The same control makes it hard to leave anything at good enough.",detail:"the skilled hand. You are practical and nimble, and you make real things with real craft. You need to do the work with your own hands to feel it counts."},Chitra:{themes:['creativity','identity_core'],text:"You build things that are meant to be looked at, and you notice the difference between made and well made. Care for how things look is a discipline, and it can become the whole point.",detail:"the architect of beauty. You are visually gifted, and you build striking things, real or figurative. You can get lost polishing the surface of something that was already finished underneath."},Swati:{themes:['freedom_vs_structure','money_perception'],text:"Independence is a must for you. You need slack, room to move and your own terms, and you give up income to get them. That flexibility keeps you upright and makes you slow to commit.",detail:"independence like the wind. You move freely, adapt and resist being tied down. You need enough space to breathe, or you get restless even in good situations."},Vishakha:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','becoming'],text:"You are driven by goals and can keep working toward one result for years. The hard part is the fork in the road: two good aims take turns instead of joining up.",detail:"the goal at any cost. You are driven and determined, and you get what you set out to get. The cost is that you sometimes forget to ask what the goal was actually for."},Anuradha:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','service'],text:"You keep people, and your loyalty is close to a discipline. That same steadiness keeps you in situations long after the terms stopped being fair.",detail:"devotion that outlasts the feeling. You stay loyal long past the point most people would quit. You treat your friendships and your causes as sacred. Your staying power is the gift and, when aimed wrong, the trap."},Jyeshtha:{themes:['leadership','isolation_risk'],text:"You end up the senior one, officially or not, and responsibility comes well before recognition. You earn the position, and it is lonelier than it looks from outside.",detail:"the eldest who protects alone. You are responsible and strong, and you tend to carry others without asking for help back. Isolation is the risk of being the one everyone leans on."},Mula:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','letting_go'],text:"You go to the root of things and will pull them up to look. Wanting the real cause suits research. It has also cost you situations that were simply comfortable.",detail:"the root, pulled up to see what's underneath. You like to investigate, and you are willing to take things apart to find the real base. Sometimes you tear down things that were fine, just to be sure."},'Purva Ashadha':{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','voice_income'],text:"You don't give in easily, and other people draw strength from your conviction. It carries you a long way, and it doesn't check itself.",detail:"unbeatable conviction. You are confident and persuasive, and hard to talk out of a position once you take it. Your strength is that your belief is real. The cost is not always knowing when to change your mind."},'Uttara Ashadha':{themes:['late_recognition','becoming'],text:"What you win, you win late and keep. Your chart pays for staying power, not speed, so the early years can look like proof that it isn't working.",detail:"the victory that comes late. You are patient and principled, and you win by lasting, not by speed. The things you achieve tend to actually last."},Shravana:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','spiritual_path'],text:"You learn by listening, and people tell you things they hadn't planned to. Being so open keeps you well informed and fills your head with other people's business.",detail:"the listener. You learn by hearing, and you connect through talk and stories. You care about being really heard as much as being seen."},Dhanishta:{themes:['creativity','mass_reach'],text:"There is rhythm in how you work, and often real music in your life. You are made for performing with a group, and the pace you set is hard for others to keep up with.",detail:"wealth through rhythm. You are musical and prosperous, and you get results through repetition and disciplined practice. The name means \"the wealthiest\", and that wealth is earned through steady effort, not luck."},Shatabhisha:{themes:['isolation_risk','depth_over_breadth'],text:"You work best behind a screen: alone, on the problem, with the door shut. The solitude is how you work, and it slides into isolation without anyone noticing, including you.",detail:"the healer who hides. You solve problems for others while keeping your own wounds private. You are really skilled at fixing things, except the broken parts of yourself you won't let anyone see."},'Purva Bhadrapada':{themes:['spiritual_path','power_and_control'],text:"You run hot on ideas, and the intensity is never moderate. The same force that carries a belief can burn the thing it was meant to build.",detail:"fire with a purpose. You are intense and sometimes fierce, and you can change lives. You need a real direction for that intensity, or it burns whoever is holding it, including you."},'Uttara Bhadrapada':{themes:['depth_over_breadth','emotional_pattern'],text:"You are steadier than your circumstances, and you can hold things in without letting them out. The depth is real. From outside, your restraint can look like having nothing to say.",detail:"the weight carried in silence. You are deep and patient, and you can carry huge responsibility without complaint. You are steady to a fault, and sometimes too self-reliant to ask for help."},Revati:{themes:['service','letting_go'],text:"You help other people cross over: to the next stage, the next city, the next version of themselves. The role suits you, and it puts your own crossing last.",detail:"the gentle end of the road. You are kind and caring, and yours is the last of the Moon's 27 star groups. You carry the wisdom of endings, and the difficulty of fully finishing something for someone else's sake."}},h={Ashwini:{themes:['identity_core'],text:"You come across as quick and self-starting. People expect action from you before they expect thought.",detail:"the healer's speed. You are fast, driven by instinct and first on the scene. You want to fix things straight away and move on before anyone can say thank you."},Bharani:{themes:['identity_core','service'],text:"You come across as intense and able to carry weight, so people bring you what they can't hold themselves.",detail:"the one who carries what others can't. You are intense and private, and you can hold extremes like birth, death and heavy loads without flinching. But the weight builds up if you never put it down."},Krittika:{themes:['identity_core','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You come across as direct and hard to fool. The edge in how you speak shows before your warmth does.",detail:"the cutting truth. You are sharp and cleansing, and you can't stand padding or pretending. You say what needed saying, sometimes before checking whether the room was ready to hear it."},Rohini:{themes:['identity_core','gifts'],text:"You are nice to look at and easy to be around. The pull is real, and it draws attention you didn't ask for.",detail:"beauty that draws people in and keeps them. You are sensual, magnetic and focused on growth, and strongly attached to what you love. The downside is that you can get possessive of the very things your charm attracts."},Mrigashira:{themes:['identity_core','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"You seem curious and a little unfinished, as if you're halfway to somewhere. People see you as still searching.",detail:"the searcher who never quite arrives. You are curious and gentle, always chasing something just out of reach. The searching becomes who you are, and sometimes it keeps you from settling into what you already have."},Ardra:{themes:['identity_core','emotional_pattern'],text:"You come across as sharp and unsettled, and your mood shows. People find you interesting before they find you restful.",detail:"the storm that clears the air. You are turbulent, and you bring the kind of change that alters a life. You are drawn to breaking things open to see what's really inside, including yourself. You need outside guidance more than most people do. Your urge to tear things down is hard to control on your own."},Punarvasu:{themes:['identity_core','letting_go'],text:"You come across as forgiving and hard to keep down, so people assume you are fine. That isn't always true.",detail:"the return after the loss. You have renewal and resilience: the ability to rebuild cleaner each time something falls apart. You are hopeful in a way that has actually been tested."},Pushya:{themes:['identity_core','service'],text:"You come across as steady and safe, and strangers tell you things. Their trust comes early, and it is a job.",detail:"the nourisher. You are protective and giving, and most at ease when you provide for others. You are often the last to let yourself be looked after in return."},Ashlesha:{themes:['identity_core','depth_over_breadth'],text:"You come across as watchful and hard to read. People sense you are sizing them up, because you are.",detail:"the one who sees beneath the surface. You are so perceptive it can be unsettling, and you can read what someone is hiding. The real question is always what you do with what you see."},Magha:{themes:['identity_core','leadership'],text:"You carry yourself with rank, whether or not you hold any. People place you higher than your title.",detail:"the throne of the ancestors. You are proud and commanding, and you carry a family line whether you want to or not. Its duties and honour were handed down to you, not chosen."},'Purva Phalguni':{themes:['identity_core','creativity'],text:"You come across as warm and fond of pleasure, and rooms relax around you. Being liked is the easy part for you.",detail:"pleasure as a birthright. You are relaxed and artistic, and really good at enjoying life. The risk is mistaking ease for fulfilment and never testing yourself against anything harder."},'Uttara Phalguni':{themes:['identity_core','service'],text:"You come across as reliable and decent, the one who keeps the deal, so people plan around you.",detail:"the loyal patron. You are generous inside a bond, you keep promises, and your relationships work like contracts. You are reliable, and sometimes slow to open up to someone new."},Hasta:{themes:['identity_core','gifts'],text:"You come across as good with your hands and precise with small things, so people give you the delicate work.",detail:"the skilled hand. You are practical and nimble, and you make real things with real craft. You need to do the work with your own hands to feel it counts."},Chitra:{themes:['identity_core','creativity'],text:"People notice how you look and how you make things look. In your chart, presentation is not a side issue.",detail:"the architect of beauty. You are visually gifted, and you build striking things, real or figurative. You can get lost polishing the surface of something that was already finished underneath."},Swati:{themes:['identity_core','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"You come across as independent and hard to pin down. People sense you could leave, and it shapes how they treat you.",detail:"independence like the wind. You move freely, adapt and resist being tied down. You need enough space to breathe, or you get restless even in good situations."},Vishakha:{themes:['identity_core','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You come across as driven and a little hungry. People can see you are aiming at something before you have named it.",detail:"the goal at any cost. You are driven and determined, and you get what you set out to get. The cost is that you sometimes forget to ask what the goal was actually for."},Anuradha:{themes:['identity_core','marriage_as_engine'],text:"You come across as loyal and tactful, so people trust you with the group before they trust you with the decision.",detail:"devotion that outlasts the feeling. You stay loyal long past the point most people would quit. You treat your friendships and your causes as sacred. Your staying power is the gift and, when aimed wrong, the trap."},Jyeshtha:{themes:['identity_core','leadership'],text:"You carry yourself as the senior one in the room, and often you are. Your manner keeps some people at a distance.",detail:"the eldest who protects alone. You are responsible and strong, and you tend to carry others without asking for help back. Isolation is the risk of being the one everyone leans on."},Mula:{themes:['identity_core','depth_over_breadth'],text:"You come across as blunt and unwilling to gloss over things. People find you either clarifying or harsh, with little in between.",detail:"the root, pulled up to see what's underneath. You like to investigate, and you are willing to take things apart to find the real base. Sometimes you tear down things that were fine, just to be sure."},'Purva Ashadha':{themes:['identity_core','voice_income'],text:"You come across as confident and hard to argue down. Your certainty persuades people well before anyone has checked it.",detail:"unbeatable conviction. You are confident and persuasive, and hard to talk out of a position once you take it. Your strength is that your belief is real. The cost is not always knowing when to change your mind."},'Uttara Ashadha':{themes:['identity_core','late_recognition'],text:"You come across as solid and a little formal. People treat you as a fixture, and usually you are.",detail:"the victory that comes late. You are patient and principled, and you win by lasting, not by speed. The things you achieve tend to actually last."},Shravana:{themes:['identity_core','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You come across as attentive, and people say more around you than they meant to.",detail:"the listener. You learn by hearing, and you connect through talk and stories. You care about being really heard as much as being seen."},Dhanishta:{themes:['identity_core','creativity'],text:"You carry rhythm and drive, and groups find you easy to follow. The pace is yours, not theirs.",detail:"wealth through rhythm. You are musical and prosperous, and you get results through repetition and disciplined practice. The name means \"the wealthiest\", and that wealth is earned through steady effort, not luck."},Shatabhisha:{themes:['identity_core','isolation_risk'],text:"You come across as private and hard to place. People notice your reserve before anything else about you.",detail:"the healer who hides. You solve problems for others while keeping your own wounds private. You are really skilled at fixing things, except the broken parts of yourself you won't let anyone see."},'Purva Bhadrapada':{themes:['identity_core','spiritual_path'],text:"You come across as intense and a little otherworldly. The effect is strong, and it isn't always welcome.",detail:"fire with a purpose. You are intense and sometimes fierce, and you can change lives. You need a real direction for that intensity, or it burns whoever is holding it, including you."},'Uttara Bhadrapada':{themes:['identity_core','emotional_pattern'],text:"You come across as calm, deep and hard to rush. People mistake your stillness for having no opinion.",detail:"the weight carried in silence. You are deep and patient, and you can carry huge responsibility without complaint. You are steady to a fault, and sometimes too self-reliant to ask for help."},Revati:{themes:['identity_core','service'],text:"You come across as gentle and safe to approach, so people take shelter with you before asking if you have room.",detail:"the gentle end of the road. You are kind and caring, and yours is the last of the Moon's 27 star groups. You carry the wisdom of endings, and the difficulty of fully finishing something for someone else's sake."}},u={Sun:{1:{themes:['identity_core','leadership'],text:"Your life is about who you are. You are visible, you take yourself seriously and people see you as proud. Your body follows the state of your self-respect.",detail:"People see you before you speak. Your sense of self and your body are joined. Your stamina is high and your presence is hard to miss. You are the first thing people notice about your own life. Gift: natural authority and a body that bounces back. Cost: an ego that fills every room, and taking everything personally because everything is about you. Your father and other authority figures shaped how you come across."},2:{themes:['money_perception','voice_income'],text:"Your standing and your family's money are tied together here. Income comes with a name attached, and your voice carries authority whether you mean it to or not.",detail:"Your sense of self is built on what you own and how you speak. Your self-worth and your bank balance sit in the same account. Gift: a voice with authority and a real ability to earn. Cost: money problems that feel like crises about who you are, and a pride in things you own that can crowd out people. Your family's wealth, or the lack of it, shaped your early sense of self."},3:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','voice_income'],text:"Courage doesn't come automatically; you choose it. You push through with writing, siblings and short bursts of effort, and everyone can see the effort.",detail:"You become yourself through speaking, writing and trying. Gift: courage, communication, and siblings or peers who matter. Cost: a restless sense of self, always moving, never sure who you are when you stop. Your father may have been there in words more than in person."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','childhood_weight'],text:"Your father and your home sit in the same house (area of life). Your roots are a source of pride, and they are also where the pressure came from.",detail:"Your sense of self is rooted in home and where you come from. The Sun, which stands for the father, sits in the house of the mother, so home was where you learned who you are. Gift: deep roots and a sense of self that doesn't need an audience. Cost: a life lived mostly at home, and authority figures who took over your private space. You are most yourself where you grew up."},5:{themes:['creativity','leadership'],text:"Your authority shows in what you make and teach. Children, creative work and risky bets all carry your name.",detail:"You find yourself through what you create, and what you make carries your name. Gift: creative authority, intelligence, and joy in being seen for your work. Cost: treating children (real or creative) as an extension of your ego, and pride in the product. Romance and play are where you feel most alive."},6:{themes:['service','health_discipline'],text:"You win by grinding through opposition. You meet debts, rivals and illness head on, and your body works the overtime.",detail:"You know who you are by what you overcome. Gift: strength against enemies, skill at work, health through effort. Cost: a self that needs conflict to feel real, and a father who was demanding or absent. You are strongest when you have an opponent."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','identity_core'],text:"Your standing gets worked out through partnership. People measure you by who you commit to, and that person is rarely the quiet one.",detail:"You find yourself through another person, in partnership. Gift: a partner with authority, and a self that feels complete in a relationship. Cost: letting your partner outshine you, or choosing partners who fight you for the centre. For you, marriage is a question about who you are."},8:{themes:['reinvention','depth_over_breadth'],text:"Crisis remakes you. The authority you end up with is not the one you started with.",detail:"Your sense of self is forged in crisis. You have been broken down and rebuilt more than once. Gift: courage when everything changes, and a self that survives what would break others. Cost: a father who felt distant or out of reach, and an ego tested by things you can't control. Hidden matters like inheritance, secrets and the occult shape who you become."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','becoming'],text:"Faith, teachers and your father set your direction. You take belief systems seriously and can become the person others come to for answers.",detail:"You find yourself through belief. You pass on a way of seeing the world, not a product. Gift: authority as a teacher, faith, and a father who guided you. Cost: the preacher's downside, which is sounding like a lecturer and mistaking your view for the truth. The warning for the Sun in the 9th house: you tend to be given the pulpit, and your tone decides whether people stay."},10:{themes:['leadership','identity_core'],text:"Your career is who you are. Public work is where you prove yourself, and going unseen at work feels like being nobody.",detail:"Your career is who you are. The world sees you do the thing, and the thing is you. Gift: public authority, achievement, and a father who showed you ambition. Cost: a life lived for reputation, and a sense of self that falls apart when the career does. Most traditions call this the strongest house for the Sun."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','leadership'],text:"Gains come through networks and senior allies. Your circle gives you standing, and it expects something back.",detail:"You find yourself through the group. People know you by who you're connected to, and you gain through networks. Gift: influence, friends in high places, income through community. Cost: a self defined by who you know, and a father who was one of many. Your ambitions are big and shared."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','letting_go'],text:"Recognition comes indirectly. You work behind the scenes, abroad or in retreat, and your ego gets worked on rather than shown off.",detail:"You work behind the scenes. Recognition comes late, from far away, or not at all, and you learn to exist without it. Gift: spiritual authority, service, and a strength that doesn't need anyone watching. Cost: a father who was absent or foreign, and an ego dissolved before it was built. Solitude is where you find yourself."}},Moon:{1:{themes:['emotional_pattern','identity_core'],text:"Your mood is the first thing people meet. Your mind changes quickly, and your body shows it faster than you can hide it.",detail:"Your feelings show on your face. You can't hide a mood and should stop trying. Gift: emotional presence. People feel you right away, and the public likes you. Cost: moods that rule your body, and a self that changes with the tide. Your mother shaped who you are directly."},2:{themes:['money_perception','voice_income'],text:"Your money moves with your mood and with your family's. Income goes up and down, and your voice carries feeling unusually well.",detail:"Feeling safe and having money are the same thing for you. Your bank balance calms or rattles your nerves. Gift: a caring voice, and money through caring work or the public. Cost: spending to feel safe, and family money used as emotional currency. Your mother is in your voice."},3:{themes:['voice_income','creativity'],text:"Money and momentum come through speaking, writing and performing. Your courage comes in waves, not steadily.",detail:"Your feelings need to move, through talk, writing, travel and effort. Gift: emotional courage and a mind that throws up ten ideas at once. Cost: restlessness, boredom with routine, and nerves that run hot. If the Moon also rules a money house, money comes through communication."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','family_conditioning'],text:"Your mother and your home are the centre of your chart. Comfort here is a need, not a preference.",detail:"The Moon at home. Feeling safe is your foundation, and home is what keeps you steady. Without it, nothing works. Gift: deep contentment when settled, and a mother who was there. Cost: never leaving, and moods that live in the walls. This is the Moon's natural place."},5:{themes:['creativity','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your feelings flow through what you make. Creative work and children are how your mind steadies itself.",detail:"You feel through creating and loving. Gift: creativity driven by feeling, warmth with children, and romance that feels like home. Cost: moods tied to being praised for what you make, and emotional risk-taking in love and in risky bets."},6:{themes:['health_discipline','service'],text:"Your daily routine carries your mood. Work and health are tangled together, and stress shows up in your body before it shows up in words.",detail:"Your feelings run through work and the body. Stress hits you physically first. Gift: emotional toughness under pressure and real care for serving others. Cost: anxiety as your baseline, health that mirrors your mood, and a habit of nursing others while neglecting yourself."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','emotional_pattern'],text:"You need a partner the way other people need air. The relationship steadies your mood, which puts a lot of weight on it.",detail:"You need a partner to feel complete, and that need is the thing to watch. Gift: emotional openness in relationships and a caring partner. Cost: moods ruled by your partner's moods, and feelings on public display. The public loves you; the marriage steadies you."},8:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your feelings go deep and stay hidden. You are drawn to what is buried, and the changes here are sudden, not gradual.",detail:"Your emotional intensity is hard for others to match. You work through things in the deep end. Gift: psychological depth, intuition, and toughness in a crisis. Cost: emotional ups and downs, a bond with your mother marked by upheaval, and feelings that come out as obsession. Traditionally a hard placement, but it gives depth."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','becoming'],text:"You feel your faith rather than argue it. Travel, teachers and belief are what actually settle your mind.",detail:"You feel faith rather than think it. Meaning feeds you emotionally. Gift: devotion, optimism, and a mother who was a teacher. Cost: moods tied to what you believe, and a wandering heart looking for a philosophy to belong to. Foreign places feel like home."},10:{themes:['mass_reach','reinvention'],text:"The public sees your moods. Your career is visible and popular, and it moves in cycles, not a straight line.",detail:"The public sees your feelings. You are known for how you care. Gift: popularity, a career in caring or public-facing work, and a mother who showed you ambition. Cost: emotional exposure, and moods that swing with your reputation."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','money_perception'],text:"Your network feeds you emotionally and financially. Gains come through groups, and your mood follows your circle.",detail:"Friends are family, and the group is home. Gift: a sense of belonging, gains through community, and a wide circle of care. Cost: moods that depend on being included, and a mother who was more a friend than a parent."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','letting_go'],text:"Your inner life happens out of sight. Solitude, foreign places and sleep are where your mind really resets.",detail:"Your inner life is huge and private. Gift: imagination, compassion, and recovery through time alone. Cost: isolation that drowns you instead of restoring you, a mother who felt absent or distant, and feelings that hide even from you. Know the difference between solitude and hiding."}},Mars:{1:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','identity_core'],text:"Your drive is physical and easy to see. You go at things directly, and your body carries the marks of how you do it.",detail:"People feel your force first. Gift: physical energy, courage, quick decisions, and a body that acts. Cost: temper, accidents, and a presence that looks aggressive before you open your mouth. Patience is something you learn; you aren't born with it."},2:{themes:['money_perception','voice_income'],text:"You fight for money; it isn't handed to you. Your speech is sharp, and family finances have friction built in.",detail:"You fight for money and with words. Gift: pushy earning and a voice that cuts. Cost: harsh words that hurt family, and money won and lost on impulse."},3:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','voice_income'],text:"Courage is your strong point. You push, compete and finish what you start, with your hands and your voice.",detail:"Courage is the gift. You act while others are still thinking. Gift: bravery, getting things started, and drive in how you communicate. Cost: conflict with siblings, and nervous energy that picks fights. One of the best houses for Mars."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','childhood_weight'],text:"There is heat in your home. Your roots are fought over, and peace at home takes deliberate work, not just time.",detail:"Heat in the home. Conflict is how you learned about family. Gift: strength to protect, and property through effort. Cost: arguments at the dinner table, a mother who fought, and trouble finding peace where you live."},5:{themes:['creativity','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Creative work here is competitive and risky. You make things fast, and risky bets pull at you.",detail:"Creative fire and competitive love. Gift: passionate creating, courage in romance, and drive in your children. Cost: conflict with children, a gambling instinct, and love as a contest."},6:{themes:['service','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You are built for opposition. Debts, rivals and hard work all give way to your persistence here.",detail:"You win by outlasting. Enemies become fuel. Gift: winning against opposition, strength at work, health through effort. Cost: a life that needs a fight, injuries, and conflict with staff or colleagues. One of the best houses for Mars."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','power_and_control'],text:"Partnership runs hot. The bond gives you energy, and arguing is part of how it works, not a flaw in it.",detail:"Your drive shows up inside partnership. Your reflex is to treat your partner as someone to beat in an argument. Gift: a passionate, active partner and courage in love. Cost: conflict in marriage, a partner who fights, and heat that settles around age twenty-eight into intensity you can manage."},8:{themes:['power_and_control','depth_over_breadth'],text:"Crises come suddenly and hit the body. You get through them by force, and that same force is what walks you into them.",detail:"Force aimed at hidden things. Gift: courage in a crisis, research, surgery, and drive toward the occult. Cost: a higher risk of accidents and sudden losses, fights over inheritance, and anger that goes underground. Traditionally a hard placement."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You defend your beliefs rather than hold them quietly. You argue about ideas, and you test teachers before you follow them.",detail:"You fight for what you believe. Gift: brave conviction, and a father who pushed you. Cost: crusading, clashes with teachers, and a philosophy that needs enemies."},10:{themes:['leadership','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your career is a battle. You get ahead by pushing, and the work is physical, technical or fought over.",detail:"Your ambition is public and physical. Gift: command, achievement, and a career built on drive. Cost: clashes with authority, a ruthless reputation, and a forceful father. Mars is strong here: this is the general's house."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Gains come from campaigns and from allies who fight beside you. You earn your network; you don't inherit it.",detail:"You push your networks to move. Gift: gains through effort, energetic friends, and ambitions reached. Cost: conflict in groups, competitive friends, and pushing people away by pushing too hard."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','health_discipline'],text:"Your drive runs underground: alone, abroad or at night. Energy you don't use turns on your body.",detail:"Your energy turns inward, sometimes against yourself. Gift: hidden strength, courage when alone, and drive in foreign places. Cost: self-sabotage, secret enemies, and anger with nowhere to go. Point it outward, or it becomes the enemy inside."}},Mercury:{1:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','identity_core'],text:"Your mind is your main tool: quick, talkative and youthful, and your sense of self is tied to being understood correctly.",detail:"You are your mind. Gift: quick, talkative, youthful and adaptable. Cost: nervous energy, and being seen as clever before kind."},2:{themes:['voice_income','money_perception'],text:"You make money by talking and calculating. Your family's trade was often based on words or numbers.",detail:"Words are money. Gift: earning through speaking, writing, analysis and trade. Cost: a voice that calculates, and family talks that feel like negotiations."},3:{themes:['voice_income','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Writing, messaging and short trips drive your life. Your hands and your tongue do the earning here.",detail:"The messenger at home. Gift: easy communication, writing, siblings who matter, and short trips. Cost: scattered attention and a mind that never stops. This house suits Mercury well."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your mind works at home. Study, documents and property paperwork sit at the base of your life.",detail:"You can't separate work and home. Gift: learning at home, property through brains, and a mother who taught. Cost: restlessness at home, and thinking when you should be feeling."},5:{themes:['creativity','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your intelligence flows through what you make. Teaching, analysis and clever work are your creative outlet.",detail:"Creative intelligence. Gift: thinking in stories and games, and clever children. Cost: a mind that plays instead of commits, and romance that stays in words."},6:{themes:['service','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your mind serves the daily grind. Routines, systems, debts and figuring out what's wrong are what it works on.",detail:"The analyst. Gift: solving problems, precision at work, and health through understanding your body. Cost: worry as a job, and illness driven by nerves. Mercury is strong here."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You need a partner you can talk to. Agreements, contracts and business partnerships hold the relationship up.",detail:"You partner with minds. Gift: conversation as closeness, a clever partner, and business through partnership. Cost: relationships that stay in the head, and a partner who argues."},8:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your mind goes to hidden things: research, investigation and handling other people's money.",detail:"You uncover what is hidden. Gift: research, the occult, and other people's secrets, reading what sits under what's said. Cost: a suspicious mind, and knowing things you'd rather not know. Traditionally a hard placement, but it makes investigators."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You question beliefs instead of accepting them, so you study the teaching and can end up teaching it.",detail:"The teacher's mind. Gift: understanding by explaining, philosophy, and a father who taught. Cost: intellectual arrogance, and mistaking a teaching for the truth."},10:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','mass_reach'],text:"Your career runs on words or analysis. You become known for how you explain things, not for what you own.",detail:"Your career runs on communication. Gift: a public voice, writing, trade, and analysis as a job. Cost: a reputation for cleverness over substance. Mercury is strong here."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Gains come through information and networks. Your circle is wide, and it trades in what you know.",detail:"Gains through analysis and networks. Gift: information as money, clever friends, and ambitions reached through communication. Cost: friends who are contacts, not companions."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You do your thinking in private. You research alone, abroad or for a long time before you say anything out loud.",detail:"Your mind works in private. Gift: your best thinking happens unseen, plus imagination and foreign languages. Cost: communication that hides, and thoughts that go round in circles without landing."}},Jupiter:{1:{themes:['identity_core','gifts'],text:"People see you as generous and worth listening to. Your body grows with your standing, and so does your self-belief.",detail:"A big presence. Gift: people trust you before you've earned it, and you are generous with that trust. Cost: weight, physical or moral, and an ego that grows with the body."},2:{themes:['money_perception','voice_income'],text:"Money comes easily and leaves through generosity. Your voice teaches, and your family valued knowledge over cash.",detail:"Wealth through wisdom. Gift: money comes when you teach, a generous voice, and a family that gave. Cost: spending on principle, and a mouth that lectures."},3:{themes:['voice_income','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your effort has faith behind it. Writing, teaching and siblings carry you further than pushing alone would.",detail:"The preacher's voice. Gift: courage in what you believe, siblings who guide, and words that inspire. Cost: every message wants to be a sermon."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','gifts'],text:"Home is the blessing. Property, your mother and the beliefs you inherited are the base you build everything else on.",detail:"Your home was generous, or you make it so. Gift: property, a mother who gave, and deep contentment. Cost: a home that grows past what you can manage, and comfort that stops growth."},5:{themes:['creativity','gifts'],text:"Teaching, children and creative work are your strong ground. What you make teaches people, whether you meant it to or not.",detail:"Creative luck and a gift for teaching. Gift: knowledge gathers around you, children who are blessings, and wisdom in love. Cost: giving away too much of what you make, and pride in your children."},6:{themes:['service','health_discipline'],text:"You spend your faith on service. You take on other people's debts and problems, and the work is really useful.",detail:"Growth through service. Gift: obstacles make you bigger, and enemies become teachers. Cost: the weight of work, and faith tested by daily struggle."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','gifts'],text:"Your partner is a teacher and a source of standing. The marriage carries more of your fortune than your career does.",detail:"Your partner is a teacher. Gift: marriage widens how you see the world, with a wise, generous spouse. Cost: a partner who preaches, and growth that depends on being in a pair."},8:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','letting_go'],text:"Support comes through crisis and other people's resources. Inheritance, insurance and hidden subjects are open channels.",detail:"Other people's resources flow to you. Gift: inheritance, investment, a partner's money, and occult wisdom. Cost: money that comes and goes through crisis, and faith tested by loss."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','becoming'],weight:1.5,text:"This is the house of the teacher and the law. Belief, higher study and your father set the direction of your whole life.",detail:"Jupiter's natural house. Gift: faith, teaching, good fortune, and a father who was a guru (a spiritual teacher). Cost: rigid beliefs, and a philosophy that never doubts itself."},10:{themes:['leadership','late_recognition'],text:"Your career carries moral weight. The public trusts you, and your work advises, teaches or judges instead of just producing.",detail:"Public standing through wisdom. Gift: known as the one who knows, with a career in teaching, law or advice. Cost: a reputation bigger than the substance behind it."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','money_perception'],text:"Gains are large and come through elders, teachers and wide circles. The network itself is your asset.",detail:"Gains multiply through groups. Gift: your networks are your fortune, your friends are teachers, and your ambitions are blessed. Cost: stretching too thin by being generous to many."},12:{themes:['spiritual_path','letting_go'],text:"The blessing is private. It works through retreat, foreign places and giving, and nobody keeps a public tally.",detail:"Private faith and inherited authority, working behind the scenes. Gift: mentoring, service, time alone that feeds you, and fortune from abroad. Cost: a quiet drain from giving too much to causes, people and ideas without keeping track, and mistaking withdrawal for devotion."}},Venus:{1:{themes:['identity_core','gifts'],text:"Your attractiveness is built in and you know it. Comfort and pleasant things steer your decisions more than you admit.",detail:"Charm is your first tool. Gift: beauty, grace, and doors that open. Cost: charm used instead of substance, and vanity."},2:{themes:['money_perception','voice_income'],text:"Money comes through taste, art and your voice. You spend on beauty as a normal habit, not as a treat.",detail:"Money through beauty and voice. Gift: earning by being pleasant to hear or see, and a well-off family. Cost: spending on pleasure, and a voice that flatters."},3:{themes:['voice_income','creativity'],text:"Your effort is artistic. Singing, writing and performing drive you, and siblings or neighbours are part of the loop.",detail:"Art in communication. Gift: beautiful writing, charming siblings, and pleasure in short trips. Cost: the message is beautiful before it is true."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','money_perception'],text:"Home is where the beauty goes. Property, comfort and your mother are both pleasures and costs in equal measure.",detail:"Your taste shows up at home. Gift: a beautiful house, a loving mother, and property. Cost: comfort as a cage, and home as the whole world."},5:{themes:['creativity','gifts'],text:"Love and creativity share a house, so romance, children and what you make all run on the same current.",detail:"Creative love. Gift: romance and art are the same act, and your children are beautiful. Cost: love as entertainment, and pleasure over depth."},6:{themes:['health_discipline','service'],text:"Pleasure and duty share a bed here. Relationships get tangled up with work, and your body pays for indulgence.",detail:"Love through service. Gift: you show care by fixing things, and may work in beauty or health. Cost: love that criticises, and a body that gets overindulged."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','gifts'],text:"Partnership is central, and your chart pays out through it. The risk is choosing harmony over truth when the two split.",detail:"Venus in its natural house. Gift: partnership is your natural state, with a beautiful, loving spouse. Cost: the natural blind spot, which is losing yourself in the couple."},8:{themes:['power_and_control','money_perception'],text:"Love and money are intense, hidden and life-changing. Income comes in surges, and this same house takes surges back.",detail:"Love and money are intense, hidden and life-changing. Gift: sexual depth, inheritance, and a partner's money. Cost: income in surges that reverse, and love that consumes."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','creativity'],text:"Beauty is a belief here. Art, foreign cultures and faith turn out to be the same pursuit under different names.",detail:"Beauty in belief. Gift: love from abroad, art through faith, and a generous philosophy. Cost: idealising what is far away."},10:{themes:['mass_reach','marriage_as_engine'],text:"Your career faces the public and runs on looks and style. You are known for your taste, and relationships open most doors.",detail:"Public grace. Gift: a career in beauty, art or diplomacy, and an audience that loves you. Cost: liked before respected."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','money_perception'],text:"Gains come through women, art and social circles. Your network is fun, and it is also your income.",detail:"Gains through charm. Gift: friends bring fortune, and your networks are beautiful. Cost: friendships that are deals."},12:{themes:['letting_go','isolation_risk'],text:"Pleasure is private and costly. Foreign places, hidden attachments and comfort in retreat run up the bill.",detail:"Secret love, hidden pleasure. Gift: beauty in private rooms, spiritual love, and romance abroad. Cost: a pull toward affairs, loneliness in love, and pleasure that hides."}},Saturn:{1:{themes:['identity_core','late_recognition'],text:"You were serious early, and your body carries the weight. Your sense of self builds slowly here and you doubt it often.",detail:"You were serious when young. Gift: discipline, staying power, and a life that tends to get lighter after age thirty-six. Cost: a body and self that felt old before their time."},2:{themes:['money_perception','under_producing'],text:"Money is a fear before it is a number. Savings come slowly, and your speech is careful, dry and short.",detail:"Money is slow and earned. Gift: wealth that lasts once it's built. Cost: a fear of not having enough that is built into the chart, not imagined, and a voice that holds back."},3:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','late_recognition'],text:"Your courage is made, not natural. The effort is steady, unglamorous and in the end decisive.",detail:"Courage is built, not given. Gift: communication that gets better with age, and disciplined effort. Cost: fear of speaking up, and siblings who were a burden. Saturn is good here."},4:{themes:['childhood_weight','home_foundation'],text:"Your roots often feel cold or heavy. Home is work, and your mother carried something that reached you before you could name it.",detail:"Home was heavy. Gift: you build stability because you didn't have it. Cost: a childhood that often felt cold, a mother who was all duty, and a home that feels like work."},5:{themes:['creativity','under_producing'],text:"Creating comes late and is taken seriously. Children, students and creative work tend to come later and cost more.",detail:"Creative discipline. Gift: recognition that is slow, technical and earned, and that stays. Cost: children may come late, joy is rationed, and creativity feels like homework."},6:{themes:['service','health_discipline'],text:"You outlast opposition. Debts, rivals and long-running routines are your arena, and staying power is your whole method.",detail:"You outwork obstacles. Gift: long-term health problems and long-term enemies both give way to persistence. Cost: work that never ends. Saturn is strong here."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','late_recognition'],text:"Partnership is as much duty as pleasure. The bond comes late, with someone older, or feels heavy, and it holds when lighter ones would not.",detail:"Partnership is a duty, and it lasts. Gift: commitment that survives everything. Cost: you take on the relationship and then carry it alone, and marriage tends to come late or feel heavy."},8:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','letting_go'],text:"Long endurance and hard lessons sit here. Changes are slow, and what you inherit comes with obligations attached.",detail:"Shared money and hidden matters get checked closely. Gift: traditionally a long life, and toughness through loss. Cost: borrowing gets punished, inheritance comes late, and a fear of what is hidden."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','becoming'],text:"Your faith is tested, not handed to you. Teachers let you down, and the belief that survives is the one you built yourself.",detail:"Your faith gets tested and then can't be shaken. Gift: a philosophy that survived doubt, and a teacher who arrives late. Cost: a cold father, and belief that is rigid or missing."},10:{themes:['late_recognition','leadership'],weight:1.5,text:"Your career is a long build. Recognition is slow, earned and lasting, and the early years can look a lot like failure.",detail:"Your career is your life's work, and it takes your life. Gift: real authority after forty. Cost: a demanding father, and a reputation built on hard labour. Saturn is strong here."},11:{themes:['late_recognition','mass_reach'],text:"Gains come late and through older people. Your network is small, useful and slow to form.",detail:"Gains are slow and permanent. Gift: few friends, kept for life, and ambitions reached late. Cost: loneliness in a crowd. Saturn is strong here."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','letting_go'],text:"You pay the cost out of sight, through isolation, institutions and foreign places. Your sleep is where the debt shows up.",detail:"The lesson is letting go of control over what you can't see. Gift: spiritual discipline, and time alone that makes you grow. Cost: hidden enemies, isolation, and a fear of losing what you never really held."}},Rahu:{1:{themes:['identity_core','reinvention'],text:"Your identity is a hunger. You want to be somebody, and you try on different versions of yourself until one sticks.",detail:"The hunger to become someone. Gift: an ambitious, magnetic, unusual identity. Cost: an unstable sense of self, and a body full of cravings."},2:{themes:['money_perception','voice_income'],text:"Here the hunger lands on money and speech. Income can be large and unusual, and your family's story around money is unclear.",detail:"An obsession with wealth and speech. Gift: unusual ways of earning, and money from abroad. Cost: an appetite that is never full, and speech that deceives."},3:{themes:['voice_income','mass_reach'],text:"Your ambition runs through your voice and the media. You push hard into channels other people haven't used yet.",detail:"Courage turned up until it becomes reckless. Gift: media, bold communication, and siblings abroad. Cost: taking risks just for the sake of it. Rahu (the point of hunger in the chart) does well here."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','family_conditioning'],text:"Your roots are unsettled: homes abroad, mixed backgrounds, and a mother's story that won't sit still.",detail:"You chase peace and keep moving it somewhere else. Gift: property, homes abroad, and a hunger for roots. Cost: tearing down your own foundation while looking for a truer one."},5:{themes:['creativity','mass_reach'],text:"Creating is risky and hungry. You gamble on what you make, and the size of the audience matters too much.",detail:"Creative hunger and a taste for risky bets. Gift: fame through what you make, and unusual children. Cost: gambling, and creativity that chases attention."},6:{themes:['service','health_discipline'],text:"You beat opposition in unusual ways. Debts, rivals and your body's odd complaints are the field you play on.",detail:"You feed on competition. Gift: winning against enemies, and work abroad. Cost: what it does to your body. Rahu (the point of hunger in the chart) is strong here."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','reinvention'],text:"Your partner is foreign, unusual or bigger than the life you expected, and the bond changes your standing.",detail:"The foreign partner, the unusual bond. Gift: a marriage that breaks your rules and makes you bigger. Cost: obsession with your partner, and a relationship that never settles."},8:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','power_and_control'],text:"You are drawn to what is hidden, to other people's money and to the occult. The falls are sudden, and they teach you.",detail:"An obsession with what is hidden. Gift: occult power, and sudden wealth through other people. Cost: crisis, scandal, and hunger for what can't be controlled."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','becoming'],text:"Your beliefs are unusual and put together by you. You borrow from foreign systems, and you choose your teachers instead of inheriting them.",detail:"Unusual faith. Gift: rejecting the religion you were raised in and building your own. Cost: false gurus (spiritual teachers), and a philosophy that changes with your appetite."},10:{themes:['mass_reach','reinvention'],text:"Your career is a hunger for the public eye. You rise fast in something unusual, and the standing feels borrowed until one day it doesn't.",detail:"A hunger for fame. Gift: public life is your calling. Cost: public life is your addiction, and a reputation that swells and bursts. Rahu (the point of hunger in the chart) is strong here."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','money_perception'],text:"Gains are large, come through networks and can't fully be explained. Your circle is wide, and the wanting doesn't stop at enough.",detail:"Gains through big networks. Gift: the crowd feeds you. Cost: you feed the crowd, and friends who use you. Rahu (the point of hunger in the chart) is strong here."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','letting_go'],text:"Your hunger works offstage: foreign places, hidden spending, and a mind busy at night.",detail:"Foreign places, hidden spending, and windfalls followed by collapse. Gift: a spiritual hunger, and life abroad. Cost: risky bets tend to go badly in your hands, and secret enemies."}},Ketu:{1:{themes:['identity_core','letting_go'],text:"You are half detached from your own identity. People find you hard to read because you do too.",detail:"Detached from your self-image. Gift: freedom from ego. Cost: not knowing who you are, and a body that feels borrowed."},2:{themes:['money_perception','letting_go'],text:"You don't much care about money or family talk, and there are sudden gaps. You hold what you have loosely, sometimes too loosely.",detail:"Detached from money and family. Gift: wealth comes when you stop chasing it. Cost: speech that pushes people away, and distance from family."},3:{themes:['voice_income','under_producing'],text:"Your effort comes and goes, and your voice goes quiet for stretches. What you do push at, you push at without needing an audience.",detail:"Courage without ego. Gift: acting without needing credit, and spiritual communication. Cost: distant siblings, and effort that goes unrewarded. Ketu (the point of letting go in the chart) does well here."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','childhood_weight'],text:"Your roots have a hole in them. Home, mother or country feels partly missing, and you make peace with that instead of trying to fill it.",detail:"Rootless by design. Gift: home is wherever you are. Cost: home is nowhere in particular, and a mother who was elsewhere."},5:{themes:['creativity','letting_go'],text:"You create for its own sake and drop things easily. With children or students, something is kept at a distance.",detail:"Creative and spiritual skill you seem to be born with. Gift: talent without training, and intelligence that runs on intuition. Cost: children who may come late or feel distant, and creativity that hides."},6:{themes:['service','health_discipline'],text:"You are unusually good at hard work nobody else wants. You meet illness and opposition with calm detachment, not a fight.",detail:"Enemies fade away. Gift: you handle conflict, health and mess without being swallowed by them. Cost: illness that is hard to diagnose. Ketu (the point of letting go in the chart) is strong here."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','letting_go'],text:"Your partnership feels old, as if it was already finished. You are in it but not fully arrived.",detail:"Detachment in partnership. Gift: freedom in love. Cost: you are hard to hold on to, and partners tend to be spiritual or absent."},8:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','spiritual_path'],text:"This house suits you. Depth, research, hidden things and crisis are home ground for you, and ordinary security is not.",detail:"The mystic's placement. Gift: death, the occult and big change feel familiar. Cost: sudden loss, and crises that feel like memories."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','letting_go'],text:"You inherit a belief and then drop it. Your relationship with teachers is complicated, and the faith you keep is stripped down.",detail:"You have already done the faith part. Gift: wisdom without a teacher. Cost: living without needing belief, and a father who was absent or a monk."},10:{themes:['reinvention','outside_counsel'],text:"Your career reinvents itself and goes quiet for stretches. Bad advice is the main risk here, so get good counsel.",detail:"Your career reinvents itself and goes quiet for stretches. Gift: a natural sense for what others miss, and not caring about status. Cost: breaks now and then that are not failure, but you must plan for them with money set aside."},11:{themes:['letting_go','mass_reach'],text:"Gains come and go without the usual attachment. Your network is real, and you don't lean your weight on it.",detail:"Detached from networks and gains. Gift: freedom from the crowd. Cost: the crowd is not where you belong, and gains slip away."},12:{themes:['spiritual_path','letting_go'],weight:1.5,text:"Here your chart points away from the world. Retreat, foreign places and spiritual practice are where this placement makes sense.",detail:"Liberation. Gift: the most spiritual placement in the chart. Cost: the least worldly one. Money slips away, and so does your interest in the world."}}},l={Sun:{exalted:{themes:['leadership','identity_core'],text:"Your authority is at full strength. You take charge without being asked and rarely look unsure in public. The cost is that you don't listen well when corrected.",detail:"The self at full strength: decisive, brave, allergic to waiting. You know who you are by what you start. Gift: leadership that doesn't need a committee. Cost: impatience with anyone slower, and a habit of mistaking winning for being right. You are built to lead, and life tests whether you can also follow when it matters."},debilitated:{themes:['identity_core','outside_counsel'],text:"You negotiate authority instead of assuming it. You defer, check with others, and can spend years waiting to be given what you could have taken.",detail:"The self that only sees itself in a mirror: you know who you are by how people receive you. Gift: grace, fairness, and a real sense of what other people need. Cost: authority that hesitates, decisions put off until someone else decides, and an identity that bends to keep the peace. The work is building a self that holds its shape without an audience."},own:{themes:['leadership','identity_core'],text:"You are at ease out front and the role fits you, so you rarely stop to ask whether it is the right role.",detail:"The Sun at home: warm, generous, made to be seen. You feel most alive with an audience, even a small one. Gift: a presence that lifts rooms and a loyalty that is royal. Cost: needing to be at the centre, and a pride that bruises easily. The question that follows you: is this for them, or for the applause?"}},Moon:{exalted:{themes:['emotional_pattern','home_foundation'],text:"Your mind is steady and hard to shake. That same steadiness makes you slow to notice when something has really gone wrong.",detail:"The Moon at its steadiest: you feel safe through comfort, routine, touch and things that don't change. Gift: a calm that others lean on. Cost: holding on to people, habits and grudges, because letting go feels dangerous. Your calm is real. Being inflexible is its downside."},debilitated:{themes:['emotional_pattern','depth_over_breadth'],text:"Your feelings run deep and work against themselves. Your mind holds more than it shows, and it needs a real outlet, not better management.",detail:"Your feelings run at full strength and in full privacy. You feel everything and show almost none of it. Gift: emotional depth and loyalty that survives anything. Cost: suspicion, control and holding on to a hurt for years. Here the Moon is debilitated (in its weakest sign), but that isn't weakness. It's a Moon that never learned to be casual. Feeling safe means trust, and trust costs a lot."},own:{themes:['emotional_pattern','home_foundation'],text:"Feeling is your first language, and home is your anchor. The risk is treating your mood as proof of what is actually happening.",detail:"The Moon at home: deep, protective, full of memory. You feel everything and forget nothing. Gift: the most instinctive caring of any sign. Cost: moods that come and go like the tide, and a habit of pulling back into your shell and dragging loved ones in with you. Feeling safe means family. The risk is never leaving it."}},Mars:{exalted:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','leadership'],text:"Your drive is organised. You work hard, with structure, for years, and the discipline, not the aggression, is your real talent.",detail:"Mars at its most effective: disciplined, ambitious, and patient in its aggression. Gift: achievement through steady effort, like a general rather than a soldier. Cost: ruthlessness, and a drive that never switches off."},debilitated:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your push comes and goes and often turns inward. Anger shows up late and sideways, instead of in the moment it belonged to.",detail:"Drive tangled up with feeling: you act to protect, and you can't act when you're hurt. Gift: fierce loyalty and the strength to protect. Cost: passive aggression, effort that follows your mood, and anger that turns inward. Here Mars is debilitated (in its weakest sign): a warrior whose armour is on the inside. The practice is expressing anger before it turns sour."},own:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','power_and_control'],text:"Force comes naturally and is there whenever you want it. Nothing calms it down automatically, so calming it has to be your choice.",detail:"Mars on home ground: forceful, relentless and hard to stop. Gift: willpower that outlasts everyone. Cost: a taste for revenge, control, and a power to do harm that you must choose not to use."}},Mercury:{exalted:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','under_producing'],text:"Your analysis is exact, and you can find the flaw in anything, including your own work. That is exactly what stops you from finishing and handing it over."},debilitated:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','outside_counsel'],text:"Your mind works through pictures and feelings, not step by step. Your intuition is real, and the details need a second pair of eyes.",detail:"A mind that thinks in pictures, impressions and feelings instead of lines of logic. Gift: imagination, intuition and creative language. Cost: vagueness, being talked out of what you know, and struggling to say the exact thing when it matters. Here Mercury is debilitated (in its weakest sign): a mind that doesn't work in straight lines. That's a limit in a spreadsheet and a gift in a poem."},own:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','under_producing'],text:"Your mind is a well-made tool. You learn fast and explain clearly, which makes learning an easy excuse for not finishing.",detail:"Mercury at home: quick, curious, always making connections. Gift: wit, adaptability, and the ability to explain anything to anyone. Cost: knowing a little about many things instead of a lot about one, and a mind that talks itself out of commitments."}},Jupiter:{exalted:{themes:['gifts','spiritual_path'],text:"Faith, generosity and good advice are built into you here. The risk is growing without cutting anything back.",detail:"Jupiter at its strongest: faith rooted in care, family and emotional truth. Gift: generosity, protection, and a wisdom that looks after people. Cost: giving too much to family, and growth that never leaves home."},debilitated:{themes:['spiritual_path','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You earn your beliefs the hard way and without sentiment. You trust what has been tested and quickly dismiss the rest.",detail:"Faith held back by realism: you believe in what you can build and distrust what you can't. Gift: practical, disciplined growth. Cost: pessimism where faith was needed, and holding back generosity until it's earned. Here Jupiter is debilitated (in its weakest sign): a Jupiter that learned to expect less. The practice is trusting growth."},own:{themes:['spiritual_path','gifts'],text:"Teaching and belief come naturally, and people ask you what to think. That lets your conviction run ahead of the evidence.",detail:"Jupiter on home ground: wise, hopeful and endlessly generous. Gift: faith without needing proof, and kindness without limit. Cost: naivety, preaching, and giving until nothing is left."}},Venus:{exalted:{themes:['gifts','marriage_as_engine'],text:"Love and taste are turned all the way up. You give easily, and you idealise the person in front of you.",detail:"Venus at its most open: kind, romantic and endlessly giving. Gift: unconditional love and a real sense of beauty in everything. Cost: idealising people who don't deserve it, and being used because your kindness can't say no."},debilitated:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','service'],text:"You show affection through being useful and pointing out what could be better. The feeling is real, and it shows up dressed as a correction.",detail:"Love as service: you show it by helping, improving and fixing. Gift: real, practical care and attention to what a partner actually needs. Cost: criticism where affection was wanted, and self-worth tied to being useful. Here Venus is debilitated (in its weakest sign): love that struggles to simply receive. The practice is accepting care without earning it."},own:{themes:['gifts','money_perception'],text:"Beauty, comfort and relationships are your home ground. The pull toward pleasant things is strong enough to make decisions on its own.",detail:"Venus on home ground: graceful, pleasure-loving, made for partnership. Gift: natural tact and an eye for beauty. Cost: losing yourself in a relationship, and staying in a bad one because leaving would cause conflict."}},Saturn:{exalted:{themes:['late_recognition','leadership'],text:"Your discipline is fair and it holds. You build slowly, keep your word, and people trust you to run things.",detail:"Saturn at its best: justice, balance and commitment that lasts. Gift: relationships and systems built to last, and real fairness. Cost: duty in love, and partnership that feels like a contract before it feels warm."},debilitated:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','late_recognition'],text:"Patience doesn't come naturally, and delay feels like personal failure. Meanwhile your chart asks you to keep going before any reward shows up.",detail:"Discipline at war with impulse: you want to act now and are made to wait. Gift: courage that has been tested and earned. Cost: frustration, doubting your own drive, and anger at delays. Here Saturn is debilitated (in its weakest sign): a warrior in a waiting room. The practice is learning that patience is a kind of action."},own:{themes:['late_recognition','isolation_risk'],text:"Limits are what you work with, not what stops you. The long game comes naturally, and warmth takes a separate decision.",detail:"Saturn on home ground: structure, patience and discipline. Gift: systems that serve many people, and a fairness that lasts. Cost: detachment, and a sense of duty that neglects the person next to you."}}},c={Sun:{themes:['becoming','identity_core'],text:"Your soul's work is authority and the self: what your light is for, and what it costs to make it the centre of the room.",detail:"The Sun is not just \"who you are\". It's the basic fact of being your own separate self, the will that gets you out of bed feeling your life matters. It rules authority, father figures, vitality and the ego in its healthiest form. That means not vanity, but the basic confidence that you're allowed to take up space. A strong Sun gives natural leadership and toughness. A stressed Sun can show up as an inflated need to be right. Or the opposite: a person who can't quite believe they're allowed to be seen."},Moon:{themes:['becoming','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your soul's work is feeling: what you attach to, what soothes you, and learning to steady your mind without your mother in the room.",detail:"The Moon is the fastest-moving, most changeable planet, and that's what it rules. It covers your emotional weather and your gut reactions before you've had time to think. It also covers your bond with your mother or whoever cared for you first. It isn't your personality. It's what you actually need, underneath the personality, to feel okay. A well-placed Moon gives emotional toughness and real warmth. A stressed Moon can mean moods that come without warning, or a nervous system that never fully believes it's safe."},Mars:{themes:['becoming','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your soul's work is force: what you fight for, what you burn through, and the point where courage turns into hunger.",detail:"Mars rules raw drive: courage, anger, competition, physical energy, and the will to fight for something. It's the planet that turns a wish into action. A strong Mars gives quick decisions and the stamina to push through resistance. A stressed Mars can mean a temper that moves faster than your judgement. Its quieter failure is drive that never gets let out and turns into frustration or anger at yourself."},Mercury:{themes:['becoming','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your soul's work is the mind and the word: what you say, how you trade, and the difference between clever and true.",detail:"Mercury rules how you think and how you get your thinking across to someone else: language, logic, trade, short trips, siblings. It's the planet of the mind as a tool, not as a source of wisdom (that's Jupiter's job). Mercury wants to be understood, not necessarily to be deep. A strong Mercury gives quick, clear communication and a real skill with information. A stressed Mercury can mean a mind that talks faster than it thinks, or one that gets stuck circling the same worry."},Jupiter:{themes:['becoming','spiritual_path'],text:"Your soul's work is belief and guidance: what you teach, who you follow, and the point where you stop questioning your faith.",detail:"Jupiter rules expansion of every kind: luck, growth, higher education, faith, generosity, and the search for a \"why\" behind your life. It's traditionally called the great benefic (the most helpful planet), because wherever it sits it tends to give more of what that area already has. A strong Jupiter gives real optimism, wisdom, and generosity that comes back to you. A stressed Jupiter can mean overconfidence, overpromising, or a belief system so sure of itself it stops listening. It becomes the preacher who forgot how to be a student."},Venus:{themes:['becoming','marriage_as_engine'],text:"Your soul's work is love, taste and desire: what you attach to, what you buy, and what relationships ask of you in return.",detail:"Venus rules love, beauty, pleasure and art. Less obviously, it also rules money and comfort. In the old view, what you value and what you find beautiful are the same instinct pointed two ways. It's the planet of romance and taste: what draws you in, what you find worth having. A strong Venus gives natural charm and a real ability to enjoy pleasure without guilt. A stressed Venus can mean chasing comfort instead of real connection, or undervaluing yourself in a way that shows up in both love and money."},Saturn:{themes:['becoming','late_recognition'],text:"Your soul's work is time, work and grief: carrying weight without becoming the weight, and paying what you owe.",detail:"Saturn rules structure, limits, time, and the lessons you only learn the slow way: through delay, restriction and repetition. It's traditionally feared because it holds back. But what it gives, once earned, doesn't vanish the way Jupiter's easy gifts sometimes do. A strong Saturn gives real, earned mastery and the patience to build something that lasts. A stressed Saturn can mean constant self-doubt or a fear of never being \"ready\". Relationships and work can feel like duty long before they feel like joy."}},y={Sun:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','power_and_control'],text:"Your partner comes with authority and needs the standing that goes with it. The relationship raises the question of whose name the household runs under.",detail:"The Sun is not just \"who you are\". It's the basic fact of being your own separate self, the will that gets you out of bed feeling your life matters. It rules authority, father figures, vitality and the ego in its healthiest form. That means not vanity, but the basic confidence that you're allowed to take up space. A strong Sun gives natural leadership and toughness. A stressed Sun can show up as an inflated need to be right. Or the opposite: a person who can't quite believe they're allowed to be seen."},Moon:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your partner brings care and mood. The bond feeds you, and it makes your emotional weather something you share.",detail:"The Moon is the fastest-moving, most changeable planet, and that's what it rules. It covers your emotional weather and your gut reactions before you've had time to think. It also covers your bond with your mother or whoever cared for you first. It isn't your personality. It's what you actually need, underneath the personality, to feel okay. A well-placed Moon gives emotional toughness and real warmth. A stressed Moon can mean moods that come without warning, or a nervous system that never fully believes it's safe."},Mars:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','power_and_control'],text:"Your partner is direct, energetic and happy to argue. The friction is the fuel here, and it also wears you down.",detail:"Mars rules raw drive: courage, anger, competition, physical energy, and the will to fight for something. It's the planet that turns a wish into action. A strong Mars gives quick decisions and the stamina to push through resistance. A stressed Mars can mean a temper that moves faster than your judgement. Its quieter failure is drive that never gets let out and turns into frustration or anger at yourself."},Mercury:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your partner is quick, talkative and young in manner. The relationship runs on talk, which means it needs talk to keep going.",detail:"Mercury rules how you think and how you get your thinking across to someone else: language, logic, trade, short trips, siblings. It's the planet of the mind as a tool, not as a source of wisdom (that's Jupiter's job). Mercury wants to be understood, not necessarily to be deep. A strong Mercury gives quick, clear communication and a real skill with information. A stressed Mercury can mean a mind that talks faster than it thinks, or one that gets stuck circling the same worry."},Jupiter:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','spiritual_path'],text:"Your partner acts as a teacher and a source of standing. The benefit is real, and it can quietly turn into a pecking order.",detail:"Jupiter rules expansion of every kind: luck, growth, higher education, faith, generosity, and the search for a \"why\" behind your life. It's traditionally called the great benefic (the most helpful planet), because wherever it sits it tends to give more of what that area already has. A strong Jupiter gives real optimism, wisdom, and generosity that comes back to you. A stressed Jupiter can mean overconfidence, overpromising, or a belief system so sure of itself it stops listening. It becomes the preacher who forgot how to be a student."},Venus:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','gifts'],text:"Your partner comes through beauty, comfort and pleasure. The ease is real, but ease alone doesn't hold a relationship up.",detail:"Venus rules love, beauty, pleasure and art. Less obviously, it also rules money and comfort. In the old view, what you value and what you find beautiful are the same instinct pointed two ways. It's the planet of romance and taste: what draws you in, what you find worth having. A strong Venus gives natural charm and a real ability to enjoy pleasure without guilt. A stressed Venus can mean chasing comfort instead of real connection, or undervaluing yourself in a way that shows up in both love and money."},Saturn:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','late_recognition'],text:"Your partner is older, in years or in manner, and the bond is built on duty and time. It is slow and heavy, and it holds.",detail:"Saturn rules structure, limits, time, and the lessons you only learn the slow way: through delay, restriction and repetition. It's traditionally feared because it holds back. But what it gives, once earned, doesn't vanish the way Jupiter's easy gifts sometimes do. A strong Saturn gives real, earned mastery and the patience to build something that lasts. A stressed Saturn can mean constant self-doubt or a fear of never being \"ready\". Relationships and work can feel like duty long before they feel like joy."}},f={themes:['identity_core','leadership'],weight:1.5,text:"The planet that rules your lagna (your rising sign) also rules your career. So who you are and what you do in public are one question, not two. With no line between work and self, rest is hard to justify."},p={1:{themes:['identity_core','leadership'],weight:1.5,text:"Your first house is the strongest in your chart by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). You carry the chart yourself, so anything you build starts with your own standing, not with a partner or a plan.",detail:"This is the house of your body walking into a room before you say a word. It covers how you come across, how you handle anything new, and your physical vitality. Whatever sits here colours your whole personality, the way a tinted window colours everything you see through it. This house answers: what's the first impression, and what's it like to simply be you, day to day?"},2:{themes:['money_perception','voice_income'],weight:1.5,text:"Your second house is the strongest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Money, voice and what you hold are where your support sits, and building up savings comes easier to you than performing.",detail:"This is what you own, what you're worth and, less obviously, how you speak. In the old systems, the mouth and voice belong here next to money. Both are things you put out into the world that have value. Words and wealth are treated as cousins. This house answers: what do you have, what do you value, and what does your voice carry?"},3:{themes:['voice_income','drive_vs_resistance'],weight:1.5,text:"Your third house is the strongest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Effort, your hands and your voice are backed, so your chart pays for doing, not for thinking it over.",detail:"This is the house of the short trip, not the long journey: siblings, neighbours, the daily commute, the emails you send before lunch. Less obviously, it's also the house of courage: the nerve it takes to speak up, try the thing, and act before you feel fully ready. This house answers: what does bravery look like for you day to day? And how do you get your ideas out of your head and into the world?"},4:{themes:['home_foundation','gifts'],weight:1.5,text:"Your fourth house is the strongest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Your roots are the asset: home, land and inner ground. Work built from there holds.",detail:"This is the deepest house in the chart, the foundation everything else is built on. It's your actual home, but also your mother (or the parent who cared for you) and your family line. It's the private inner floor you stand on when nobody's watching. In some traditions it's also read as the end of things, the place you return to in the end. This house answers: what does \"safe\" mean to you, and what were you standing on before you understood anything else?"},5:{themes:['creativity','gifts'],weight:1.5,text:"Your fifth house is the strongest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). What you make and what you teach is the supported channel, so creative work is not a side project in your chart.",detail:"This is the house of what you make because you want to, not because you have to. It covers art, romance in its playful early stage, and games. It also covers children (real ones, or the things you create and raise) and joy for its own sake. It's also the house of intelligence and risky bets: the mind at play, gambling included. This house answers: what do you make when nobody's grading it, and where does your joy really live?"},6:{themes:['service','drive_vs_resistance'],weight:1.5,text:"Your sixth house is the strongest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). You have unusual backing in conflict, debt and daily grind, so the hard road really is the easier one for you.",detail:"This is the house of the daily grind: your job, looking after your body, and the obstacles and small enemies of ordinary life. It isn't the glamorous career (that's the 10th). It's the unglamorous doing: the routine, the discipline of showing up. This house answers: how do you handle a problem that won't go away on its own? And what does your body need from you that you keep putting off?"},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','gifts'],weight:1.5,text:"Your seventh house is the strongest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Partnership carries your chart, and going it alone throws away the support you actually have.",detail:"This is the house of the other person: marriage, business partners and open enemies. In the old systems, anyone you face one to one lives here, whether you love them or fight them. It's the mirror house: what you find here often shows what you can't yet see in yourself. This house answers: who do you become around one other person, and what kind of partner do you actually attract?"},8:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','power_and_control'],weight:1.5,text:"Your eighth house is the strongest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Depth, other people's money and crisis are where your backing is, so hidden work pays better than surface work.",detail:"This is the most misunderstood house in the chart. It isn't simply \"death\". It's anything that changes you by taking something away first. That includes shared money (inheritance, debt, a partner's income) and sex as merging rather than performing. It also covers the occult, surgery and grief. It's the house of what you can't control alone and have to go through, not around. This house answers: what breaks you open, and what do you inherit, literally or emotionally, from the people you're bound to?"},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','becoming'],weight:1.5,text:"Your ninth house is the strongest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Belief, teachers and work far from home are supported, and your life runs better with a clear set of beliefs behind it.",detail:"This is the house of the beliefs you build your life around: religion, philosophy, higher education and long-distance travel. It also holds the teachers who shaped how you see the world. It's the house of the \"why\", the worldview that makes everything else make sense. This house answers: what do you actually believe, who taught you to believe it, and what are you here to pass on?"},10:{themes:['leadership','mass_reach'],weight:1.5,text:"Your tenth house is the strongest in your chart by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Public work is where your support is, and it should lead.",detail:"This is the house of what the world sees you do: your career and your reputation. In the old systems it is also your father, or the parent who stood for authority and achievement. It's the most visible house in the chart, the one strangers can guess from your public life alone. This house answers: what does the world pay you for, and what will people say you did with your life?"},11:{themes:['mass_reach','money_perception'],weight:1.5,text:"Your eleventh house is the strongest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Gains come through networks and groups, so your circle is infrastructure, not just a social life.",detail:"This is the house of the group: friends, communities and networks. It covers the gains that come not from your own effort but from being connected to people. Think of the introduction, the lucky break, the crowd. This house answers: who stands beside you, and what do you receive simply by belonging?"},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','spiritual_path'],weight:1.5,text:"Your twelfth house is the strongest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Retreat, foreign places and unseen work are where your support sits, which is an unusual place to find it.",detail:"This is the last house, and it rules endings: solitude, hidden things, what you lose and what you give away. In its spiritual reading it also rules liberation itself, when the ego finally stops needing anything. It's also read as foreign places and institutions (hospitals, retreats, places you go to be alone). This house answers: what are you meant to let go of, and what happens when you're finally, completely alone with yourself?"}},w={1:{themes:['identity_core','drive_vs_resistance'],weight:1.5,text:"Your first house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Your sense of self gets the least backing, so you have to build it on purpose. Leading from the front costs you more than it should.",detail:"This is the house of your body walking into a room before you say a word. It covers how you come across, how you handle anything new, and your physical vitality. Whatever sits here colours your whole personality, the way a tinted window colours everything you see through it. This house answers: what's the first impression, and what's it like to simply be you, day to day?"},2:{themes:['money_perception','under_producing'],weight:1.5,text:"Your second house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Building up savings is not your supported route, so income does better when it keeps flowing than when you hold on to it.",detail:"This is what you own, what you're worth and, less obviously, how you speak. In the old systems, the mouth and voice belong here next to money. Both are things you put out into the world that have value. Words and wealth are treated as cousins. This house answers: what do you have, what do you value, and what does your voice carry?"},3:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','under_producing'],weight:1.5,text:"Your third house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Raw effort gives back less than it should, so leverage and other people's help matter more than pushing harder.",detail:"This is the house of the short trip, not the long journey: siblings, neighbours, the daily commute, the emails you send before lunch. Less obviously, it's also the house of courage: the nerve it takes to speak up, try the thing, and act before you feel fully ready. This house answers: what does bravery look like for you day to day? And how do you get your ideas out of your head and into the world?"},4:{themes:['home_foundation','childhood_weight'],weight:1.5,text:"Your fourth house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Your roots give the least back, so home and inner ground need upkeep instead of being something you can draw on.",detail:"This is the deepest house in the chart, the foundation everything else is built on. It's your actual home, but also your mother (or the parent who cared for you) and your family line. It's the private inner floor you stand on when nobody's watching. In some traditions it's also read as the end of things, the place you return to in the end. This house answers: what does \"safe\" mean to you, and what were you standing on before you understood anything else?"},5:{themes:['creativity','under_producing'],weight:1.5,text:"Your fifth house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Creative work and risky bets get the least support, so build through craft and repetition, not one big swing.",detail:"This is the house of what you make because you want to, not because you have to. It covers art, romance in its playful early stage, and games. It also covers children (real ones, or the things you create and raise) and joy for its own sake. It's also the house of intelligence and risky bets: the mind at play, gambling included. This house answers: what do you make when nobody's grading it, and where does your joy really live?"},6:{themes:['health_discipline','service'],weight:1.5,text:"Your sixth house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Open conflict and grinding routine cost you more than they cost other people, so skip the fights you don't need to have.",detail:"This is the house of the daily grind: your job, looking after your body, and the obstacles and small enemies of ordinary life. It isn't the glamorous career (that's the 10th). It's the unglamorous doing: the routine, the discipline of showing up. This house answers: how do you handle a problem that won't go away on its own? And what does your body need from you that you keep putting off?"},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','outside_counsel'],weight:1.5,text:"Your seventh house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Partnership gets the least support, so write agreements down instead of assuming them.",detail:"This is the house of the other person: marriage, business partners and open enemies. In the old systems, anyone you face one to one lives here, whether you love them or fight them. It's the mirror house: what you find here often shows what you can't yet see in yourself. This house answers: who do you become around one other person, and what kind of partner do you actually attract?"},8:{themes:['power_and_control','money_perception'],weight:1.5,text:"Your eighth house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Shared money and sudden change are thin ground, so keep debt small and your savings boring.",detail:"This is the most misunderstood house in the chart. It isn't simply \"death\". It's anything that changes you by taking something away first. That includes shared money (inheritance, debt, a partner's income) and sex as merging rather than performing. It also covers the occult, surgery and grief. It's the house of what you can't control alone and have to go through, not around. This house answers: what breaks you open, and what do you inherit, literally or emotionally, from the people you're bound to?"},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','outside_counsel'],weight:1.5,text:"Your ninth house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Inherited beliefs and assigned teachers give the least back, so the faith that works is the one you put together yourself.",detail:"This is the house of the beliefs you build your life around: religion, philosophy, higher education and long-distance travel. It also holds the teachers who shaped how you see the world. It's the house of the \"why\", the worldview that makes everything else make sense. This house answers: what do you actually believe, who taught you to believe it, and what are you here to pass on?"},10:{themes:['late_recognition','under_producing'],weight:1.5,text:"Your tenth house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Public standing gets the least support, so recognition comes through the work itself, not through your title.",detail:"This is the house of what the world sees you do: your career and your reputation. In the old systems it is also your father, or the parent who stood for authority and achievement. It's the most visible house in the chart, the one strangers can guess from your public life alone. This house answers: what does the world pay you for, and what will people say you did with your life?"},11:{themes:['mass_reach','money_perception'],weight:1.5,text:"Your eleventh house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Gains through networks are thin, so build your income on direct work, not on your circle.",detail:"This is the house of the group: friends, communities and networks. It covers the gains that come not from your own effort but from being connected to people. Think of the introduction, the lucky break, the crowd. This house answers: who stands beside you, and what do you receive simply by belonging?"},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','letting_go'],weight:1.5,text:"Your twelfth house is the weakest by Ashtakavarga (a system that scores how much support each part of the chart has). Retreat and hidden spending drain you instead of restoring you, so ration your time alone and watch what goes out.",detail:"This is the last house, and it rules endings: solitude, hidden things, what you lose and what you give away. In its spiritual reading it also rules liberation itself, when the ego finally stops needing anything. It's also read as foreign places and institutions (hospitals, retreats, places you go to be alone). This house answers: what are you meant to let go of, and what happens when you're finally, completely alone with yourself?"}},b={themes:['drive_vs_resistance','under_producing'],weight:1.5,text:"One of your planets sits in a sign where it has almost no support. It still works, but uphill, and its results come later and smaller than the rest of your chart suggests."},v={Ketu:{themes:['timing_now','letting_go'],text:"You are in a Ketu dasha (a planetary period that runs for years). Things thin out, attachments loosen and work that was central goes quiet. That suits research, practice and finishing, not launching.",detail:"Ketu (the south lunar node) is the shadow point opposite Rahu, and it stands for detachment. It points to skill you seem to have been born with rather than earned this time. It also brings a real lack of interest in the rewards that skill could bring. Wherever Ketu sits, there's often real talent paired with not caring about being recognised for it. That can look like calm freedom from wanting, or like a career that never quite takes off, depending on how aware you are of it."},Venus:{themes:['timing_now','marriage_as_engine'],text:"You are in a Venus dasha (a planetary period that runs for years). Relationships, money, art and comfort are switched on, and the pull toward pleasant things is strong enough to make decisions for you.",detail:"Venus rules love, beauty, pleasure and art. Less obviously, it also rules money and comfort. In the old view, what you value and what you find beautiful are the same instinct pointed two ways. It's the planet of romance and taste: what draws you in, what you find worth having. A strong Venus gives natural charm and a real ability to enjoy pleasure without guilt. A stressed Venus can mean chasing comfort instead of real connection, or undervaluing yourself in a way that shows up in both love and money."},Sun:{themes:['timing_now','leadership'],text:"You are in a Sun dasha (a planetary period that runs for years). Authority, being seen and matters around your father are active, and because this period is short, it rewards deciding over thinking it over.",detail:"The Sun is not just \"who you are\". It's the basic fact of being your own separate self, the will that gets you out of bed feeling your life matters. It rules authority, father figures, vitality and the ego in its healthiest form. That means not vanity, but the basic confidence that you're allowed to take up space. A strong Sun gives natural leadership and toughness. A stressed Sun can show up as an inflated need to be right. Or the opposite: a person who can't quite believe they're allowed to be seen."},Moon:{themes:['timing_now','home_foundation'],text:"You are in a Moon dasha (a planetary period that runs for years). Mood, home, your mother and the public are active, and what you build now is built on feeling as much as on plans.",detail:"The Moon is the fastest-moving, most changeable planet, and that's what it rules. It covers your emotional weather and your gut reactions before you've had time to think. It also covers your bond with your mother or whoever cared for you first. It isn't your personality. It's what you actually need, underneath the personality, to feel okay. A well-placed Moon gives emotional toughness and real warmth. A stressed Moon can mean moods that come without warning, or a nervous system that never fully believes it's safe."},Mars:{themes:['timing_now','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You are in a Mars dasha (a planetary period that runs for years). The push is on, conflict sits closer to the surface and your body takes more wear, so aim your force at one target, not several.",detail:"Mars rules raw drive: courage, anger, competition, physical energy, and the will to fight for something. It's the planet that turns a wish into action. A strong Mars gives quick decisions and the stamina to push through resistance. A stressed Mars can mean a temper that moves faster than your judgement. Its quieter failure is drive that never gets let out and turns into frustration or anger at yourself."},Rahu:{themes:['timing_now','reinvention'],text:"You are in a Rahu dasha (a planetary period that runs for years). Hunger, foreign places and unusual routes are open, and things can move faster than your judgement of them.",detail:"Rahu (the north lunar node) is not a physical planet. It's a calculated point, a shadow. In the old systems it stands for obsessive desire: a turned-up hunger for whatever it touches, often outside your comfort zone. It has no rules of its own, which is exactly what makes it restless. It wants what it doesn't understand yet. Wherever Rahu sits, expect an oversized appetite. You tend to chase that thing past the point of contentment before learning what the chase was there to teach."},Jupiter:{themes:['timing_now','spiritual_path'],text:"You are in a Jupiter dasha (a planetary period that runs for years). Teaching, belief, advice and growth are switched on, and the risk is taking on more than you can finish.",detail:"Jupiter rules expansion of every kind: luck, growth, higher education, faith, generosity, and the search for a \"why\" behind your life. It's traditionally called the great benefic (the most helpful planet), because wherever it sits it tends to give more of what that area already has. A strong Jupiter gives real optimism, wisdom, and generosity that comes back to you. A stressed Jupiter can mean overconfidence, overpromising, or a belief system so sure of itself it stops listening. It becomes the preacher who forgot how to be a student."},Saturn:{themes:['timing_now','late_recognition'],text:"You are in a Saturn dasha (a planetary period that runs for years). The work is slow, structural and unglamorous, and what you build now is what lasts. Nothing about it is quick.",detail:"Saturn rules structure, limits, time, and the lessons you only learn the slow way: through delay, restriction and repetition. It's traditionally feared because it holds back. But what it gives, once earned, doesn't vanish the way Jupiter's easy gifts sometimes do. A strong Saturn gives real, earned mastery and the patience to build something that lasts. A stressed Saturn can mean constant self-doubt or a fear of never being \"ready\". Relationships and work can feel like duty long before they feel like joy."},Mercury:{themes:['timing_now','voice_income'],text:"You are in a Mercury dasha (a planetary period that runs for years). Talking, writing, trade and negotiation are active, and the returns come from what you say and how often you say it.",detail:"Mercury rules how you think and how you get your thinking across to someone else: language, logic, trade, short trips, siblings. It's the planet of the mind as a tool, not as a source of wisdom (that's Jupiter's job). Mercury wants to be understood, not necessarily to be deep. A strong Mercury gives quick, clear communication and a real skill with information. A stressed Mercury can mean a mind that talks faster than it thinks, or one that gets stuck circling the same worry."}},k={Janma:{verdict:'mixed',guide:'don\'t start anything new about yourself today; keep running what is already running'},Sampat:{verdict:'push',guide:'ask for the money: today backs gains and getting things'},Vipat:{verdict:'hold',guide:'put off the risky move; today costs more than it gives back'},Kshema:{verdict:'push',guide:'lock things in: secure, sign and steady what you already have'},Pratyak:{verdict:'hold',guide:'expect friction and don\'t force it; move the confrontation to another day'},Sadhaka:{verdict:'push',guide:'do the hard thing on your list: today is made for finishing'},Vadha:{verdict:'hold',guide:'avoid the big decision and the long trip; keep the day small'},Mitra:{verdict:'push',guide:'call the person who can help; today is good for alliances'},'Ati-Mitra':{verdict:'push',guide:'push the important one: this is the strongest day of the cycle'}},_=[{term:'lagna',definition:"The sign that was rising over the eastern horizon at the moment you were born, also called the rising sign or ascendant. It changes about every two hours, which is why your birth time matters so much. It sets where all twelve houses (areas of life) start. It describes the shape of your life and how other people read you before you've said anything."},{term:'nakshatra',definition:"One of twenty-seven lunar mansions (star groups the Moon passes through). The sky is split by where the Moon sits on each of the twenty-seven nights it takes to go around. Each one covers thirteen degrees and twenty minutes of sky and has its own image, ruling planet and character. Indian astrology reads the Moon's nakshatra as the texture of your mind, and the rising nakshatra as the texture of your body and manner."},{term:'whole-sign house',definition:"The oldest way of splitting a chart into twelve areas of life. The whole rising sign becomes the first house, the next sign the second, and so on, with no messy edges. So a planet is simply in the house of the sign it's in. Each house covers one area: the first is the self, the fourth is home, the seventh is partnership, the tenth is public work."},{term:'Ashtakavarga',definition:"A scoring system that turns a chart into numbers. For each planet, the planets and the rising sign each either support or don't support each of the twelve signs. The supports are then added up. The result shows which parts of a chart have backing and which run on thin support. That's why it's used to say where effort pays off and where it doesn't."},{term:'bindu',definition:"A single point of support in the Ashtakavarga count (the system that scores support in a chart). One planet gives one bindu to a sign when it supports that sign. More bindus in a sign means a planet there has more behind it. Almost none means the planet works, but uphill, and its results come later and smaller."},{term:'Sarvashtakavarga',definition:"The total Ashtakavarga score (the system that scores support in a chart). All seven planets' bindus (support points) are added up for each sign, giving twelve totals. The highest total marks the area of life with the most support, and the lowest marks the area with the least. It's the quickest way to see where a chart is strong and where it isn't."},{term:'Atmakaraka',definition:"The planet at the highest degree in the chart, whatever sign or house it's in. It's treated as the soul planet: the marker of what your life is working on from start to finish. Its nature (authority, feeling, force, mind, belief, desire or time) names the debt your soul is settling."},{term:'Darakaraka',definition:"The planet at the lowest degree in the chart, read as the signature of your partner and of what marriage brings. It describes the character of the relationship rather than a specific person. It's read together with the seventh house (the house of partnership), not instead of it."},{term:'dasha',definition:"A period of life ruled by one planet. Indian astrology splits a life into a fixed order of these periods, worked out from where the Moon was at your birth. So the same chart gives different results at different times, depending on which planet is in charge right now. It's the timing part of the system."},{term:'mahadasha',definition:"The main period in the dasha sequence (the order of planetary periods), lasting six to twenty years depending on the planet. The planet ruling it sets the general theme of that stretch of life. It shows what's switched on, what gets built, and what tends to get neglected."},{term:'antardasha',definition:"The sub-period inside a mahadasha (a main planetary period). Each main period is split again among all nine planets in the same order, giving a second, shorter layer of timing. It explains why one long period isn't the same all the way through, and why a hard decade still has stretches that move."},{term:'tara bala',definition:"A daily reading made by counting from the lunar mansion (the Moon's star group) at your birth to the one the Moon is in today. The count lands on one of nine positions, each with a traditional verdict, some good and some not. It's used as a simple push-or-hold signal for the day, not a forecast."},{term:'Rahu',definition:"The north lunar node. It isn't a body but the point where the Moon's path crosses the Sun's path heading north, where eclipses happen. It's read as hunger and turning things up: where your chart's appetite points, the foreign and the unusual. It also rules things that grow faster than the judgement guiding them."},{term:'Ketu',definition:"The south lunar node, the point opposite Rahu. It's read as taking away rather than wanting: detachment, what you're already done with, and areas where you're skilled but not interested. It's linked with research, practice and solitude, and with results that come without the usual satisfaction."},{term:'dignity',definition:"How comfortable a planet is in the sign it's in. A planet in a sign it owns works on home ground. An exalted one works at full stretch. A debilitated one works against the grain. Dignity doesn't mean good or bad. It shows how easily that planet gets its work done, and at what cost."},{term:'exaltation',definition:"The sign where a planet is thought to work at its fullest, traditionally with one exact degree of peak strength. It makes that planet's qualities obvious and mostly unchecked. That's a strength in what it produces and a weakness in what it fails to hold back."},{term:'debilitation',definition:"The sign opposite a planet's exaltation (its strongest sign), where it works against its own grain. Its work still gets done, but indirectly, later, or in a form the planet wouldn't have chosen. It describes difficulty and a different way of working, not a verdict on your life."},...t.GLOSSARY_EXTRA]},825,[826]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"NAKSHATRA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"GANA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"GRAHA_THEMES",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"BHAVA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DIGNITY_STATE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return h}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DIGNITY_NOTE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"COMBUST_NOTE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return u}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"VARGOTTAMA_NOTE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return c}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DASHA_NOTE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return y}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DASHA_LORD_ROLE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return p}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"YOGA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return f}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"YOGA_ABSENT",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return b}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SADE_SATI",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return w}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DIVISIONAL",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return v}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"BAV_NOTE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return k}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"GLOSSARY_EXTRA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return M}});const t={Ashwini:{deity:'the Ashwini Kumaras, divine healers',symbol:'a horse\'s head',gana:'Deva',quality:'quick starts, healing and speed'},Bharani:{deity:'Yama, lord of restraint and endings',symbol:'the womb',gana:'Manushya',quality:'carrying a heavy load, restraint, endings and beginnings'},Krittika:{deity:'Agni, the fire god',symbol:'a razor or flame',gana:'Rakshasa',quality:'cutting, purifying and sharp judgment'},Rohini:{deity:'Brahma, the creator',symbol:'a chariot or ox cart',gana:'Manushya',quality:'growth, beauty and fertile ground'},Mrigashira:{deity:'Soma, the Moon god',symbol:'a deer\'s head',gana:'Deva',quality:'searching, curiosity and restless looking'},Ardra:{deity:'Rudra, the storm god',symbol:'a teardrop',gana:'Manushya',quality:'storms, upheaval and sharp feeling that clears the air'},Punarvasu:{deity:'Aditi, mother of the gods',symbol:'a quiver of arrows',gana:'Deva',quality:'return, renewal and starting again'},Pushya:{deity:'Brihaspati, teacher of the gods',symbol:'a cow\'s udder or lotus',gana:'Deva',quality:'nourishing, steady support and care'},Ashlesha:{deity:'the Nagas, serpent beings',symbol:'a coiled serpent',gana:'Rakshasa',quality:'coiling, hypnotic insight and holding on'},Magha:{deity:'the Pitris, the ancestors',symbol:'a royal throne',gana:'Rakshasa',quality:'lineage, status and authority'},'Purva Phalguni':{deity:'Bhaga, god of shared fortune',symbol:'the front legs of a bed',gana:'Manushya',quality:'rest, pleasure and creative play'},'Uttara Phalguni':{deity:'Aryaman, god of agreements',symbol:'the back legs of a bed',gana:'Manushya',quality:'agreements, support and steady friendship'},Hasta:{deity:'Savitar, the Sun in its giving form',symbol:'a hand',gana:'Deva',quality:'skilled hands, craft and getting things done'},Chitra:{deity:'Tvashtar, the divine craftsman',symbol:'a bright jewel',gana:'Rakshasa',quality:'design, brilliance and making something striking'},Swati:{deity:'Vayu, the wind',symbol:'a young shoot swaying in the wind',gana:'Deva',quality:'independence, flexibility and moving with the wind'},Vishakha:{deity:'Indra and Agni together',symbol:'a triumphal arch',gana:'Rakshasa',quality:'single-minded goals and a fixed target'},Anuradha:{deity:'Mitra, god of friendship',symbol:'a lotus',gana:'Deva',quality:'devotion, friendship and working in a group'},Jyeshtha:{deity:'Indra, king of the gods',symbol:'a circular amulet',gana:'Rakshasa',quality:'seniority, protection and carrying authority'},Mula:{deity:'Nirriti, goddess of dissolution',symbol:'a bunch of tied roots',gana:'Rakshasa',quality:'roots, digging to the base and tearing out what is false'},'Purva Ashadha':{deity:'Apas, the waters',symbol:'a fan or elephant tusk',gana:'Manushya',quality:'invincibility, persuasion and early victory'},'Uttara Ashadha':{deity:'the Vishvadevas, the universal gods',symbol:'an elephant tusk',gana:'Manushya',quality:'lasting victory, principle and steady effort'},Shravana:{deity:'Vishnu, the preserver',symbol:'an ear or three footprints',gana:'Deva',quality:'listening, learning and connecting'},Dhanishta:{deity:'the eight Vasus',symbol:'a drum',gana:'Rakshasa',quality:'rhythm, wealth and drive'},Shatabhisha:{deity:'Varuna, lord of the cosmic waters',symbol:'an empty circle',gana:'Rakshasa',quality:'a hundred healers, secrecy and solitary research'},'Purva Bhadrapada':{deity:'Aja Ekapada, the one-footed goat',symbol:'the front of a funeral cot',gana:'Manushya',quality:'burning intensity, transformation and strong ideals'},'Uttara Bhadrapada':{deity:'Ahir Budhnya, the serpent of the deep',symbol:'the back of a funeral cot',gana:'Manushya',quality:'depth, restraint and calm strength'},Revati:{deity:'Pushan, guardian of travellers',symbol:'a fish or drum',gana:'Deva',quality:'safe passage, guidance and care at the end of a road'}},n={Deva:'Deva ("divine") nakshatras are read as gentle and easy-going.',Manushya:'Manushya ("human") nakshatras are read as worldly and mixed, with feeling and appetite in balance.',Rakshasa:'Rakshasa ("fierce") nakshatras are read as intense, forceful and hard to pin down. This describes temperament, not morality.'},s={Sun:'self, father, authority and health',Moon:'mind, mother and mood',Mars:'energy, courage, conflict and property',Mercury:'speech, intellect and trade',Jupiter:'wisdom, teachers, children and growth',Venus:'love, comfort, art and the spouse',Saturn:'work, duty, delay and endurance',Rahu:'hunger, ambition, foreign things and obsession',Ketu:'detachment, old skill, loss and a spiritual pull'},o=[{topics:'self, body and character',kind:'corner and trine'},{topics:'wealth, speech and family',kind:'neutral'},{topics:'courage, effort and siblings',kind:'growth house'},{topics:'home, mother and peace of mind',kind:'corner'},{topics:'children, intelligence and past merit',kind:'trine'},{topics:'enemies, debts, illness and service',kind:'hard house'},{topics:'spouse, partners and business',kind:'corner'},{topics:'sudden change, hidden things and endurance',kind:'hard house'},{topics:'luck, father, teachers and purpose',kind:'trine'},{topics:'career, status and action',kind:'corner'},{topics:'gains, income and friends',kind:'growth house'},{topics:'losses, expenses, foreign lands and release',kind:'hard house'}],h={exalted:'is exalted. It is at its strongest and most comfortable, and delivers its themes with ease and sometimes with excess.',moolatrikona:'is in its moolatrikona zone, the home base of the planet. Its strength is close to that of its own sign.',own:'is in its own sign. It is steady, at ease and acts in its own way.',friend:'is in a friend\'s sign. It is supported and does its work without much friction.',neutral:'is in a neutral sign. It is neither helped nor hindered by the sign.',enemy:'is in an enemy\'s sign. It works against the grain and needs more effort to deliver.',debilitated:'is debilitated. It is at its weakest, and its themes come out awkward or underpowered. Cancellation rules (neecha bhanga) can reverse this.'},l='Friend and enemy here use the permanent friendships from Parashara. Some astrologers also adjust for temporary friendship by house position, which this app does not.',u='A planet very close to the Sun is called combust, and classical texts read its themes as burnt or hidden. The orbs used: Moon 12, Mars 17, Mercury 14 (12 if retrograde), Jupiter 11, Venus 10 (8 if retrograde), Saturn 15 degrees. Sources differ on the exact numbers.',c='A planet in the same sign in the birth chart and in the navamsa is called vargottama. It is read as strengthened, because both layers say the same thing.',y='The mahadasha (main period) sets the subject of the years. The antardasha (sub-period) shows which part of that subject is active. The pratyantardasha (the layer below) lasts weeks to months and tunes the detail. Years here are 365.25 days; some astrologers use 360-day years, which shifts dates by a few months over a lifetime.',p={Ketu:'Ketu periods are read as a time of letting go and of turning inward.',Venus:'Venus periods are read as a time of relationships, comfort, money and art.',Sun:'Sun periods are read as a time of authority, visibility and the question of who you are.',Moon:'Moon periods are read as a time of mood, home, family and public feeling.',Mars:'Mars periods are read as a time of effort, conflict, property and decisive action.',Rahu:'Rahu periods are read as a time of hunger, ambition and unusual routes.',Jupiter:'Jupiter periods are read as a time of learning, growth, teachers and children.',Saturn:'Saturn periods are read as a time of work, duty, delay and slow structure.',Mercury:'Mercury periods are read as a time of study, trade, writing and many small moves.'},f={gajakesari:{name:'Gajakesari yoga',rule:'Jupiter in the 1st, 4th, 7th or 10th sign from the Moon.',meaning:'Traditionally linked with a good name, learning and support from other people. It reads stronger when Jupiter and the Moon are both well placed.',note:'Some texts do not count Jupiter in the same sign as the Moon.'},budhaditya:{name:'Budha-Aditya yoga',rule:'Sun and Mercury in the same sign.',meaning:'A sharp mind and clear speech are the classic reading.',note:'Mercury never strays far from the Sun, so this is very common. It counts for more when Mercury is not combust and both sit in good signs.'},chandraMangala:{name:'Chandra-Mangala yoga',rule:'Moon and Mars in the same sign.',meaning:'Feeling and drive are fused. Classically tied to earning power and enterprise, and also to a short temper and mood swings.'},ruchaka:{name:'Ruchaka yoga (Mahapurusha)',rule:'Mars in its own or exalted sign, in a corner house (1st, 4th, 7th, 10th) from the lagna.',meaning:'Courage, command and physical energy are the classic reading.'},bhadra:{name:'Bhadra yoga (Mahapurusha)',rule:'Mercury in its own or exalted sign, in a corner house from the lagna.',meaning:'A sharp intellect, skill in speech and trade are the classic reading.'},hamsa:{name:'Hamsa yoga (Mahapurusha)',rule:'Jupiter in its own or exalted sign, in a corner house from the lagna.',meaning:'Wisdom, ethics and standing as a teacher or guide are the classic reading.'},malavya:{name:'Malavya yoga (Mahapurusha)',rule:'Venus in its own or exalted sign, in a corner house from the lagna.',meaning:'Comfort, charm and artistic taste are the classic reading.'},shasha:{name:'Shasha yoga (Mahapurusha)',rule:'Saturn in its own or exalted sign, in a corner house from the lagna.',meaning:'Discipline, authority over large systems and endurance are the classic reading.'},raja:{name:'Raja yoga',rule:'A lord of a corner house (or the lagna) joined to a lord of a trine (5th or 9th), in the same sign or swapping signs.',meaning:'A classic marker of rank and effectiveness in the areas those houses cover.',note:'How much it delivers depends on where the planets sit and how strong they are. The 6th, 8th and 12th houses weaken it.'},dharmaKarmadhipati:{name:'Dharma-Karmadhipati yoga',rule:'The lords of the 9th (purpose) and 10th (career) joined in the same sign or swapping signs, or one planet ruling both.',meaning:'Purpose and career pull in the same direction, so work tends to feel like a calling.',note:'It is read as weaker if the joined planets sit in the 6th, 8th or 12th house.'},yogakaraka:{name:'Yogakaraka',rule:'One planet ruling both a corner house and a trine for your lagna.',meaning:'This is read as the most useful planet in the chart, and its periods are where the chart is traditionally said to pay off, if the planet is well placed.'},dhana:{name:'Dhana yoga',rule:'Lords of two wealth houses (1st, 2nd, 5th, 9th, 11th) joined, with one of them ruling the 2nd or 11th.',meaning:'It links the houses of income and assets. Classically it is about making and keeping money.',note:'Strength and timing depend on the planets involved and their periods.'},harsha:{name:'Harsha yoga (Viparita Raja)',rule:'The lord of the 6th house sitting in the 6th, 8th or 12th.',meaning:'A hard house whose lord sits in another hard house. Read as gain that comes out of difficulty: opponents, debts and illness lose force.'},sarala:{name:'Sarala yoga (Viparita Raja)',rule:'The lord of the 8th house sitting in the 6th, 8th or 12th.',meaning:'A hard house whose lord sits in another hard house. Read as endurance and recovery after upheaval.'},vimala:{name:'Vimala yoga (Viparita Raja)',rule:'The lord of the 12th house sitting in the 6th, 8th or 12th.',meaning:'A hard house whose lord sits in another hard house. Read as thrift, independence and losses that do not stick.'},neechaBhanga:{name:'Neecha Bhanga (cancelled debilitation)',rule:'A debilitated planet whose sign lord, or the lord of its exaltation sign, stands in a corner house from the lagna or the Moon.',meaning:'The planet starts weak and works its way up. The classic reading is a rise after a struggle.',note:'Texts list several cancellation rules. The app checks this one.'},kemadruma:{name:'Kemadruma yoga',rule:'No planet (apart from the Sun and the nodes) in the Moon\'s sign or in the signs before and after it.',meaning:'Classically read as emotional isolation and a feeling of having to manage alone.',note:'It is cancelled by planets in a corner house from the Moon, or the Moon in a corner house from the lagna. Many modern astrologers treat it lightly.'},sunapha:{name:'Sunapha yoga',rule:'A planet (not the Sun or the nodes) in the sign after the Moon.',meaning:'Classically read as self-made resources and a mind that works things out for itself.'},anapha:{name:'Anapha yoga',rule:'A planet (not the Sun or the nodes) in the sign before the Moon.',meaning:'Classically read as ease, good health and a pleasant presence.'},duradhara:{name:'Duradhara yoga',rule:'Planets (not the Sun or the nodes) in the signs on both sides of the Moon.',meaning:'The Moon is supported from both sides, which classically reads as comfort and generosity.'},guruChandala:{name:'Guru-Chandala yoga',rule:'Jupiter and Rahu in the same sign.',meaning:'Teaching and tradition meet the outsider. It is read as unconventional beliefs, or as being pulled between rules and appetite.',note:'This is a later tradition, not from the earliest texts, and astrologers differ on how negatively to read it.'},kalaSarpa:{name:'Kala Sarpa pattern',rule:'All seven classical planets on one side of the Rahu and Ketu axis.',meaning:'Life is read as running through one narrow channel, with strong ups and downs around the themes of the nodes.',note:'Many astrologers do not use this at all, and those who do disagree about the exact rule.'},parivartana:{name:'Parivartana yoga (sign exchange)',rule:'Two planets sitting in each other\'s signs.',meaning:'The two planets and the houses they rule are tied together, each acting in the other\'s territory. Read as a strong link between those areas of life.'}},b='The app tests Gajakesari, Budha-Aditya, Chandra-Mangala, the five Mahapurusha yogas, Raja, Dharma-Karmadhipati, Yogakaraka, Dhana, Viparita Raja, Neecha Bhanga, Kemadruma, Sunapha, Anapha, Duradhara, Guru-Chandala, Kala Sarpa and sign exchange. Hundreds of other yogas exist in the texts; these are the ones with a clear rule that can be checked.',w={what:'Sade Sati is the seven and a half years when Saturn passes through the sign before your Moon sign, your Moon sign, and the sign after it. It is read as a long stretch of testing, slow work and cutting back. How hard it is depends on Saturn\'s condition in your chart, and astrologers argue about how heavy it really is.',rising:'Rising phase: Saturn is in the sign before your Moon sign. In the usual telling, pressure first shows up in spending, sleep, distance and things you have been avoiding.',peak:'Peak phase: Saturn is over your Moon sign. In the usual telling, the weight lands on mood, health and how you see yourself. This is the heaviest phase.',setting:'Setting phase: Saturn is in the sign after your Moon sign. In the usual telling, pressure moves to family, money and speech while you rebuild.',none:'Saturn is not in the sign before, on, or after your Moon sign, so you are not in Sade Sati.',dhaiya:'Dhaiya (small Saturn periods) is when Saturn is in the 4th or 8th sign from your Moon, about two and a half years each. The 4th is linked to pressure at home and peace of mind, the 8th to hidden stress and sudden change. Traditions differ on how much weight to give it.'},v={navamsa:'The navamsa (D9) splits each sign into nine parts of 3 degrees 20 minutes. It is read as the inner strength of each planet and the nature of marriage and purpose. A planet strong in both the birth chart and the navamsa is read as reliable.',dashamsa:'The dashamsa (D10) splits each sign into ten parts of 3 degrees. It is read as career and public action. The ten parts of an odd sign count from that sign; the ten parts of an even sign count from its 9th sign.',note:'There are sixteen standard divisional charts in the texts. The app computes the navamsa and dashamsa, which are the two most used.'},k='Each planet scores 0 to 8 bindus in each sign, and 4 is the average. As a common rule of thumb, 5 or more is strong, 3 or fewer is weak. In the combined table (Sarvashtakavarga) a sign with 28 or more is read as strong, since the average is about 28.',M=[{term:'pada',definition:'One quarter of a nakshatra, 3 degrees 20 minutes wide. Each pada falls in exactly one navamsa sign, so the pada refines the reading of the star group.'},{term:'gana',definition:'The temperament group of a nakshatra: Deva (gentle), Manushya (worldly) or Rakshasa (intense). It describes style, not goodness.'},{term:'moolatrikona',definition:'The part of a sign where a planet is read as strongest after its exaltation. It sits between exalted and own sign in strength.'},{term:'combust',definition:'A planet too close to the Sun to be seen. Classical texts read its themes as burnt, hidden or overshadowed by the Sun\'s themes.'},{term:'vargottama',definition:'A planet in the same sign in the birth chart and the navamsa chart. It is read as strengthened.'},{term:'navamsa',definition:'The ninth-part divisional chart (D9). It is read as the inner strength of the planets and the nature of marriage.'},{term:'dashamsa',definition:'The tenth-part divisional chart (D10). It is read as career and public action.'},{term:'pratyantardasha',definition:'The third layer of the Vimshottari periods, inside the sub-period. It lasts weeks to months.'},{term:'Vimshottari',definition:'The main Jyotish timing system. It splits 120 years among nine planets in a fixed order, starting from the planet that rules your Moon\'s nakshatra.'},{term:'yoga',definition:'A named combination of planets in the chart that the texts read for a specific result, such as Gajakesari or Raja yoga. The rule is checkable; how strongly it shows depends on the rest of the chart.'},{term:'kendra',definition:'A corner house: the 1st, 4th, 7th or 10th. Planets here are strong and visible.'},{term:'trikona',definition:'A trine house: the 1st, 5th or 9th. They are the houses of merit, purpose and luck.'},{term:'dusthana',definition:'A hard house: the 6th, 8th or 12th. They cover difficulty, loss and release, and they weaken a planet that sits there.'},{term:'yogakaraka',definition:'A planet that rules both a corner house and a trine for your lagna. It is read as the most helpful planet in your chart.'},{term:'Sade Sati',definition:'The seven and a half years when Saturn passes over the sign before your Moon sign, your Moon sign and the sign after it. A long period of testing and slow work.'},{term:'bhava',definition:'A house. Jyotish counts houses by whole signs from the lagna, so each house is exactly one sign.'}]},826,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"SUN_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MOON_SIGN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"RISING",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLANET_IN_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return h}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ASPECT",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return u}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PATTERN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ELEMENT_LACK",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return y}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ELEMENT_HEAVY",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return c}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MANIFEST",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return p}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CHART_RULER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return f}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_HOUSE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return w}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"RETURN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return b}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"GLOSSARY",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return v}});var t=r(d[0]);const o={Aries:{themes:['identity_core','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You feel most like yourself when something is starting, and least like yourself when it needs keeping up. The cost is a trail of things you began and nobody finished.",detail:"This is the self at full strength: decisive, brave, and unable to stand waiting. You know who you are by what you start. Gift: you can lead without needing a committee. Cost: you get impatient with anyone slower, and you can mistake winning for being right. You are built to lead, and life tends to test whether you can also follow when it matters."},Taurus:{themes:['identity_core','money_perception'],text:"You are built to hold your ground, and that is both your talent and your trap. You keep defending what once felt comfortable long after it stopped feeling that way.",detail:"You build your sense of self on things that last: your body, the land, the things you can touch and keep. People know you by how reliable you are. Gift: a steadiness people lean on without you asking them to. Cost: pride in never changing, which can turn into refusing to grow. Your strength is physical. Neglect your body and your whole self dims."},Gemini:{themes:['identity_core','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You are more than one person, and every version of you is real. Depth tends to come late, because knowing a little about a lot pays off sooner.",detail:"Your self is made of curiosity. You feel most alive when you are learning, talking, or linking two ideas nobody thought to link. Gift: you adapt fast, and your wit opens doors. Cost: you change to match the room, so people ask which version is the real one. You are allowed to be several things. The work is knowing which one is talking."},Cancer:{themes:['identity_core','home_foundation'],text:"You get your bearings from where you belong, so the state of your home limits everything else. From the inside, being needed and being used can feel the same.",detail:"Your sense of self is rooted in belonging: to a family, a place, a circle you protect. You know who you are by who you care for. Gift: real emotional strength. People feel safe under your roof. Cost: you guard the nest so hard you never leave it, and you take every slight personally because everything feels personal. Your strength is care. Your risk is smothering."},Leo:{themes:['identity_core','creativity'],text:"You are made to be seen doing the thing, not to do it quietly. So recognition is something you need to function, not vanity, and anyone can use it to steer you.",detail:"The Sun is at home here (Leo is its own sign): warm, generous, made to be seen. You feel most alive with an audience, even a small one. Gift: you lift a room, and your loyalty is royal in the best sense. Cost: you need to be at the centre, and your pride bruises easily. The question that follows you: is this for them, or for the applause?"},Virgo:{themes:['identity_core','service','under_producing'],text:"You are built around fixing things, which makes you useful and hard to please. The standard that makes the work better is the same one that slows it down.",detail:"You prove yourself by being useful and getting it right. You feel most real when you are good at something. Gift: skill, sharp judgement, and a work ethic that gets things done. Cost: you never quite believe you are enough, because there is always one more thing to fix. You can also turn that eye on others when they did not ask. Your worth is not your output. That sentence can take years to believe."},Libra:{themes:['identity_core','marriage_as_engine'],text:"You find yourself through other people, so your judgement is sharp in company and blurry alone. Fairness is what you value. Indecision is the price.",detail:"You see yourself best in a mirror: you know who you are by how people receive you. Gift: grace, fairness, and a real sense of what other people need. Cost: you hesitate to take charge, you put off decisions until someone else makes them, and you bend yourself to keep the peace. The work is building a self that keeps its shape without an audience."},Scorpio:{themes:['identity_core','power_and_control','depth_over_breadth'],text:"You run at one intensity, and there is no lower setting. When you commit, you commit fully, which is why pulling away is your only brake.",detail:"Your identity is forged in the deep end: intensity, privacy, and a refusal to be casual about anything. Gift: courage in a crisis, and total loyalty once you give it. Cost: using control in place of trust, and testing people to see if they will stay. You tend to be remade more than once in life. Each time, you need less of the armour."},Sagittarius:{themes:['identity_core','freedom_vs_structure','spiritual_path'],text:"You face outward, toward the bigger picture, and detail feels like a cage until you see it is the work. Your optimism is a method, not just a mood.",detail:"Your self is built on a view of the world. You feel most alive when you believe in something and can say why. Gift: optimism that spreads, and a moral compass you actually follow. Cost: preaching to people who came for company, and leaving before the boring middle is done. Your identity is the search. Make sure you sometimes arrive."},Capricorn:{themes:['identity_core','late_recognition'],text:"You are built to carry things a long way: slow, steady, and unimpressed by early wins. The risk is treating every year as a down payment on a life you keep putting off.",detail:"Your identity is earned, never given. You define yourself by what you have built and how long it lasted. Gift: authority that comes late and holds. Cost: measuring your worth by what you achieve, and being unable to rest because rest feels like falling behind. You are old when young. The reward is being young when old, if you let it come."},Aquarius:{themes:['identity_core','isolation_risk','mass_reach'],text:"You stand a little outside the group you belong to. That is how you see it clearly, and why you never quite feel you belong. Distance is your tool and your isolation.",detail:"You belong to the group and stand apart from it at the same time. You feel most alive when you add to something bigger than one life. Gift: original thinking, and a real fairness that does not play favourites. Cost: emotional distance. You can care about humanity and struggle with the person in front of you. Your identity is an idea. Remember it lives in a body."},Pisces:{themes:['identity_core','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your edges are soft: you soak up the room, then wonder which part of the mood was yours. That openness is a gift when you aim it and a drain when you do not.",detail:"Your sense of self is porous. You know who you are by what you absorb and what you melt into. Gift: compassion and imagination with no bottom. Cost: a self so open it loses its shape, and escape as your first answer to pain. The work is setting boundaries that let you feel without drowning."}},n={Aries:{themes:['emotional_pattern','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your feelings come fast, burn out fast, and leave you confused that anyone is still arguing. You calm down by moving, not by talking.",detail:"Your feelings arrive fast, hot, and honest. You react before you decide to. Gift: emotional courage. You say the thing. Cost: a temper that leaves before the apology arrives, and a need to feel safe by acting rather than by being held. For you, feeling safe means moving."},Taurus:{themes:['emotional_pattern','home_foundation'],text:"You calm yourself through your body: food, weight, familiar rooms, the same way home. Comfort really does steady you, and it is also where you hide.",detail:"This is the Moon at its steadiest. You feel safe through comfort, routine, touch, and things that do not change. Gift: emotional toughness that others borrow. Cost: holding on to people, habits, and grudges, because letting go feels like danger. Your calm is real. Your stubbornness is its shadow."},Gemini:{themes:['emotional_pattern','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You deal with feelings by naming them, which is why you can describe a mood you have not had yet. Talking helps, until it becomes a way of not feeling.",detail:"You process feelings by talking about them. You need to name a mood to know you are having it. Gift: you put feelings into words well, and your lightness helps others breathe. Cost: thinking a feeling instead of feeling it, and getting restless when things go quiet. For you, feeling safe means conversation."},Cancer:{themes:['emotional_pattern','family_conditioning'],text:"You remember feelings in detail, for a long time. That memory makes you loyal, and it brings old hurts back to life whenever the same tone of voice returns.",detail:"The Moon is at home here (Cancer is its own sign): deep, protective, full of memory. You feel everything and forget nothing. Gift: the most natural nurturing of any sign. Cost: moods that come and go like the tide, and a habit of retreating into your shell and pulling loved ones in with you. Family is where you feel safe. The risk is never leaving it."},Leo:{themes:['emotional_pattern','creativity'],text:"You need your feelings witnessed to believe they happened, so being overlooked feels like being erased. Your warmth is generous, and it is also a request.",detail:"Your feelings need to be seen to feel real. You are warm and generous, and quietly hurt when nobody notices. Gift: emotional generosity and loyalty. Cost: needing appreciation the way others need air, and a pride that hides hurt until it bursts out. For you, feeling safe means being valued out loud."},Virgo:{themes:['emotional_pattern','service'],text:"You handle a feeling by fixing something, usually something small and nearby. Worry is not a flaw in you. It is your first rough reaction to caring.",detail:"Your feelings get sorted, analysed, and quietly managed. You feel safe when things are in order. Gift: practical care. You show love by fixing things. Cost: worry as your default, and criticising yourself and others when the order slips. Being useful makes you feel safe. The trap is never feeling useful enough."},Libra:{themes:['emotional_pattern','marriage_as_engine'],text:"You steady yourself by keeping the room calm, so your own feelings get read last. Peace you buy by staying quiet is a loan, and it charges interest.",detail:"Your feelings tune in to the other person. You feel what the room feels first. Gift: tact and real emotional fairness. Cost: not knowing your own mood until someone else leaves, and swallowing anger to keep the peace. For you, feeling safe means harmony. The cost is the harmony you fake."},Scorpio:{themes:['emotional_pattern','power_and_control'],text:"You feel things privately and under pressure, and you test people before you show them anything. You give trust slowly and take it back all at once.",detail:"Your feelings run at full intensity and full privacy. You feel everything and show almost none of it. Gift: emotional depth and a loyalty that survives anything. Cost: suspicion, control, and holding on to a hurt for years. Tradition calls Scorpio the Moon's fall (its hardest sign). That does not make you weak. It is a Moon that never learned to be casual. Trust is what makes you feel safe, and trust is expensive."},Sagittarius:{themes:['emotional_pattern','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"Your feelings need somewhere to go: a plan, a trip, a bigger picture. Stepping back really helps you, and it is also how you outrun the smaller, closer thing.",detail:"Your feelings need room. You feel safe when you know you can leave. Gift: emotional optimism and faith that things work out. Cost: restlessness dressed up as freedom, and a habit of philosophising about a feeling instead of sitting with it. The open road is where you feel safe. The risk is never unpacking."},Capricorn:{themes:['emotional_pattern','childhood_weight'],text:"You manage feelings by taking responsibility for them, often before checking whose they were. Your composure is real and costly, and you pay for it privately later.",detail:"You hold your feelings to a standard. You feel safe when you have earned it. Gift: emotional discipline, and a steadiness under pressure that others rely on. Cost: a nervous system that never feels finished, and trouble accepting care because you have not earned it. Being capable makes you feel safe. Let someone hold you anyway."},Aquarius:{themes:['emotional_pattern','isolation_risk'],text:"You step back from your own feelings and study them like weather on a map. Understanding a feeling is not the same as having it.",detail:"You watch your feelings from a little distance. You feel safe when you understand what you feel. Gift: emotional clear-headedness and real care for the group. Cost: a distance that comes across as coldness, and surprise when your own emotions finally arrive. Perspective makes you feel safe. The risk is watching your own life from outside it."},Pisces:{themes:['emotional_pattern','family_conditioning'],text:"You take on a room's mood without noticing, then treat it as your own. Time alone is not a luxury for you. It is how you find out what you actually feel.",detail:"Your feelings have no walls: yours, theirs, and the room's all arrive at once. Gift: compassion and intuition that can feel almost psychic. Cost: soaking up other people's pain and calling it yours, and escaping into fantasy when real life is too loud. Pulling back is what makes you feel safe. The work is pulling back and then coming back."}},s={Aries:{themes:['identity_core','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You arrive before anyone introduces you: direct, quick, a little impatient. People see you as ready, so they hand you the start of things and rarely the cleanup.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Aries rising, you meet it head on. Mars rules your chart, so you move first and think on the way. People read you as brave, direct and ready, often before you feel it. Your gift is a fast, honest start that gets things moving. Your cost is that you can seem pushy or impatient, and people hand you the fights along with the starts. Slow your first reaction by one breath."},Taurus:{themes:['identity_core','money_perception'],text:"You come across as unhurried and solid, and people slow down around you. That same steadiness gets mistaken for agreement long after you have stopped agreeing.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Taurus rising, you meet it calmly. Venus rules your chart, so comfort, taste and a steady pace shape your first impression. People read you as grounded and safe to be around. Your gift is presence: rooms settle when you arrive. Your cost is that you can be slow to shift, and your quiet can be read as yes when you mean no. Say the no out loud."},Gemini:{themes:['identity_core','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You come across as quick, up to date, and easy to talk to, and that gets you in almost anywhere. It also gets you underestimated on anything that needs staying power.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Gemini rising, you meet it with questions. Mercury rules your chart, so talk, ideas and quick movement come first. People read you as bright, young and easy to talk to. Your gift is that you can walk into almost any room and connect. Your cost is that people may not take you seriously on long work, and you can scatter yourself. Pick one thing and let people see you finish it."},Cancer:{themes:['identity_core','home_foundation'],text:"You come across as warm and careful, so people bring you their situation early. The shell is real: what they see is your manner, not where you actually stand.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Cancer rising, you meet it carefully. The Moon rules your chart, so your mood and your sense of safety shape your first impression. People read you as kind and caring, sometimes guarded. Your gift is that people feel looked after around you. Your cost is that your shell goes up fast when you feel exposed, and your moods show on your face. Let the people who have earned it past the shell."},Leo:{themes:['identity_core','leadership'],text:"You take up space whether you mean to or not, so blending in is not an option for you. The room decides you are confident and then holds you to it.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Leo rising, you meet it warmly and visibly. The Sun rules your chart, so being seen is part of how you work. People read you as confident, warm and a natural lead. Your gift is that you lift the room and people follow your lead. Your cost is that you can take a lack of attention personally, and pride makes backing down hard. Let the work earn the applause."},Virgo:{themes:['identity_core','service'],text:"You come across as capable and a little reserved, which invites work rather than closeness. People bring you the problem before they bring you themselves.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Virgo rising, you meet it by noticing. Mercury rules your chart, so you scan, sort and spot what needs fixing. People read you as capable, neat and a little reserved. Your gift is that people trust you with details and with problems. Your cost is that you can come across as critical, and you are usually hardest on yourself. Say what is working before what is wrong."},Libra:{themes:['identity_core','marriage_as_engine'],text:"You meet the world by adjusting to it, and you do it so smoothly it reads as charm. The cost is a long wait before anyone learns what you actually think.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Libra rising, you meet it gracefully. Venus rules your chart, so manners, looks and fairness shape your first impression. People read you as pleasant, balanced and easy to like. Your gift is that you put people at ease and bring sides together. Your cost is that you can agree to keep the peace and decide too late. Choose, then stay kind about it."},Scorpio:{themes:['identity_core','power_and_control'],text:"You give little away, so people fill the silence with their own theory about you. Privacy is your strategy. Being misread is the bill.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Scorpio rising, you meet it watchfully. Mars and Pluto rule your chart, so you read people before you let them read you. People see you as intense, private and hard to fool. Your gift is depth: people tell you things they tell no one else. Your cost is that you can seem cold or suspicious at first, and you test people before you trust them. Show one card early."},Sagittarius:{themes:['identity_core','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"You arrive open and unguarded, which opens doors, and sometimes windows you meant to keep shut. Frankness looks like freedom until it looks like carelessness.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Sagittarius rising, you meet it openly. Jupiter rules your chart, so optimism, humour and a wide view shape your first impression. People read you as friendly, honest and up for anything. Your gift is that you bring hope and a bigger picture into the room. Your cost is that you can be blunt, restless and quick to promise. Promise less, then deliver it."},Capricorn:{themes:['identity_core','late_recognition'],text:"You come across as older, contained, and safe to put in charge, even at ages when you were neither. Responsibility finds you early and does not check whether you asked for it.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Capricorn rising, you meet it seriously. Saturn rules your chart, so duty, patience and a long view shape your first impression. People read you as mature, reliable and in control, often older than your years. Your gift is that people trust you with responsibility early. Your cost is that you can seem cold or hard to reach, and you carry more than you show. Let people see the effort, not just the result."},Aquarius:{themes:['identity_core','isolation_risk'],text:"People see you as an outsider even in rooms that like you. That gives you freedom and costs you belonging. People ask your advice but do not quite include you.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Aquarius rising, you meet it on your own terms. Saturn and Uranus rule your chart, so ideas and independence come first. People read you as friendly but a little apart, and hard to predict. Your gift is a fresh view and fairness to everyone. Your cost is that you can hold people at arm's length and argue for the sake of it. Let one person close enough to know you."},Pisces:{themes:['identity_core','emotional_pattern'],text:"You come across as soft and hard to pin down, so people project the version of you they prefer. Being agreeable at the door is not the same as agreeing.",detail:"Your rising sign (the sign on the horizon when you were born) is how you meet the world. With Pisces rising, you meet it softly. Jupiter and Neptune rule your chart, so feeling and imagination shape your first impression. People read you as gentle, dreamy and easy to open up to. Your gift is that people feel understood around you. Your cost is that you soak up other people's moods and can be hard to pin down. Protect your edges before a crowded day."}},h={Sun:{1:{themes:['identity_core'],text:"Your identity is the project itself. You are visible by default, and blending in is not an option for you.",detail:"People see you before you speak. Your identity and your body are bound together: your vitality is high and your presence is hard to miss. You are the first thing people notice about your own life. Gift: natural authority and a body that bounces back. Cost: an ego that fills every room, and taking everything personally because everything is about you. Fathers and authority figures shaped how you present yourself."},2:{themes:['money_perception','identity_core'],text:"Your self-worth and your net worth get filed together, so a thin month feels like a verdict on you.",detail:"Your identity is built on what you own and how you speak. Self-worth and net worth run from the same account. Gift: a voice people listen to and a real ability to earn. Cost: money problems that feel like identity crises, and pride in possessions that can crowd out people. Your family's wealth, or the lack of it, shaped your early sense of self."},3:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','voice_income'],text:"You come into focus by saying things. Writing, talking, and everyday exchange are where you really live.",detail:"You find your identity through expression and effort. You become yourself by speaking, writing, and trying. Gift: courage, communication, and siblings or peers who matter. Cost: a restless identity, always moving, unsure who you are when you stop. Your father may have been there more in words than in person."},4:{themes:['home_foundation'],text:"Your centre of gravity is private and at home, so the work only holds up while your home base does.",detail:"Your identity is rooted in home and where you come from. The Sun (which stands for the father) sits in the house of the mother, so home was where you learned who you are. Gift: deep foundations and a sense of self that does not need a public. Cost: a life lived at home, and authority figures who ruled the private space. You are most yourself where you were raised."},5:{themes:['creativity','identity_core'],text:"People know you through what you make, so years without output feel to you like years without a self.",detail:"Your identity comes through creating. What you make carries your name. Gift: creative authority, intelligence, and joy in being seen for your work. Cost: treating children, real or creative, as extensions of your ego, and pride in the product. Romance and play are where you feel most alive."},6:{themes:['service','health_discipline'],text:"You earn your place by being useful. That builds a solid position, and it quietly trains you to earn your place every day.",detail:"You find your identity through struggle. You know who you are by what you overcome. Gift: strength against enemies, skill at work, and health through effort. Cost: a self that needs conflict to feel real, and a father who may have been demanding or absent. You are strongest when you have an opponent."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine'],text:"You come into focus opposite someone. Partnership is not decoration here. It is the mirror your identity runs on.",detail:"You find yourself through another person, in partnership. Gift: a partner with authority, and a self that feels complete in a relationship. Cost: losing your own light to your partner's, or choosing partners who compete for the centre. For you, marriage is a question about identity."},8:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','power_and_control'],text:"You are shaped by what breaks and gets rebuilt, so a crisis works as a method for you rather than an interruption.",detail:"Your identity is forged in crisis. You have fallen apart and been rebuilt more than once. Gift: courage when things change, and a self that survives what would break others. Cost: a father who may have felt distant or out of reach, and an ego tested by things you cannot control. Hidden matters like inheritance, secrets, and the occult shape who you become."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','becoming'],text:"You are built around a belief you can pass on, and life keeps giving you chances to teach it.",detail:"Your identity comes through belief. You pass on a view of the world rather than a product. Gift: authority as a teacher, faith, and a father who was a guide. Cost: the preacher's shadow. You can sound like you are lecturing, and mistake your view for the truth. The warning for a Sun in the 9th house (the house of belief and teaching) is simple. You are given the pulpit, and your tone decides whether people stay."},10:{themes:['late_recognition','leadership'],text:"Your identity and your public role are the same thing, so your career is a question of who you are, not just what you earn.",detail:"Your identity is your career. The world sees you do the thing, and the thing is who you are. Gift: public authority, achievement, and a father who showed you ambition. Cost: a life lived for reputation, and an identity that falls apart when the career does. Most traditions call this the strongest house for the Sun."},11:{themes:['mass_reach'],text:"You take shape inside a group, so your network is not just support for the work. It is where the work lands.",detail:"Your identity comes through the group. People know you by who you are connected to, and you gain through networks. Gift: influence, friends in high places, and income through community. Cost: a self defined by who you know, and a father who felt like one voice among many. Your ambitions are large and shared."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','letting_go'],text:"You are most yourself when nobody is watching, so being visible really tires you out rather than just being inconvenient.",detail:"Your identity works behind the scenes. Recognition comes late, from far away, or not at all, and you learn to exist without it. Gift: spiritual authority, service, and a strength that does not need witnesses. Cost: a father who may have felt absent or far away, and an ego that dissolves before it is built. Time alone is where you find yourself."}},Moon:{1:{themes:['emotional_pattern','identity_core'],text:"Your mood is public. What you feel shows on you before you have decided whether to share it.",detail:"Your feelings are on your face. You cannot hide a mood and should stop trying. Gift: emotional presence. People feel you right away, and the public tends to warm to you. Cost: moods that run your body, and a self that changes like the tide. Your mother shaped your identity directly."},2:{themes:['money_perception','emotional_pattern'],text:"You feel security in your body and in your bank balance, so money trouble lands as an emotional event.",detail:"For you, feeling safe and having money are the same thing. Your bank balance calms or upsets your nervous system. Gift: a caring voice, and money through care or the public. Cost: spending to feel safe, and family money used as emotional currency. Your mother is in your voice."},3:{themes:['emotional_pattern','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You settle by talking it through. A feeling you have not said out loud stays unfinished until you say it.",detail:"Your feelings need to move, through speech, writing, travel, and effort. Gift: emotional courage and a mind that makes ten ideas at once. Cost: restlessness, boredom with routine, and a nervous system that runs hot. When the Moon rules a wealth house (a house linked to money), money comes through communication."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','family_conditioning'],text:"Home is what steadies you. What the house is doing is what you are doing, whether or not you admit it.",detail:"The Moon is at home here. Feeling safe is your foundation, and home is what keeps you steady. Without it, nothing works. Gift: deep contentment when settled, and a mother who was there. Cost: never leaving, and moods that live in the walls. This is the Moon's natural place."},5:{themes:['creativity','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your feelings need an outlet that makes something. Without one, they turn into drama for its own sake.",detail:"You feel through creating and loving. Gift: emotional creativity, warmth with children, and romance that feels like home. Cost: moods tied to being appreciated for what you make, and emotional risks in love and in gambling or speculation."},6:{themes:['health_discipline','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your mood and your body keep the same books, so stress shows up as a physical symptom before it shows up as a thought.",detail:"Your feelings run through your work and your body. Stress hits you physically first. Gift: emotional toughness under pressure and real care about serving others. Cost: anxiety as your baseline, health that mirrors your mood, and a habit of caring for others while neglecting yourself."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','emotional_pattern'],text:"You take your emotional temperature from whoever you are closest to, so choosing a partner is a big structural decision.",detail:"You need a partner to feel complete, and that need is the thing to watch. Gift: emotional openness in relationships and a caring partner. Cost: your moods follow your partner's moods, and your feelings are on public display. The public tends to warm to you. Marriage steadies you."},8:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','emotional_pattern'],text:"You feel deeply and in private, and what you have not said sits in your body, building up interest.",detail:"Your emotional intensity is hard for others to match. You process things in the deep end. Gift: psychological depth, intuition, and resilience in a crisis. Cost: emotional ups and downs, a mother whose life may have held upheaval, and feelings that surface as obsession. Traditionally this is a hard placement, and it produces depth."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','emotional_pattern'],text:"You need a bigger picture to feel steady, so belief is upkeep for you, not a luxury.",detail:"You feel your faith rather than think it. Meaning feeds you emotionally. Gift: devotion, optimism, and a mother who was a teacher. Cost: moods tied to belief, and a wandering heart looking for a philosophy to belong to. Foreign places feel like home."},10:{themes:['late_recognition','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your inner state is on public display, so a private year shows up in your work and everyone reads it.",detail:"The public sees your feelings. You are known for how you care. Gift: popularity, a career in caring or public-facing work, and a mother who showed you ambition. Cost: emotional exposure, and moods that swing with your reputation."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','emotional_pattern'],text:"You need a group to feel real, and the wrong group can meet that need well enough to keep you too long.",detail:"Friends are family, and the group is home. Gift: emotional belonging, gains through community, and a wide circle of care. Cost: moods that depend on being included, and a mother who was more a friend than a parent."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your feelings run underground and surface late, which is why time alone is something you need, not a sign of trouble.",detail:"Your inner life is vast and private. Gift: imagination, compassion, and recovery through time alone. Cost: isolation that drowns you instead of restoring you, a mother who may have felt absent or distant, and emotions that hide even from you. Know the difference between solitude and hiding."}},Mercury:{1:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','identity_core'],text:"You think out loud and in public, so people take your first draft as your final position.",detail:"You are your mind. Gift: quick, verbal, youthful, and adaptable. Cost: nervous energy, and being seen as clever before kind."},2:{themes:['money_perception','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You think about value: what a thing is worth, what you are worth, and where the two stopped matching.",detail:"Words are money. Gift: earning through speaking, writing, analysis, and trade. Cost: a voice that calculates, and family talks that feel like negotiations."},3:{themes:['mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your mind is your main tool here, quick and hungry, and it picks breadth over depth unless you make it choose.",detail:"Mercury, the messenger, is at home here. Gift: easy communication, writing, siblings who matter, and short trips. Cost: scattered attention and a mind that never stops. This is Mercury's own house."},4:{themes:['family_conditioning','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your thinking carries the accent of the home you grew up in, including the arguments that never got finished there.",detail:"Your mind and your home cannot be pulled apart. Gift: learning at home, property through brains, and a mother who taught. Cost: restlessness at home, and thinking where you should feel."},5:{themes:['creativity','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You think best while making something, so an idea you never build never gets properly tested.",detail:"This is creative intelligence. Gift: thinking in stories and games, and children who are clever. Cost: a mind that plays instead of committing, and romance that stays in words."},6:{themes:['service','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your attention goes to detail and fixing mistakes. That is very useful at work and harmful when you aim it at yourself.",detail:"You are the analyst. Gift: solving problems, precision at work, and health through understanding. Cost: worry as a job, and nerves that show up in your health. Mercury is strong here."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You think by talking to one person. That works well, and it makes the choice of that person matter a lot.",detail:"You partner with minds. Gift: conversation as closeness, a clever partner, and business through partnership. Cost: relationships that stay in the head, and a partner who argues."},8:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your mind goes after what is hidden and does not stop when the answer gets uncomfortable.",detail:"You uncover what is hidden. Gift: research, the occult, and other people's secrets. You read beneath what is said. Cost: a suspicious mind, and knowing things you would rather not know. Traditionally a hard placement, and it produces investigators."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You think in systems and big frameworks. The risk is a beautiful theory that never had to survive a fact.",detail:"You have a teacher's mind. Gift: understanding by explaining, philosophy, and a father who taught. Cost: intellectual arrogance, and mistaking doctrine for truth."},10:{themes:['late_recognition','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your thinking is your public product, so the record of what you said is the career itself.",detail:"Your career runs on communication. Gift: a public voice, and a profession in writing, trade, or analysis. Cost: a reputation for cleverness over substance. Mercury is strong here."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You think inside a network, and the ideas that stick with you are usually ones the group had already agreed on.",detail:"You gain through analysis and networks. Gift: information as currency, clever friends, and goals reached through communication. Cost: friends who are contacts, not companions."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You think best when nobody is watching, and the thought that matters tends to arrive before you have the words for it.",detail:"Your mind works in private. Gift: your best thinking happens alone, plus imagination and foreign languages. Cost: communication that hides, and thoughts that circle without landing."}},Venus:{1:{themes:['identity_core','gifts'],text:"People see you as pleasant before anything else. That opens doors and delays being taken seriously.",detail:"Charm is your first tool. Gift: beauty, grace, and doors that open. Cost: charm used in place of substance, and vanity."},2:{themes:['money_perception'],text:"You have a working sense of what things are worth, and the same instinct quietly spends on comfort.",detail:"Money comes through beauty and your voice. Gift: earning by being pleasant to hear or see, and a family with money. Cost: spending on pleasure, and a voice that flatters."},3:{themes:['voice_income','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Charm runs through what you say, so persuading comes easier than being accurate, and you have to choose which one you are doing.",detail:"Your communication is an art. Gift: beautiful writing, charming siblings, and pleasure in short trips. Cost: making the message beautiful before making it true."},4:{themes:['home_foundation'],text:"You need your home to be pleasant in order to function. That is a real need, and an expensive one.",detail:"Your sense of beauty lands in the home. Gift: a beautiful house, a loving mother, and property. Cost: comfort as a cage, and home as the whole world."},5:{themes:['creativity','gifts'],text:"You are built to make attractive things, and the pleasure of making is often as much the payment as money is.",detail:"This is creative love. Gift: romance and art are the same act for you, and children who are beautiful. Cost: love as entertainment, and pleasure over depth."},6:{themes:['service'],text:"You show affection through service. You prove you care by doing the task, then wonder why nobody noticed.",detail:"You love through service. Gift: showing care by fixing things, and work in beauty or health. Cost: love that criticises, and a body that gets overindulged."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine'],text:"Partnership is where your talent for balance gets used, and where you trade your position for peace.",detail:"Venus is at home here. Gift: partnership feels natural, and a beautiful, loving spouse. Cost: the natural blind spot, which is losing yourself in the couple."},8:{themes:['power_and_control','depth_over_breadth'],text:"What you love, you want completely, and that intensity will not settle for something more comfortable.",detail:"Love and money run intense, hidden, and life-changing. Gift: sexual depth, inheritance, and money through partnership. Cost: income that comes in surges and then reverses, and love that consumes."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"You are drawn to what is foreign to you, in people and in beliefs, and the distance is part of the pull.",detail:"You find beauty in belief. Gift: love from abroad, art through faith, and a generous philosophy. Cost: idealising what is far away."},10:{themes:['late_recognition','leadership'],text:"Being likeable is part of your public role, so your relationships and your career are the same conversation.",detail:"You have public grace. Gift: a career in beauty, art, or diplomacy, and an audience that loves you. Cost: being liked before being respected."},11:{themes:['mass_reach'],text:"Friendship is where your affection has the most room, and your network pays you in opportunity rather than closeness.",detail:"You gain through charm. Gift: friends who bring good fortune, and beautiful networks. Cost: friendships that are transactions."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','letting_go'],text:"You love privately and from a distance, and an unspoken attachment can run for years on almost nothing.",detail:"This is secret love and hidden pleasure. Gift: beauty in private places, spiritual love, and romance abroad. Cost: a pull toward secret affairs, loneliness in love, and pleasure that hides."}},Mars:{1:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','identity_core'],text:"Your drive is visible and physical. People meet the push before they meet the reasons behind it.",detail:"Force is your first impression. Gift: physical energy, courage, decisiveness, and a body that acts. Cost: temper, haste that invites accidents, and a presence that reads as aggressive before you open your mouth. For you, patience is learned, not natural."},2:{themes:['money_perception','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You fight over money and worth, and money arguments here are rarely about the actual amount.",detail:"You fight for money and with words. Gift: earning hard and a voice that cuts. Cost: harsh words that hurt family, and money won and lost on impulse."},3:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','voice_income'],text:"Your aggression comes out as speech. You argue well, and you win arguments you would have done better to leave.",detail:"Courage is the gift. You act where others stop to think. Gift: bravery, initiative, and drive in communication. Cost: conflict with siblings, and a nervous energy that picks fights. This is one of the best houses for Mars."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','childhood_weight'],text:"There is friction at your base, in the home or in how the home used to be, and it does not stay there.",detail:"There is heat in the home. Conflict is how you learned about family. Gift: protective strength, and property through effort. Cost: arguments at the dinner table, a mother who may have fought hard, and trouble finding peace where you live."},5:{themes:['creativity','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You push hardest when you are making something, and competition sharpens the work until it starts to replace it.",detail:"This is creative fire and competitive love. Gift: passionate creating, courage in romance, and drive in your children. Cost: conflict with children, a gambling streak, and love as a contest."},6:{themes:['health_discipline','service'],text:"Your drive goes into the daily grind, which gets a lot done and burns your body as fuel.",detail:"You win by outlasting. Enemies become fuel. Gift: beating opposition, strength at work, and health through effort. Cost: a life that needs a fight, strain injuries from pushing too hard, and conflict with staff or colleagues. This is one of Mars's best houses."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"The heat in your life comes through partnership. You either partner with a fighter or become one.",detail:"Your drive lands inside partnership. Your reflex is to treat your partner as an opponent in an argument you need to win. Gift: a passionate, active partner and courage in relationships. Cost: conflict in marriage, a partner who fights, and heat that tends to settle around age twenty-eight into an intensity you can steer."},8:{themes:['power_and_control','depth_over_breadth'],text:"You are willing to go where other people stop. That is your edge in a crisis, and it is also your appetite for one.",detail:"Your force goes into hidden things. Gift: courage in a crisis, research, surgery, and drive toward the occult. Cost: a higher risk of accidents and sudden losses, fights over inheritance, and anger that goes underground. Traditionally a hard placement."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You fight for your beliefs, and here conviction hardens into something you defend rather than question.",detail:"You fight for beliefs. Gift: brave conviction, and a father who pushed you. Cost: crusading, conflict with teachers, and a philosophy that needs enemies."},10:{themes:['leadership','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your ambition is open and people can see it, which wins you the role and the pushback at the same time.",detail:"Your ambition is public and physical. Gift: command, achievement, and a career built on drive. Cost: conflict with authority, a ruthless reputation, and a father who was forceful. Mars is strong here. This is the general's house."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','leadership'],text:"You drive the group forward, which makes you useful to it and puts you at odds with it on a regular basis.",detail:"You push networks to move. Gift: gains through effort, energetic friends, and goals reached. Cost: conflict in groups, competitive friends, and pushing people away by pushing too hard."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','health_discipline'],text:"Your anger goes underground instead of out, and what you do not express comes back as tiredness.",detail:"Your energy turns inward, sometimes against yourself. Gift: hidden strength, courage when alone, and drive in foreign places. Cost: self-sabotage, secret enemies, and anger with no outlet. Point it outward, or it becomes the enemy inside."}},Jupiter:{1:{themes:['gifts','identity_core'],text:"People give you room. They trust you on presence alone, which is a real asset and easy to spend.",detail:"Your presence is expansive. Gift: people trust you before you have earned it, and you are generous with that trust. Cost: a tendency to put on weight, in the body or in self-importance."},2:{themes:['money_perception'],text:"Money comes in more easily than it stays, because the appetite that earns it also grows what you think you need.",detail:"Wealth comes through wisdom. Gift: money arrives when you teach, a generous voice, and a family that gave. Cost: spending on principle, and a mouth that lectures."},3:{themes:['voice_income','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your reach is through words. People believe you when you speak, which gives you power and a constant duty to be accurate.",detail:"You have the preacher's voice. Gift: courage in belief, siblings who guide you, and communication that inspires. Cost: every message wants to be a sermon."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','family_conditioning'],text:"Your family or home really supports you, and the comfort there quietly delays you leaving.",detail:"The home was generous, or you make it so. Gift: property, a mother who gave, and contentment at the root. Cost: a home that grows past what you can hold, and comfort that stops growth."},5:{themes:['creativity','gifts'],text:"What you make has scale built in, and the risk is starting big instead of simply starting.",detail:"You have creative luck and a gift for teaching. Gift: knowledge gathers around you, children who are blessings, and wisdom in love. Cost: being too generous with what you make, and pride in your children."},6:{themes:['service','health_discipline'],text:"You get further by being useful than by being ambitious, and daily work is where your luck actually lands.",detail:"You grow through service. Gift: obstacles make you bigger, and enemies become teachers. Cost: weight from work, and a faith tested by daily struggle."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine'],text:"Partnership grows your position, and it grows your obligations at exactly the same rate.",detail:"Your partner is a teacher. Gift: marriage widens how you see the world, and a wise, generous spouse. Cost: a partner who preaches, and growth that depends on being in a couple."},8:{themes:['power_and_control','money_perception'],text:"Other people's money and resources open up to you. That is real support, and a kind of leverage that comes with terms.",detail:"Other people's resources flow to you. Gift: inheritance, investment, money through partnership, and occult wisdom. Cost: money that comes and goes through crisis, and faith tested by loss."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','becoming'],text:"Belief, study, and travel are how you grow, and life keeps offering you teachers you are slow to accept.",detail:"This is Jupiter's own house. Gift: faith, teaching, fortune, and a father who was a guru. Cost: dogma, and a philosophy that never doubts itself."},10:{themes:['late_recognition','leadership'],text:"Your public standing builds slowly, and the position tends to arrive bigger than the ambition that asked for it.",detail:"Your public standing comes through wisdom. Gift: being known as the one who knows, and a career in teaching, law, or advice. Cost: a reputation that gets ahead of the substance."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','money_perception'],text:"Your network is your wealth. Gains here come through people rather than through direct effort.",detail:"Your gains multiply through groups. Gift: networks are your fortune, friends are teachers, and your goals are blessed. Cost: stretching too thin by being generous to many."},12:{themes:['spiritual_path','letting_go'],text:"What supports you is mostly invisible, and you underrate it because it never sent you a bill.",detail:"Private faith and inherited authority work behind the scenes. Gift: mentors, service, time alone that feeds you, and fortune from abroad. Cost: a quiet drain. You give too much to causes, people, and ideas without keeping track, and you mistake withdrawing for devotion."}},Saturn:{1:{themes:['identity_core','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You carry weight in how you come across, and your self-doubt is built in, not a mood you can argue your way out of.",detail:"You were serious when young. Gift: discipline, endurance, and a life that often gets lighter after thirty-six. Cost: a body and a self that felt old before their time."},2:{themes:['money_perception'],text:"You work for money. It comes late and stays. Scarcity becomes a habit that outlasts the times that taught it.",detail:"Money is slow and earned. Gift: wealth that lasts once built. Cost: a fear of not having enough that is built in, not imagined, and a voice that holds back."},3:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','childhood_weight'],text:"Your speech was corrected early, so you edit before you speak, and others read the caution as reserve.",detail:"Courage is built, not given. Gift: communication that gets better with age, and disciplined effort. Cost: fear of speaking up, and siblings who could feel like a burden. Saturn does well here."},4:{themes:['childhood_weight','home_foundation'],text:"Your foundation was built under pressure, and you have been reinforcing it ever since without calling it that.",detail:"The home was heavy. Gift: the stability you built because you did not have it. Cost: a childhood that could feel cold, a mother who may have been all duty, and a home that feels like work."},5:{themes:['creativity','under_producing'],text:"Making things is serious work for you, not play, and your standards arrive long before your skill does.",detail:"This is creative discipline. Gift: recognition that is slow, technical, and earned, and then stays. Cost: children who may come later, joy that is rationed, and creativity that feels like homework."},6:{themes:['health_discipline','service'],text:"Your body sets the rules and enforces them, so discipline is not a virtue for you. It is the price of working at all.",detail:"You outwork obstacles. Gift: long-term health problems and long-term enemies both give way to persistence. Cost: work that never ends. Saturn is strong here."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Partnership is a structure with duties. It either becomes something you can lean on or it becomes the lesson.",detail:"Partnership is a duty, and it lasts. Gift: a commitment that survives everything. Cost: you take the relationship on and then carry it alone, and marriage may come late or feel heavy."},8:{themes:['power_and_control','depth_over_breadth'],text:"You are careful with what you share, because the real fear is losing control, not losing money.",detail:"Shared money and hidden matters get audited. Gift: tradition links it with a long life, and with resilience through loss. Cost: borrowing and leverage get punished, inheritance comes late, and you fear what is hidden."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','becoming'],text:"You have to earn your beliefs rather than inherit them, so faith comes slowly here and lasts once it arrives.",detail:"Your faith gets tested and then holds firm. Gift: a philosophy that survived doubt, and a teacher who arrives late. Cost: a father who may have felt cold, and beliefs that are rigid or missing."},10:{themes:['late_recognition','leadership'],text:"Your career is the long carry. Recognition is held back until the work cannot be denied, and then it does not leave.",detail:"Your career is your life's work, and it takes your life. Gift: real authority, often after forty. Cost: a father who demanded a lot, and a reputation built on hard labour. Saturn is strong here."},11:{themes:['isolation_risk','mass_reach'],text:"Your friends are few and long-lasting, and you are the one who carries the group's obligations.",detail:"Gains are slow and permanent. Gift: few friends, kept forever, and goals reached late. Cost: loneliness in a crowd. Saturn is strong here."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','letting_go'],text:"Your heaviest work happens out of sight, and you finish things nobody thinks to credit you for.",detail:"Let go of control over what you cannot see. Gift: spiritual discipline, and time alone that helps you mature. Cost: hidden enemies, isolation, and a fear of losing what you never held."}},Uranus:{1:{themes:['reinvention','identity_core'],text:"You are wired to break your own patterns, so your identity keeps reorganising instead of settling."},2:{themes:['money_perception','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"Your income comes in unevenly, and the steady money other people budget with is not available to you."},3:{themes:['mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your thinking jumps instead of walking. That gives you the insight and loses your audience mid-sentence."},4:{themes:['home_foundation','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"Your home base moves more than most, by choice or by circumstance, so you build roots rather than inherit them."},5:{themes:['creativity','reinvention'],text:"What you make is odd on purpose, and the oddness that makes it yours also makes it slow to find a place."},6:{themes:['freedom_vs_structure','health_discipline'],text:"You cannot keep a routine you did not design, and your body objects to work that bores it."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"You need room inside a partnership, and the setup that works for you does not look like anyone else's."},8:{themes:['power_and_control','reinvention'],text:"Crises hit suddenly, not gradually, and what breaks is usually the thing you most wanted to control."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','reinvention'],text:"Your beliefs have been rebuilt from the ground up at least once, and handed-down doctrine does not survive contact with you."},10:{themes:['reinvention','late_recognition'],text:"Your career changes shape more than once, and the pattern only makes sense looking back."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"You join unusual groups and leave them cleanly, so your network is wide rather than deep."},12:{themes:['letting_go','isolation_risk'],text:"What shakes you up comes from somewhere you cannot see, and the release is sudden rather than negotiated."}},Neptune:{1:{themes:['identity_core','isolation_risk'],text:"People see what they need to see in you, and correcting that costs more effort than living with it."},2:{themes:['money_perception'],text:"Money is unclear for you. The numbers blur, you feel value rather than count it, and the accounting keeps getting put off."},3:{themes:['voice_income','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Your words work by suggestion, not statement. That is powerful in art and vague in agreements."},4:{themes:['family_conditioning','childhood_weight'],text:"Something at the root of your family goes unspoken, and the family story you were given has soft edges where the facts should be."},5:{themes:['creativity','gifts'],text:"What you make comes through you rather than from you, so you produce work you cannot later explain or reliably repeat."},6:{themes:['health_discipline','service'],text:"Your daily routine falls apart unless you protect it, and your body reacts to atmosphere as much as to anything physical."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','letting_go'],text:"You idealise a partner before you even meet them, which builds the disappointment into the relationship from the start."},8:{themes:['letting_go','power_and_control'],text:"Your boundaries around shared money and shared feelings stay leaky, and you find out afterwards what you gave away."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','outside_counsel'],text:"Faith comes naturally to you rather than through reasoning, and the openness that makes you devoted also makes you easy to fool."},10:{themes:['mass_reach','late_recognition'],text:"The public sees an image rather than a person, and the image runs ahead of what you have actually built."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','spiritual_path'],text:"You join causes rather than clubs, and the group's ideal is easier to love than its members."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','spiritual_path'],text:"Time alone is how you work best, and you are the one who draws the line between retreat and disappearing."}},Pluto:{1:{themes:['reinvention','identity_core'],text:"You rebuild yourself completely rather than adjusting, and people who knew the earlier you do not recognise the current one."},2:{themes:['money_perception','power_and_control'],text:"Money feels like survival for you, so a threat to your money feels like a threat to your whole existence."},3:{themes:['voice_income','power_and_control'],text:"You speak with force whether you mean to or not, and your words land harder than the volume suggests."},4:{themes:['family_conditioning','childhood_weight'],text:"Your family had a power structure, and you learned it early and in detail, without being told it was a lesson."},5:{themes:['creativity','depth_over_breadth'],text:"What you make comes out of something that cost you, and the lighter version of your work never quite convinces."},6:{themes:['service','reinvention'],text:"Your daily work changes you, and you keep taking on tasks that require becoming someone else to finish."},7:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','power_and_control'],text:"Partnership runs intense and unequal until the question of power gets put openly on the table."},8:{themes:['power_and_control','depth_over_breadth'],text:"You are at your most capable in a crisis. That is real power, and one reason you keep ending up near one."},9:{themes:['spiritual_path','reinvention'],text:"One of your beliefs has already collapsed and been rebuilt, and the rebuilt one has teeth the inherited one lacked."},10:{themes:['leadership','power_and_control'],text:"Your public position carries more force than you mean it to, so you either use that authority on purpose or it leaks."},11:{themes:['mass_reach','power_and_control'],text:"The groups you join get reshaped around you, whether or not that was the plan."},12:{themes:['isolation_risk','letting_go'],text:"What you are working on is buried and old, and most of your life's work happens where no one can check it."}}},u={'Sun-Moon':{harmony:{themes:['identity_core','emotional_pattern'],text:"What you want and what you need point the same way. That removes a common friction, and it also removes a useful check on yourself.",detail:"You feel at ease with yourself, and confidence comes easily."},tension:{themes:['identity_core','emotional_pattern'],text:"What you intend and what you need pull apart, so by Thursday your mood is arguing with the plan you committed to on Monday.",detail:"What you want and what you need pull apart, which makes you restless, self-critical, and driven. If you were born near a full moon (Sun and Moon opposite), you feel pulled between yourself and others. You see both sides and look for balance in relationships."}},'Sun-Mercury':{harmony:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','identity_core'],text:"You think the way you are. Your reasoning and your identity run on one tool, which is efficient, and it makes criticism of an idea feel like criticism of you."},tension:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','identity_core'],text:"What you say and what you mean are slightly out of step, so even careful listeners end up misquoting you."}},'Sun-Venus':{harmony:{themes:['identity_core','gifts'],text:"Being liked comes easily and costs you little. That is a real asset, and poor practice for being disliked."},tension:{themes:['identity_core','money_perception'],text:"You want approval and resent needing it, so you undercut your charm right about when it starts working."}},'Sun-Mars':{harmony:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','leadership'],text:"Your will and your actions are wired together. You decide and move in one go, which is decisive and skips the second look.",detail:"You act with confidence and have plenty of physical drive."},tension:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your drive fights your own direction, so your effort makes heat for a while before it gets you anywhere.",detail:"Anger at authority and at yourself, and energy that fights its own goals. You may clash with men, with authority, and with partners over control."}},'Sun-Saturn':{harmony:{themes:['late_recognition','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Patience with yourself is built in. The ambition is real, the timeline is long, and neither is up for debate.",detail:"Your discipline serves you, and what you achieve tends to last."},tension:{themes:['under_producing','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Something in you checks the work before it starts, so your output gets delayed by a standard you never agreed to.",detail:"Self-doubt, fear of failure, and the inner critic. Authority feels like the enemy, and your father can feel like an opponent."}},'Moon-Venus':{harmony:{themes:['emotional_pattern','marriage_as_engine'],text:"You are easy to be around and you know it. That makes closeness easy, and it makes conflict feel like bad manners.",detail:"You bring warmth and charm, and love comes easily to you."},tension:{themes:['emotional_pattern','money_perception'],text:"What comforts you and what you find beautiful disagree, so you keep choosing between being soothed and being satisfied.",detail:"Your emotional needs and your love pull apart, and you go looking for comfort. Love and security feel at odds, and you look in others for what you cannot feel yourself."}},'Moon-Mars':{harmony:{themes:['emotional_pattern','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your feelings turn into action quickly. That clears the air and skips the step where you check you read things right.",detail:"Your feelings give you drive and a passionate kind of courage."},tension:{themes:['emotional_pattern','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your reaction gets ahead of your judgement, and the apology is usually more work than a pause would have been.",detail:"Quick anger, emotional ups and downs, and friction with your mother. Your feelings and actions are at war, and you may fight with women or partners."}},'Moon-Saturn':{harmony:{themes:['emotional_pattern','health_discipline'],text:"You hold feelings in without denying them, which makes you steady in a crisis and slow to admit you need anything.",detail:"You keep your feelings disciplined, and people can rely on you."},tension:{themes:['childhood_weight','emotional_pattern'],text:"Comfort was rationed when you were young, so you treat your own needs with suspicion and call the refusal maturity.",detail:"Sadness, self-criticism, and trouble receiving. Duty fights feeling, and relationships can feel like an obligation."}},'Moon-Pluto':{harmony:{themes:['emotional_pattern','depth_over_breadth'],text:"You can sit with what most people look away from, which makes you useful in other people's worst weeks."},tension:{themes:['power_and_control','emotional_pattern'],text:"Your attachments run deep and defensive, and the fear of being left shows up looking like control."}},'Mercury-Saturn':{harmony:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','late_recognition'],text:"Your thinking is slow, structured, and easy to check. Over ten years, that is worth more than being quick for ten minutes."},tension:{themes:['under_producing','mind_as_instrument'],text:"You doubt a thought before you finish it, so good ideas get edited down into silence."}},'Venus-Mars':{harmony:{themes:['creativity','marriage_as_engine'],text:"What you want and what you go after line up, so attraction turns into action without a long inner debate.",detail:"Desire and affection work together easily for you."},tension:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','emotional_pattern'],text:"What attracts you and what you chase are not the same thing. That friction is how you are set up, not a fault.",detail:"Desire and love pull apart: the part of you that wants and the part that loves do not agree. Attraction and conflict show up in the same relationship."}},'Venus-Saturn':{harmony:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','late_recognition'],text:"You commit for the long term and mean it. That builds lasting relationships, and from outside your affection can look like duty.",detail:"Your love endures, and your commitments last."},tension:{themes:['money_perception','marriage_as_engine'],text:"Love and money both feel conditional, so you work for what should have been given and distrust it when it comes.",detail:"Fear of not being lovable, and holding back. Love feels like duty, and partners may be older, colder, or unavailable."}},'Mars-Saturn':{harmony:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','health_discipline'],text:"Your effort is disciplined, not explosive. You push in a straight line for a long time.",detail:"You have endurance, and you keep your strength under control."},tension:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','under_producing'],text:"Your push hits a wall that is partly your own, so your drive gets spent on resistance before it reaches the work.",detail:"Blocked drive, anger held in, and effort that hits a wall. Action fights caution, and you fight with authority."}},'Sun-Jupiter':{harmony:{themes:['gifts','identity_core'],text:"You get more room than the evidence justifies. That is a real advantage, and poor practice in limits.",detail:"Luck and ease tend to come to you naturally."},tension:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','money_perception'],text:"Your reach goes past your structure, so you commit to something big and then have to build the support under it.",detail:"Overconfidence, overreach, and promises not kept. Ego pulls against belief, and you can end up preaching."}},'Moon-Jupiter':{harmony:{themes:['emotional_pattern','gifts'],text:"Your default emotional setting is generous. It draws people in and makes it hard to notice when you are running on empty."},tension:{themes:['emotional_pattern','health_discipline'],text:"Your feelings swell. The mood is big, your appetite matches it, and moderation feels like being deprived."}},'Venus-Pluto':{harmony:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','depth_over_breadth'],text:"You love deeply and can stay through the parts most people walk out on. That is loyalty, and a high tolerance for intensity."},tension:{themes:['power_and_control','marriage_as_engine'],text:"Desire and control get tangled, so your attachments carry a grip you did not mean to apply."}},'Mars-Pluto':{harmony:{themes:['power_and_control','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You keep force in reserve and use it once rather than again and again. That works, and it makes people wary of you before you have done anything."},tension:{themes:['power_and_control','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your will keeps running into an immovable object, and the temptation is to push harder rather than change course."}},'Sun-Pluto':{harmony:{themes:['leadership','power_and_control'],text:"You carry authority without raising your voice, and the room adjusts around you before anyone can say why."},tension:{themes:['reinvention','power_and_control'],text:"Your identity gets torn down and rebuilt from time to time, and the different versions of you are not on speaking terms."}},'Sun-Uranus':{harmony:{themes:['reinvention','identity_core'],text:"You are original by design, so being different feels like an asset rather than a wound, and the standard version of anything bores you fast."},tension:{themes:['freedom_vs_structure','reinvention'],text:"You break the arrangement just as it starts to hold, and you defend your freedom against things that were not threatening it."}},'Moon-Uranus':{harmony:{themes:['freedom_vs_structure','emotional_pattern'],text:"You need room in your private life, and you can have it without the whole structure becoming shaky."},tension:{themes:['emotional_pattern','isolation_risk'],text:"Closeness sets off the urge to leave, so you leave the room emotionally a while before you leave it physically."}},'Saturn-Pluto':{harmony:{themes:['power_and_control','late_recognition'],text:"You get through what breaks other people, and you built that strength rather than being given it."},tension:{themes:['power_and_control','reinvention'],text:"Pressure keeps building in your life until something has to be rebuilt, not just repaired."}},'Mercury-Mars':{harmony:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"You think fast and say it, which makes you strong in an argument and quick to decide."},tension:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Your words run ahead of your judgement, and the line that wins the argument is the one you have to take back."}}},l={stellium:{themes:['depth_over_breadth','identity_core'],text:"You have a stellium (three or more planets in one area of the chart). A big share of your life goes into a single question. That focus is both your specialty and your blind spot.",weight:1.5},grandTrine:{themes:['gifts','under_producing'],text:"You have a grand trine (three planets that support each other in a closed loop). It makes one area unusually easy, so you rarely work at it. The talent runs by itself until you stop asking anything of it.",weight:1.5},tSquare:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','power_and_control'],text:"You have a T-square (two opposing planets with a third pressing on both). The pressure has nowhere to settle, so it comes out as drive. This pattern produces output and does not offer rest.",weight:1.5}},y={Fire:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','under_producing'],text:"Your chart has little Fire (the element of drive). Getting started does not come automatically, so you have to schedule momentum rather than wait for it."},Earth:{themes:['money_perception','health_discipline'],text:"Your chart has little Earth (the practical element). The plan is vivid, and the logistics stay someone else's problem until they become yours. You have to build the boring layer on purpose."},Air:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','outside_counsel'],text:"Your chart has little Air (the element of thinking). You decide from feeling and instinct rather than argument, which is fast and hard to explain to people who need reasons."},Water:{themes:['emotional_pattern','outside_counsel'],text:"Your chart has little Water (the element of feeling). You notice your own emotions late, usually as a body state or as a decision you have already made."}},c={Fire:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','under_producing'],text:"Fire (the element of drive) dominates your chart. You start with force and lose interest at the upkeep stage, which is where most of the value actually builds up."},Earth:{themes:['money_perception','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"Earth (the practical element) dominates your chart. You build things that last and resist changing them long after the world around them has changed."},Air:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','under_producing'],text:"Air (the element of thinking) dominates your chart. You can argue every side, which makes you fair and slow, and lets analysis stand in for the decision."},Water:{themes:['emotional_pattern','family_conditioning'],text:"Water (the element of feeling) dominates your chart. You read the room accurately and take it personally, so other people's weather becomes your climate."}},p={Fire:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','creativity'],text:"You get things moving through real passion, not performance. A real, lasting interest carries you further than raw effort without one.",detail:"When something really holds your attention, follow-through comes easily and results tend to build quickly. The risk is spreading that intensity across too many interests at once, so none of them gets the steady attention that actually produces something."},Earth:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','money_perception'],text:"You get things moving through systems. A written routine you repeat every day beats a big plan you revisit now and then.",detail:"Small, concrete, scheduled steps are what actually move things for you. Inspiration alone tends to stall without a structure under it. The risk is building a detailed system and then not running it. It only works if you keep it daily, not if you admire it."},Air:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','becoming'],text:"You get things moving through understanding. Thinking a subject through clearly tends to move things more than raw effort or feeling.",detail:"Real command of a subject, worked through rather than skimmed, is where your results come from. The risk is staying in thought forever. Clarity has to turn into one committed action at some point, or the understanding stays theory."},Water:{themes:['emotional_pattern','home_foundation'],text:"You get things moving through emotional alignment. Your inner state and your surroundings need to match what you want before your effort lands well.",detail:"Unsettled feelings tend to block results for you more than for the other elements. So looking after your space and your own state is not a detour from the work. It is part of it. The risk is waiting for the feeling to be perfect before you act at all."}},f={Sun:{themes:['identity_core','leadership'],text:"The Sun rules your chart (it rules your rising sign, so it steers the whole chart). Identity and being seen are your central question: what people see you doing is not separate from who you are."},Moon:{themes:['emotional_pattern','home_foundation'],text:"The Moon rules your chart (it rules your rising sign, so it steers the whole chart). Your inner state runs the machine. Mood is not a side effect for you. It is the condition everything runs on."},Mercury:{themes:['mind_as_instrument','voice_income'],text:"Mercury rules your chart (it rules your rising sign, so it steers the whole chart). Your life runs through thinking and speaking, and an idle mind feels to you like being unwell."},Venus:{themes:['marriage_as_engine','money_perception'],text:"Venus rules your chart (it rules your rising sign, so it steers the whole chart). Your life is organised around what you value and who you are bound to, and both are structural, not sentimental."},Mars:{themes:['drive_vs_resistance','leadership'],text:"Mars rules your chart (it rules your rising sign, so it steers the whole chart). You are defined by what you push against, and a life with no fight in it goes flat."},Jupiter:{themes:['spiritual_path','mass_reach'],text:"Jupiter rules your chart (it rules your rising sign, so it steers the whole chart). Your life grows through belief and reach, and holding back is a discipline you have to add yourself."},Saturn:{themes:['late_recognition','drive_vs_resistance'],text:"Saturn rules your chart (it rules your rising sign, so it steers the whole chart). Your life is a long build with the payoff at the end, and early results are not the measure."},Uranus:{themes:['reinvention','freedom_vs_structure'],text:"Uranus rules your chart (it rules your rising sign, so it steers the whole chart). The shape of your life changes more than once, and consistency is not the standard to hold yourself to."},Neptune:{themes:['spiritual_path','creativity'],text:"Neptune rules your chart (it rules your rising sign, so it steers the whole chart). Your life runs on something you cannot fully explain, and precision is a discipline you have to bring in from outside."},Pluto:{themes:['power_and_control','reinvention'],text:"Pluto rules your chart (it rules your rising sign, so it steers the whole chart). Your life moves by tearing down and rebuilding, and each time the question is what you do with the power that comes back."}},w={Saturn:{1:{themes:['timing_now','identity_core'],text:"Saturn is crossing your first house (self and body). Your identity is being rebuilt to a stricter standard, and the process shows on you."},2:{themes:['timing_now','money_perception'],text:"Saturn is in your second house (money and worth). Your money and self-worth are under review, and whatever cannot pay for itself is being cut from the budget."},3:{themes:['timing_now','mind_as_instrument'],text:"Saturn is in your third house (speech and writing). The way you speak and write is being disciplined, so you say less and say it more accurately."},4:{themes:['timing_now','home_foundation'],text:"Saturn is in your fourth house (home and family). Your home base is being repaired or replaced, and family duty weighs more than usual right now."},5:{themes:['timing_now','creativity'],text:"Saturn is in your fifth house (creativity and play). Making things is serious work now, and play has to be scheduled or it does not happen."},6:{themes:['timing_now','health_discipline'],text:"Saturn is in your sixth house (work and health). Your body and your daily routine set the rules, and this cycle the rules are not negotiable."},7:{themes:['timing_now','marriage_as_engine'],text:"Saturn is in your seventh house (partnership). Your partnerships are being stress-tested, and whatever is not holding weight tends to show it."},8:{themes:['timing_now','power_and_control'],text:"Saturn is in your eighth house (shared money and debt). Shared money, debt, and dependence get reorganised, and the reckoning is overdue rather than sudden."},9:{themes:['timing_now','spiritual_path'],text:"Saturn is in your ninth house (belief and study). Your beliefs are being tested against evidence, and the parts you inherited rather than earned often do not survive."},10:{themes:['timing_now','late_recognition'],text:"Saturn is at the top of your chart (your tenth house, career and public standing). Your public position is being weighed, and what you have actually built is what counts."},11:{themes:['timing_now','mass_reach'],text:"Saturn is in your eleventh house (friends and networks). Your network is being pruned, and friendships of convenience rather than substance tend to end quietly."},12:{themes:['timing_now','letting_go'],text:"Saturn is in your twelfth house (the hidden, private part of life). The work goes unseen and recognition is not due yet. This is the clearing out before Saturn crosses your first house."}},Jupiter:{1:{themes:['timing_now','identity_core'],text:"Jupiter is crossing your first house (self and body). You take up more room, and you can ask for better terms than the ones you have been accepting."},2:{themes:['timing_now','money_perception'],text:"Jupiter is in your second house (money and worth). Your income and your appetite both grow, and only one of them does it without your help."},3:{themes:['timing_now','voice_income'],text:"Jupiter is in your third house (speech and writing). What you say travels further than usual, so this is a window for publishing, not perfecting."},4:{themes:['timing_now','home_foundation'],text:"Jupiter is in your fourth house (home and family). Home and family gain ground, and it is a good window for moving or growing your home base."},5:{themes:['timing_now','creativity'],text:"Jupiter is in your fifth house (creativity and play). Output counts for more than polish now, and what you make finds an audience more easily than usual."},6:{themes:['timing_now','health_discipline'],text:"Jupiter is in your sixth house (work and health). Work and health respond to effort now, so systems you set up this year hold longer than they normally would."},7:{themes:['timing_now','marriage_as_engine'],text:"Jupiter is in your seventh house (partnership and contracts). Partnerships and contracts open up, and the terms on offer now are better than the ones you had settled for."},8:{themes:['timing_now','power_and_control'],text:"Jupiter is in your eighth house (shared money and other people's resources). Other people's resources become available. That is real leverage, and it still comes with terms."},9:{themes:['timing_now','spiritual_path'],text:"Jupiter is in your ninth house (belief, study, and travel). Study, travel, and teaching open up, and a belief you have been circling can take shape this year."},10:{themes:['timing_now','late_recognition'],text:"Jupiter is at the top of your chart (your tenth house, career and public standing). Your public role grows, and this is a rare stretch for asking instead of waiting."},11:{themes:['timing_now','mass_reach','money_perception'],text:"Jupiter is in your eleventh house (friends, networks, and gains). Tradition counts this among the best windows for gains, so it is a strong time to publish, release, sell, and grow your audience.",weight:1.5},12:{themes:['timing_now','letting_go'],text:"Jupiter is in your twelfth house (the hidden, private part of life). This year's gains are private, in rest, study, and repair, and they do not show on the outside yet."}},Rahu:{1:{themes:['timing_now','identity_core'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your first house (self and body). Attention lands on you whether you wanted it or not, and the urge to become someone new runs loud."},2:{themes:['timing_now','money_perception'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your second house (money and worth). Money and self-worth run hot, and the hunger to build up more gets ahead of the plan for it."},3:{themes:['timing_now','voice_income'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your third house (speech and writing). Your voice reaches further and faster now, and the volume runs ahead of the editing."},4:{themes:['timing_now','home_foundation'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your fourth house (home and family). Your home base feels unsettled, and the pull to move or rearrange your home is stronger than the reason for it."},5:{themes:['timing_now','creativity'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your fifth house (creativity and play). What you make wants scale now, and the hunger for an audience can outrun the quality of the work."},6:{themes:['timing_now','health_discipline'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your sixth house (work and health). Work multiplies and your body is asked for more than it agreed to, so your routine needs a limit built in."},7:{themes:['timing_now','marriage_as_engine'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your seventh house (partnership). Partnerships are charged and matter a lot now, and the people arriving are not neutral to where you are heading."},8:{themes:['timing_now','power_and_control'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your eighth house (shared money and hidden things). Shared money, obligations, and buried issues come up now, and the pull toward risk is strong."},9:{themes:['timing_now','spiritual_path','outside_counsel'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your ninth house (belief and teachers). A belief or a teacher takes hold fast, which is why a second opinion is worth more than usual this cycle."},10:{themes:['timing_now','late_recognition'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is at the top of your chart (your tenth house, career and public standing). Your public ambition is switched on, and it moves faster than the structure supporting it."},11:{themes:['timing_now','mass_reach'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your eleventh house (friends and networks). Your network grows fast and gains come through people, though not all of them are who they seem."},12:{themes:['timing_now','isolation_risk'],text:"The north node (a point that marks appetite and direction) is in your twelfth house (the hidden, private part of life). The pull is inward and away, and pulling back is productive as long as it stays a choice."}}},b={saturn:{themes:['timing_now','becoming'],text:"Saturn has come back to where it was when you were born, which happens near ages twenty-nine, fifty-eight, and eighty-seven. Your life's structure gets audited, and whatever you built on borrowed terms tends to come apart. It is not punishment. It is the bill arriving.",weight:1.5},jupiter:{themes:['timing_now','becoming'],text:"Jupiter has come back to where it was when you were born, which happens about every twelve years. A new chapter opens on the same subject, and the appetite shows up some months before the plan does."},nodal:{themes:['timing_now','becoming'],text:"The nodes (two points where the Moon's path crosses the Sun's, read as your direction) are back where they were at your birth. This happens roughly every eighteen and a half years. The question of direction opens again, and the answer you gave last time no longer fits the person giving it.",weight:1.5}},v=[{term:'rising sign',definition:"The zodiac sign that was rising over the eastern horizon at the time and place you were born. It changes about every two hours, which is why an exact birth time matters. It describes how you meet the world and how people read you before they know you, not what you are like on the inside."},{term:'house',definition:"One of twelve sections of the sky, worked out from your birth time and place. Each one covers an area of life. The first is self and appearance, the fourth is home and roots, the seventh is partnership, and the tenth is public standing. The house a planet sits in shows which area of your life it works in."},{term:'aspect',definition:"The angle between two planets, measured in degrees around the circle of the chart. Certain angles count because the two planets are then read as working together or working against each other. An aspect describes a relationship between two parts of you, not an event."},{term:'conjunction',definition:"Two planets in almost the same place in the sky, within a few degrees of each other. They merge: you get one behaviour with both natures in it, and it is hard to pull the two apart afterwards. Whether that helps depends on which planets they are."},{term:'opposition',definition:"Two planets on opposite sides of the chart, about a hundred and eighty degrees apart. Both needs are real and pull in different directions, so the pattern tends to show up through other people. They carry one side of it while you carry the other."},{term:'trine',definition:"Two planets about a hundred and twenty degrees apart, in signs of the same element (Fire, Earth, Air, or Water). The two work together with no friction, which makes the ability easy, and so easy to leave undeveloped. Trines describe what runs by itself, for better and for worse."},{term:'square',definition:"Two planets about ninety degrees apart. Both needs are urgent and neither gives way, so this creates pressure and, over time, skill. Squares are where most of the real work of a chart gets done."},{term:'sextile',definition:"Two planets about sixty degrees apart. A mild, workable link: the ability is there, but you have to pick it up on purpose rather than having it arrive by itself. Sextiles describe an opportunity, not a given."},{term:'stellium',definition:"Three or more planets grouped in the same sign or the same house. It focuses a big share of the chart on one subject, which builds real skill in that area and leaves other areas thinner."},{term:'grand trine',definition:"Three planets each about a hundred and twenty degrees from the other two, making a closed triangle, usually in signs of one element. It marks an area of life that works without effort, which is why it is often the least developed area."},{term:'T-square',definition:"Two planets in opposition (on opposite sides of the chart), with a third at right angles to both. The third is pressed from two sides at once. It takes the pressure of the whole pattern and turns it into action. That is why this pattern is linked with drive rather than ease."},{term:'chart ruler',definition:"The planet that rules your rising sign. It is treated as the manager of the whole chart. Its sign, house, and condition describe the main priority of your life: what the rest of the chart is arranged around."},{term:'transit',definition:"Where a planet is in the sky right now, compared with where it was when you were born. Slow planets like Saturn and Jupiter spend months or years in one house of your chart. That makes them useful for describing your current period rather than your permanent makeup."},{term:'Saturn return',definition:"The time when Saturn comes back to where it was at your birth. It takes about twenty-nine and a half years, so it falls near ages twenty-nine, fifty-eight, and eighty-seven. It is read as an audit: commitments made on borrowed terms tend to get renegotiated or ended."},{term:'north node',definition:"One of the two points where the Moon's path crosses the Sun's path, called Rahu in the Indian tradition. It is not a physical body, just a calculated point. It is read as appetite and direction: the area of life that pulls hard, moves fast, and is rarely satisfied."},{term:'progressed Sun',definition:"A symbolic method where each day after your birth stands for one year of your life. So the Sun moves about one degree a year and changes sign about every thirty years. When your progressed Sun changes sign, it marks a slow shift in what your life is organised around."},...t.GLOSSARY_EXTRA]},827,[828]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PLANET_FUNCTION",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"ASPECT_TYPE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TIGHTNESS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"HOUSE_MEANING",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"HOUSE_TYPE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return h}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"HEMISPHERE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return u}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DOMINANT_ELEMENT",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"DOMINANT_MODALITY",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return c}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"MODALITY_LACK",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return p}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"RETROGRADE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return f}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"NODE_NOTE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return y}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PATTERN_EXTRA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return b}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_PLANET",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return w}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TRANSIT_NOTE",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return T}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"GLOSSARY_EXTRA",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return v}});const t={Sun:'core identity and drive',Moon:'feelings and needs',Mercury:'thinking and speech',Venus:'love, taste and values',Mars:'drive, anger and desire',Jupiter:'growth, belief and luck',Saturn:'discipline, limits and responsibility',Uranus:'need for freedom and change',Neptune:'imagination, ideals and blur',Pluto:'power, depth and intensity',Ascendant:'rising sign, the way you come across',Midheaven:'public role and direction',Rahu:'North Node, the direction of growth'},o={conjunction:{verb:'is joined to',feel:'The two blend into one drive and are hard to pull apart.'},opposition:{verb:'faces',feel:'The two pull in opposite directions, and you tend to feel it through other people.'},trine:{verb:'flows with',feel:'The two work together easily, so the ability is natural and easy to take for granted.'},square:{verb:'clashes with',feel:'The two push against each other. The friction is uncomfortable and it drives you to act.'},sextile:{verb:'supports',feel:'The two help each other when you use them, but it takes a little effort to switch it on.'}},n={exact:'within 1 degree, the strongest kind',tight:'under 3 degrees, strong',moderate:'under 5 degrees, noticeable',wide:'over 5 degrees, a looser link'},s=[{name:'Self',topics:'your body, appearance and the way you start things'},{name:'Money',topics:'money, possessions and what you value'},{name:'Mind and nearby',topics:'siblings, speech, learning and short trips'},{name:'Home',topics:'home, family and your roots'},{name:'Joy',topics:'romance, children, play and creativity'},{name:'Work',topics:'daily work, health habits and service'},{name:'Partners',topics:'marriage, close partners and open rivals'},{name:'Shared and deep',topics:'shared money, intimacy, loss and change'},{name:'Beliefs',topics:'long travel, higher learning, beliefs and meaning'},{name:'Public life',topics:'career, reputation and your public role'},{name:'Groups',topics:'friends, groups, hopes and gains'},{name:'Hidden',topics:'solitude, rest, hidden things and what you keep out of sight'}],h={angular:'Angular houses (1st, 4th, 7th, 10th) are the corners of the chart. Planets here are visible and act fast. A chart weighted this way tends to start things and be seen doing it.',succedent:'Succedent houses (2nd, 5th, 8th, 11th) are about building and keeping. A chart weighted this way tends to hold on to what it makes and works steadily on resources.',cadent:'Cadent houses (3rd, 6th, 9th, 12th) are about learning, adjusting and thinking. A chart weighted this way tends to process and refine more than it pushes forward.'},u={above:'Seven or more planets sit above the horizon (houses 7 to 12). The weight of the chart is on public life, other people and what shows.',below:'Seven or more planets sit below the horizon (houses 1 to 6). The weight of the chart is on the private and personal: home, body, inner life and daily work.',east:'Seven or more planets sit in the eastern half (houses 10, 11, 12, 1, 2, 3). The chart leans toward self-direction: you set the course and others adapt.',west:'Seven or more planets sit in the western half (houses 4 to 9). The chart leans toward responding: your path is shaped through other people and circumstances.'},l={Fire:'Fire leads your chart. You run on enthusiasm and action and you start things fast. The cost is patience: you can burn out, or burn through people.',Earth:'Earth leads your chart. You trust what is practical, physical and proven, and you build slowly. The cost is flexibility: change you did not choose is hard on you.',Air:'Air leads your chart. You run on ideas, talk and connection, and you see more than one side. The cost is follow-through: thinking can stand in for doing.',Water:'Water leads your chart. You run on feeling and take in the mood of every room. The cost is boundaries: other people\'s weather becomes yours.'},c={Cardinal:'Cardinal leads your chart. You are built to start things and set direction. The cost is the middle: holding a project steady after the first push can bore you.',Fixed:'Fixed leads your chart. You hold position, finish what you commit to and resist pressure. The cost is change: you can hold on past the point where it helps.',Mutable:'Mutable leads your chart. You adapt, switch and take in new input easily. The cost is direction: you can bend to every situation and lose your own line.'},p={Cardinal:'No planet of yours is Cardinal. Starting something from nothing is not your natural move. You do better when something is already in motion.',Fixed:'No planet of yours is Fixed. Holding a position under pressure is not your natural move. You change course easily, which is a strength and a weakness.',Mutable:'No planet of yours is Mutable. Adapting to change you did not choose costs you more than it costs most people. You prefer a plan.'},f={Mercury:'Mercury was retrograde at your birth. You think inward first and speak later. Your thinking can look slow or odd from outside, and you often rework an idea before you share it.',Venus:'Venus was retrograde at your birth. You take longer to know what you want in love and money, and you tend to revisit what you valued. Your tastes are private.',Mars:'Mars was retrograde at your birth. Drive and anger turn inward first, so you may hold back and then act in bursts. Direct confrontation does not come naturally.',Jupiter:'Jupiter was retrograde at your birth. Your beliefs and growth come more from inside than from teachers or rules. You build your own sense of meaning.',Saturn:'Saturn was retrograde at your birth. Your relationship with rules and authority is internal: you set strict standards for yourself and push back on standards set by others.',Uranus:'Uranus was retrograde at your birth. This is true for about five months of every year, so many people share it. It colours how you experience change and freedom more than it sets you apart.',Neptune:'Neptune was retrograde at your birth. This is true for about five months of every year, so many people share it. It colours your ideals and imagination from the inside.',Pluto:'Pluto was retrograde at your birth. This is true for about five months of every year, so many people share it. It colours how you handle power and depth from the inside.'},y='The idea of the North Node as a direction of growth and the South Node as the familiar past comes from modern astrology. Older traditions read the nodes as points of eclipse that add or take away. The app uses the mean node.',b={yod:'A yod (sometimes called the finger of God) is two planets that support each other, both pointing awkwardly at a third. The apex planet is asked to adjust again and again, and it often feels like a task you were handed.',kite:'A kite is a grand trine with a fourth planet that opposes one corner and supports the other two. It gives the easy talent of the trine a direction and a reason to be used.',grandCross:'A grand cross is four planets in square and opposition to each other. It holds a lot of tension from every side at once, which makes you capable and tired. Most people with one learn to work with pressure as the normal state.',none:'No yod, kite or grand cross is present. Patterns are shown only when the angles are close enough to count.'},w={Jupiter:{effect:'Jupiter opens things up and adds room, support and appetite.',cycle:'about a year in each sign'},Saturn:{effect:'Saturn tests, slows things down and asks for structure.',cycle:'about two and a half years in each sign'},Uranus:{effect:'Uranus shakes things loose and pushes toward change and freedom.',cycle:'about seven years in each sign'},Neptune:{effect:'Neptune softens certainty. Ideals rise and so does confusion.',cycle:'about fourteen years in each sign'},Pluto:{effect:'Pluto presses on whatever is hidden or controlling and forces a deep rebuild.',cycle:'twelve to thirty years in each sign'}},T='Transits are read from the planets\' real positions today against your birth chart, using tropical signs. Orbs: 3 degrees (2 for sextiles). Retrograde passes can touch the same point three times.',v=[{term:'orb',definition:'How far an angle between two planets is from exact, in degrees. A smaller orb means a stronger link. Under 1 degree is very tight; past 5 degrees the link is loose.'},{term:'quincunx',definition:'Two planets about 150 degrees apart. They share no element or mode, so they have little in common and keep having to adjust to each other. It is the angle that builds a yod.'},{term:'yod',definition:'Two planets about 60 degrees apart that each sit about 150 degrees from a third. The third planet (the apex) is asked to adjust to both.'},{term:'kite',definition:'A grand trine plus a fourth planet opposite one corner and in sextile to the other two. It gives the trine a focus.'},{term:'grand cross',definition:'Four planets about 90 degrees apart, forming two oppositions and four squares. It carries tension from every side at once.'},{term:'angular house',definition:'The 1st, 4th, 7th and 10th houses, the four corners of the chart. Planets here are visible and act quickly.'},{term:'succedent house',definition:'The 2nd, 5th, 8th and 11th houses. They are about building, keeping and resources.'},{term:'cadent house',definition:'The 3rd, 6th, 9th and 12th houses. They are about learning, adjusting and thinking.'},{term:'retrograde',definition:'A planet that looks as if it is moving backward against the stars, because of the angle between its orbit and ours. In a birth chart it is read as that planet working more inward.'},{term:'South Node',definition:'The point exactly opposite the North Node. Modern astrology reads it as the familiar past: skills and habits that feel easy and can be overused.'},{term:'modality',definition:'The three modes of the signs. Cardinal signs start things, Fixed signs hold them and Mutable signs adapt them.'}]},828,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,_e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(_e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),_e.jaiminiFacts=function(t){const u=t.jyotish;return[e('4th from your Sun',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Sun',4),n.FOURTH_FROM_SUN),e('4th from your Moon',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Moon',4),n.FOURTH_FROM_MOON),e('3rd from your Moon',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Moon',3),n.THIRD_FROM_MOON),e('4th from your Mercury',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Mercury',4),n.FOURTH_FROM_MERCURY),e('4th from your Venus',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Venus',4),n.FOURTH_FROM_VENUS),e('4th from your Mars',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Mars',4),n.FOURTH_FROM_MARS),e('8th from your Mars',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Mars',8),n.EIGHTH_FROM_MARS),e('4th from your Jupiter',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Jupiter',4),n.FOURTH_FROM_JUPITER),e('4th from your Saturn',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Saturn',4),n.FOURTH_FROM_SATURN),e('10th from your Saturn',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Saturn',10),n.TENTH_FROM_SATURN,!0),e('4th from your Rahu',(0,o.countedPoint)(u,'Rahu',4),n.FOURTH_FROM_RAHU)]};var o=r(d[0]),t=r(d[1]),n=r(d[2]),u=r(d[3]);const e=(o,n,e,R=!1)=>{const M=e[R?n.landedSign:n.fromSign];return{k:o,v:t.SIGNS[n.landedSign],t:M.text,full:(0,u.detailOf)(M)}}},829,[830,798,831,812]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";function n(n,t,o){return((o?(n+11)%12:n)+t-1)%12}Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),e.countFrom=n,e.countedPoint=function(t,o,u){const c=t.placements.find(n=>n.body===o),s=c.retrograde&&'Rahu'!==o&&'Ketu'!==o,f=n(c.sign,u,s),l=t.placements.filter(n=>n.sign===f&&n.body!==o).map(n=>n.body);return{from:o,fromSign:c.sign,landedSign:f,occupants:l}}},830,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"FOURTH_FROM_MOON",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"THIRD_FROM_MOON",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"FOURTH_FROM_SATURN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TENTH_FROM_SATURN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return s}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"FOURTH_FROM_SUN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"FOURTH_FROM_MERCURY",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return h}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"FOURTH_FROM_VENUS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return u}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"FOURTH_FROM_JUPITER",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return c}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"FOURTH_FROM_MARS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return f}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"EIGHTH_FROM_MARS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return y}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"FOURTH_FROM_RAHU",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return p}});const t={0:{text:'You find comfort in an orderly home: the house, land, and a working bond with your mother. When you neglect it, your body usually feels the strain first.',detail:'Your Moon is fed by home and by whoever plays the mother role for you. That means an orderly house, a stable base, and land or property of your own. When this part of life is left alone, the strain tends to show in your body before your mood. Build your home on purpose instead of letting it happen around you. That is the direct way back to ease.'},1:{text:'You find comfort in what you make and teach: children, students, a body of creative work. Effort here usually pays you in cash flow, not applause.',detail:'Raising or teaching the next generation feeds you. So does a creative practice, a body of knowledge you keep building, or time given to children or students. Money also tends to follow your effort here. Put your attention in this area and income tends to come after it, sometimes with a delay.'},2:{text:'You find comfort in being useful when things are hard, like solving someone\u2019s problem or pushing your body through a tough patch. Being useful matters more than being admired.',detail:'Your Moon settles through service. That looks like daily competitive effort, helping colleagues or clients through a real struggle, or hands-on fixing. It rarely looks glamorous, and that is the point. The comfort is in being useful, not in being seen doing it.'},3:{text:'You find comfort in partnership and shared ventures, like a marriage or a business you start with someone. It works better for you than anything built alone.',detail:'A spouse, a business partner, or a second property bought together: real partnership feeds this Moon. Dealing with the public and one-to-one commitment settle you in a way solo effort doesn\u2019t. The comfort grows when you treat the partnership as a real working team, not a backdrop.'},4:{text:'You find comfort in going below the surface: research, real change, and study that isn\u2019t meant to be quick.',detail:'Deep work feeds this Moon. That means research, occult or forensic subjects, and anything where you sit with something uncomfortable until it changes. Repeating surface tasks doesn\u2019t reach it. A real breakthrough does.'},5:{text:'You find comfort in higher study and in having someone to learn from, like a mentor or teacher. It works better than figuring things out alone.',detail:'Higher learning feeds this placement, formal or informal. So does a bond with a guru (a spiritual teacher) or mentor, and travel taken to learn rather than to relax. Naming a teacher and keeping one tends to matter more for you than for most.'},6:{text:'You find comfort in responsibility people can see, like a public role or a duty done in the open. It suits you more than private wins.',detail:'This Moon settles through career, public standing, and the duty of doing work where others see it. It asks you to engage with the wider world, not pull away from it. That holds even when it feels uncomfortable at first.'},7:{text:'You find comfort in group effort: organising, sharing what you\u2019ve found, and working for a cause with other people. It suits you more than working alone.',detail:'Friend and work networks, group projects, and causes bigger than one person feed this Moon. Sharing what you know, rather than keeping it to yourself, is often what settles you.'},8:{text:'You find comfort in real time alone, not just quiet. You also gain from what you\u2019ve already put aside.',detail:'Retreat, privacy, and distance from company feed this placement. It has a money side too: savings, investment and banking, where gains come from patience rather than activity. Constant company tends to work against this Moon, even when it looks sociable from outside.'},9:{text:'You find comfort by looking after yourself first: your body, your looks, your own condition. Do this before trying to fix anything else.',detail:'Self-care, fitness, and simply looking after how you look and feel feed this Moon. Others may see it as vanity. From the inside it\u2019s closer to maintenance. The rest of life tends to follow once you keep this up.'},10:{text:'You find comfort in real closeness, with family or friends that go past the surface. You also find it in using your voice to help, not to perform.',detail:'Deep relationships feed this Moon more than wide ones. So does using your voice to speak or heal in a way that steadies someone else. Shallow socialising doesn\u2019t reach it. A few real bonds and a use for your voice do.'},11:{text:'You find comfort in making things, like writing, art or any hands-on creative work. You also find it with the people you grew up alongside.',detail:'Creative or written work, media, and physical effort feed this placement. So does closeness with siblings, or people who feel like siblings. Making something real tends to settle this Moon faster than thinking about making it.'}},o={0:{text:'Physical effort switches this Moon on. Move your body, travel, and work with your hands alongside other people.',detail:'When your drive stalls, activity restarts it. Try exercise, a short or long trip, a hands-on creative task, or working in a team instead of alone. Your mind tends to follow your body here, not lead it.'},1:{text:'A clean, orderly home switches this Moon on. Tidy your space, look after a car or property, and spend time with your mother.',detail:'It sounds small. Working from home, keeping the house in order, looking after a car or property, and staying close to your mother all help. For this placement, that is what actually gets you going.'},2:{text:'Time with children, or a turn at something creative, switches this Moon on. It helps to be the one with a working answer, not the one asking.',detail:'Spend time with children, do creative or performing work, and offer solutions out loud instead of staying quiet. Being useful out loud tends to do more for you than private effort.'},3:{text:'Focusing on health and plain, unglamorous service switches this Moon on. Think volunteering, direct competition, and the daily work of caring for your body.',detail:'Attention to health, service that asks nothing back, and facing rivals or competition head-on instead of avoiding them. That is what gets this placement moving.'},4:{text:'Partnership switches this Moon on. A real business talk, a step toward marriage, or working with someone instead of alone all help.',detail:'Starting a business or chasing a business idea switches this placement on. So do partnership talks that move a private idea into a shared commitment.'},5:{text:'The occult, research, or any study that changes you switches this Moon on. This is work that changes how you see, not just what you know.',detail:'Mystical or research-based study is what switches you on here. The best kind reorganises what you already believe instead of just adding to it.'},6:{text:'Higher learning switches this Moon on. Find a mentor, take on real study, or travel to learn.',detail:'Seeking a guru (a spiritual teacher) or other teacher helps. So does higher education, formal or not, or a pilgrimage-style trip. Your drive tends to rise when someone further ahead is there to learn from.'},7:{text:'Taking on responsibility switches this Moon on. Step into authority or build something, even a small side venture.',detail:'Work, leadership, or building your own venture switches you on, however small it starts. Your drive tends to follow the responsibility you take on, not the other way round.'},8:{text:'Being around people switches this Moon on. Try a group, a conference, a public conversation, or a wider network.',detail:'Joining groups, speaking in public, and networking with people working on similar things all switch this placement on.'},9:{text:'Time alone switches this Moon on. You need real retreat, proper sleep, and private time no one else can claim.',detail:'Pulling back, resting, and restoring yourself alone are what switch you on. Pushing through without them tends to dull your drive instead of sharpening it.'},10:{text:'Paying attention to how you present yourself switches this Moon on. Fitness, grooming, and showing up looking like yourself all help.',detail:'How you present yourself and your physical condition switch this placement on. Your drive in other areas tends to lag until you\u2019ve looked after this first.'},11:{text:'Food and real conversation switch this Moon on. An honest one-to-one talk, care about what you eat, and a look at your money all help.',detail:'Close conversation, food, and a plain look at your spending and saving switch you on. Small, private and concrete works better for you than public or abstract.'}},n={0:{text:'You look for ease at home. The catch is a bond with your mother that stays a little cold, however much you give.',detail:'This placement seeks comfort through service, hosting, land or work based at home. Alongside it, your bond with your mother rarely warms as much as your effort deserves. Sacrifices you make for home and family after committing to a partner also often go unthanked. The effort is still worth making. The thanks just come on their own timetable, not yours.'},1:{text:'You look for fulfilment in raising or teaching the next generation. The catch is that thanks come late, if at all.',detail:'This placement puts real effort into raising and educating children, hoping for the happiness that should come with it. Children can grow emotionally distant as adults despite that effort. Mental or spiritual work here also tends to take a long time to show results. It can feel unnoticed for a long while, even when it isn\u2019t wasted.'},2:{text:'You look for fulfilment in working on your own terms. The catch is that you get little credit for the effort it takes.',detail:'You prefer independence at work over serving someone else\u2019s system, and you look for satisfaction there. Credit tends to lag behind your effort anyway. There is also often some unresolved distance with an aunt or uncle on your mother\u2019s side.'},3:{text:'You look for fulfilment in marriage and public partnership. The catch is a spouse or partner who doesn\u2019t always match what you put in.',detail:'You find real meaning in marriage, business partnership and public life. Alongside it, your spouse may not give back equally. Being visible brings public scrutiny. Business partners can hold back information or later become rivals. It\u2019s still worth continuing. It just isn\u2019t guaranteed to be met evenly.'},4:{text:'You look for fulfilment in hidden or spiritual knowledge. The catch is that it never quite feels finished.',detail:'You are drawn to the occult, deep research and the mystical, subjects that reward going deep. The satisfaction you find there tends to stay incomplete. Warmth or support from in-laws can also be thinner than you expect.'},5:{text:'You look for fulfilment in teaching, counselling or travel. The catch is distance from the very mentors who shaped you.',detail:'You find meaning in advising, publishing, or travel taken to learn. Alongside that, a guru (a spiritual teacher), mentor or father figure tends to drift away or disappoint you. The pattern is specific: formally calling someone \u2018my guru\u2019 often comes before some kind of separation. That isn\u2019t because the bond failed. The role itself has a shelf life for you.'},6:{text:'You look for fulfilment in career and public standing. The catch is that the credit rarely matches the effort.',detail:'You put a lot into your work and public reputation, expecting credit to follow. It usually doesn\u2019t come at the scale you expect. You are drawn to public roles, and criticism tends to come with them. What bothers you is the gap between effort and credit, not the work itself.'},7:{text:'You look for fulfilment through groups and through wanting things. The catch is that getting what you wanted rarely feels how you expected.',detail:'You seek satisfaction through organisations, starting ventures, and a wide social circle, and you often get what you go after. The joy you expected often doesn\u2019t fully land when it arrives. Warmth from your social circle can be thinner than hoped. Closeness with an older sibling doesn\u2019t always grow the way it might.'},8:{text:'You look for fulfilment in spiritual practice. The catch is not quite feeling what everyone else says they feel.',detail:'You turn to spirituality, mentors or pilgrimage for a certain satisfaction, and often don\u2019t feel it the way others describe. Sleep can be restless. Even close intimacy doesn\u2019t always bring the depth you hoped for. The upside is that, since you aren\u2019t chasing the high yourself, you can be very good at guiding other people toward theirs.'},9:{text:'You look for fulfilment in how you are seen. The catch is feeling your image is never quite enough, whatever you\u2019ve achieved.',detail:'You can achieve a lot and still feel unsettled about how you look, how you\u2019re seen, or what it adds up to. The problem is how you see yourself, not your record. The achievements are usually real. The feeling of being enough just doesn\u2019t arrive on time.'},10:{text:'You look for fulfilment through money. The catch is that money brings its own complaint.',detail:'You seek satisfaction through finance, banking, speculation or family wealth. Even when you succeed, money brings its own frustration. That can be a loss in a settlement, or a nagging sense of not-quite-enough that stays even when you have plenty.'},11:{text:'You put your fulfilment into communication. The catch is that it rarely comes back as warmly as you give it.',detail:'You put real effort into writing, speaking or staying in touch, looking for connection through it. Your style tends to be blunt: true, but not gentle. Siblings are often on good terms with you but tend to live far away. Close friends stay few rather than many.'}},s={0:{text:'Your best path runs through facing dishonesty head-on. Name fraud, refuse to look away, and act the moment it matters instead of waiting.',detail:'This asks you to act early and on time, not to wait patiently. Take the leadership role instead of the safe seat. Be willing to take on a defining fight for something that matters. Waiting for the perfect moment tends to work against you here. At your best, you move first.'},1:{text:'Your best path runs through creating real value for others: output, products, or income that feeds someone besides you.',detail:'This isn\u2019t about earning a wage. It\u2019s about giving others something they can use, sell, or build on. Your speech carries weight too. Your ability to inspire with words tends to grow alongside your ability to produce.'},2:{text:'Your best path runs through speech that rallies people: practical, logical talk used to guide or inspire others.',detail:'This is about putting communication to work. It isn\u2019t talk for its own sake. It\u2019s the kind that organises a room, makes a case, or gets people moving the same way.'},3:{text:'Your best path runs through moving fast and decisively toward openings. It also means making new things again and again, not resting on the last one.',detail:'Hesitating costs you more than most people. At your best, you spot an opening and act on it quickly. Then you repeat the process instead of treating one success as the finish line.'},4:{text:'Your best path runs through being reliable. Show up, keep your word, and be the person others can set their watch by.',detail:'This builds slowly. Being on time and consistent adds up to standing over the years. Mentoring or raising others, such as children, students or junior staff, tends to be part of the same thread. It rewards steadiness more than any single big effort.'},5:{text:'Your best path runs through competition. Enter high-stakes, hostile ground and hold your own there.',detail:'Avoiding rivals, disputes or hard settings tends to block this path rather than protect you. Show up for the contest and use it to solve other people\u2019s problems along the way. That is where your best self lives.'},6:{text:'Your best path runs through work good enough to be paid what it\u2019s worth. Stay easy to reach while you do it.',detail:'Quality matters more than volume here. A spouse or close collaborator often helps directly. This path also asks for humility: stay in direct, one-to-one contact with people, however high you rise.'},7:{text:'Your best path runs through quiet work: research, change, and developing or fixing things behind the scenes.',detail:'Keeping things quiet is part of the method, not an obstacle. Think confidential or specialist work that changes a system without needing an audience.'},8:{text:'Your best path runs through passing on knowledge by teaching or counselling, held to a real ethical standard.',detail:'This is less about the subject you teach and more about teaching it honestly. Religious or pilgrimage-style activity tends to support and clarify the direction. But the path itself is about teaching well, not about the travel.'},9:{text:'Your best path runs through steady, hands-on effort that also creates work or chances for other people.',detail:'This is built at community scale, not global scale. It means solid, disciplined help for the people actually around you. Keep it up long enough and it becomes something others can rely on.'},10:{text:'Your best path runs through designing solutions for large groups: advocacy, organising, and work that serves many people at once.',detail:'This asks you to be legitimate. Do real advocacy or organising for a wide group. Don\u2019t run a scheme that uses the group\u2019s trust for a narrower goal.'},11:{text:'Your best path runs through removing a barrier for someone else. Give people access to a tool, a freedom or a resource they didn\u2019t have.',detail:'This placement opens doors. At your best, you make something that used to need money, status or connections available to people without them. Access is the gift here, not charity in general.'}},l={0:{text:'You feel fulfilled by building a home and land of your own, with real backing from family or homeland.',detail:'Your Sun here is satisfied by property, a settled home, and support from your family or where you come from. Building that base feeds a sense of purpose nothing else quite reaches.'},1:{text:'You feel fulfilled by learning more and by carrying on the family line. Study and children feed the same drive.',detail:'Ongoing education and the next generation are where this Sun finds satisfaction. Learning and legacy are linked for you. Each one makes you feel the effort is going somewhere.'},2:{text:'You feel fulfilled through effort and struggle: your own, and helping others through theirs.',detail:'Hands-on work satisfies this Sun. So does standing by people through a problem or an illness. Ease doesn\u2019t feed it the way earned effort does.'},3:{text:'You feel fulfilled through marriage and partnership, and it tends to come with real public recognition.',detail:'Running a household, a business partnership, and a public presence all settle this Sun. It\u2019s built to be seen inside a committed setup, not to stay private.'},4:{text:'You feel fulfilled through real change: breaking out of whatever has gone stale, and studying what\u2019s hidden under things.',detail:'Depth feeds this Sun. That means occult or hidden study, and being willing to leave a stuck situation instead of staying comfortable in it.'},5:{text:'You feel fulfilled through higher learning and a real mentor: a guru bond, formal study, or travel taken to learn.',detail:'Naming a teacher, such as a guru (a spiritual teacher), and pursuing higher education feed this Sun directly. Pilgrimage-style travel, taken for what it teaches, is part of the same drive.'},6:{text:'You feel fulfilled only after starting lower than you expected. You have to earn your rise from the bottom, not be handed it from the top.',detail:'Career success satisfies this Sun, but only the kind built up from a humbling start. Skipping that stage tends to leave the success feeling hollow later.'},7:{text:'You feel fulfilled by going after what you want openly and organising the people around you into a real network.',detail:'Following through on what you actually want feeds this Sun. So does building and looking after a social or work circle instead of leaving it loose.'},8:{text:'You feel fulfilled through giving and through time alone. The wisdom you find there matters more than money.',detail:'Charity and time alone feed this Sun in a way that piling up things doesn\u2019t. The satisfaction is in what you learn or let go of, not in what you keep.'},9:{text:'You need to look after yourself first: health, self-care, and personal integrity. Only then does public authority mean anything.',detail:'This Sun needs its own base looked after before status feels good. Skipping self-care to chase authority tends to undercut the very thing you\u2019re chasing.'},10:{text:'You feel fulfilled through family duty, honest speech and money discipline, the plain parts of providing.',detail:'Showing up for family duties, speaking plainly, and keeping money disciplined feed this Sun. The satisfaction is quiet, not public.'},11:{text:'You feel fulfilled through creative self-expression and communication. You have to earn it through real effort, not a lucky break.',detail:'Media, writing, or any hard-won creative work feed this Sun. Easy or speculative gains don\u2019t reach it the way work you really worked for does.'}},h={0:{text:'Your hidden skill is warmth one-to-one. You make people comfortable enough to actually talk to you.',detail:'Private, warm communication is where your mind is truly skilled. It\u2019s a host\u2019s kind of skill that helps a stranger relax. It\u2019s quieter than it sounds, and it\u2019s valuable.'},1:{text:'Your hidden skill is advice that pays. You solve people\u2019s money problems with words that land.',detail:'You have a natural knack for managing money or advising on it, where the right words bring someone a real gain. The same gift can cut both ways, so use it with care.'},2:{text:'Your hidden skill is a critic\u2019s eye. You spot exactly what\u2019s wrong and say so, putting logic over feelings.',detail:'Your mind is gifted at refining, correcting, and pointing out a flaw precisely. You tend to want proof, not a comforting story. That makes you useful wherever accuracy matters more than tact.'},3:{text:'Your hidden skill is running a business or service with a warmth that feels almost motherly.',detail:'You are built to run a high-quality client relationship or service the way a good home is run. You are attentive and truly care about the person on the other end.'},4:{text:'Your hidden skill is discovery, a chemist\u2019s instinct for working out how things really work.',detail:'Your mind has its edge in research, change, and a pull toward the occult or mystical. This works best as a practice you keep coming back to, not a one-off curiosity.'},5:{text:'Your hidden skill is teaching plus strategy. You can mentor people and out-think them at the same time.',detail:'Your real strength is a mind built for managing, teaching or debating. You also have a knack for strategy in the broad sense: persuading, planning and competing.'},6:{text:'Your hidden skill is building something that employs other people, rather than doing all the work yourself.',detail:'You are most gifted when you apply a technical or mechanical mind to a business that serves people and puts others to work. That suits you more than solo, hands-on output.'},7:{text:'Your hidden skill sits somewhere between hard science and mysticism, and both halves are real.',detail:'You have a knack for science, astrology or cosmology. It often comes with two sides: part sceptic, part believer. Both sides tend to help you rather than clash.'},8:{text:'Your hidden skill is speaking about life\u2019s big questions. It only matures through what you\u2019ve lived, not what you\u2019ve read.',detail:'Book knowledge alone won\u2019t get you there. Direct experience, including time alone, is what turns this into a real skill instead of a borrowed opinion.'},9:{text:'Your hidden skill is physical. Your body masters it through training, not through reasoning.',detail:'You have a deep knack for sport or physical skill. If early learning or speech ever felt slow, physical training often fixes it, not more study.'},10:{text:'Your hidden skill is creative and musical. It comes paired with a knack for managing money, your own or a household\u2019s.',detail:'Your mind is strongest in art or music. That comes paired with a real skill for managing money, whether it\u2019s your own or a whole household\u2019s.'},11:{text:'Your hidden skill is turning raw material into something new: data, writing, or any message built from scratch.',detail:'Your real strength is turning ideas or raw information into a finished piece of work others can follow. It\u2019s closer to a craft than a talent, and it rewards practice.'}},u={0:{text:'An orderly, well-kept home switches on your enjoyment. Your car and your house both matter more than they seem to.',detail:'Order at home feeds this Venus. A spotless home and a well-kept car aren\u2019t vanity for you. They\u2019re how comfort and luxury actually settle in.'},1:{text:'Creative self-expression, including raising children, brings you comfort and wealth. So does speech that carries weight.',detail:'Creative work and carrying on a family line both feed this Venus. Learning and speech become real paths to wealth here, not just ways to express yourself.'},2:{text:'You feel fulfilled through work that serves people: healing, mediation, law, medicine, or standing up for those with less power.',detail:'This Venus settles through helping jobs: settling conflicts, medicine, advocacy. The comfort comes from being truly useful to people who need it, not from status alone.'},3:{text:'This is one of the strongest versions of this placement. You feel fulfilled directly through marriage and partnership, with home and luxury built around one committed bond.',detail:'Libra is Venus\u2019s own sign, so classical astrology counts this as strong. For you, the marriage itself, not anything built alone, is the direct path to comfort, home and money ease.'},4:{text:'You feel more fulfilled by exploring hidden or taboo subjects, especially once family life is settled.',detail:'Research, hidden study, or anything seen as off-limits tends to become truly satisfying here. This usually happens after children or a settled family life are in place.'},5:{text:'You need real respect for your lineage: ancestors, a guru, or inherited knowledge. Holding back that respect tends to block your fulfilment.',detail:'Respect for where you came from and for higher knowledge isn\u2019t optional for this Venus. It\u2019s part of how comfort and satisfaction actually arrive.'},6:{text:'Your fulfilment depends on your career. You have to earn this Venus through work before you can enjoy it.',detail:'Marriage, wealth and comfort here are tied to your job and public reputation. You have to work for the luxury. It doesn\u2019t come as a given.'},7:{text:'You feel fulfilled through a private social network. Connections you keep fairly quiet are where your chances really come from.',detail:'Friends and acquaintances feed this Venus, especially when you keep them a little private instead of broadcasting them. Chances to build wealth tend to travel through those ties.'},8:{text:'You feel fulfilled through charity and putting money back in. Giving brings its own return here, and time alone helps it land.',detail:'Time alone and a habit of giving, not only collecting, are where this Venus finds ease. What you give out has a way of coming back.'},9:{text:'Your fulfilment is fully in your own hands. How you present yourself and your condition drive everything else.',detail:'Health, looks and self-presentation aren\u2019t vanity here. They\u2019re how you actually find fulfilment in marriage and money. Look after yourself first.'},10:{text:'You feel fulfilled through honest, appealing speech used at work. Communication is how wealth reaches you.',detail:'Truthful, well-put communication at work feeds this Venus directly. How you speak tends to matter as much as what you say.'},11:{text:'You feel fulfilled by helping siblings and by hands-on creative work. This area takes courage and effort, not waiting.',detail:'This Venus settles when you support brothers, sisters, or people who feel like them, and put real effort into creative work. It rewards showing up, not waiting.'}},c={0:{text:'This Jupiter asks for a sacrifice close to home: family, property, or your bond with your mother.',detail:'A real sacrifice tied to home, land or family tends to come before the contentment this placement is looking for. It\u2019s often big enough to notice. It\u2019s the price of the calm that follows.'},1:{text:'Your sacrifice runs through children and spiritual practice. Wealth here tends to grow only after you give these first.',detail:'Time and energy given to children, learning, or a serious spiritual practice come before the material growth this Jupiter offers. The order matters: sacrifice first, then plenty, not the reverse.'},2:{text:'Your sacrifice runs through serving people who have less than you, sometimes at a real cost to your health.',detail:'Your sacrifice here is duty to people with less, or simply showing up for people in a hard spot. It can cost your health if you ignore it for too long. Fulfilment through communication or teaching follows once you\u2019ve paid it.'},3:{text:'Your sacrifice runs through marriage and business partnership. Home life is often rocky before real stability sets in.',detail:'Your spouse and partnerships carry the cost here. Home life is often unsettled before your marriage finds its footing. Once it does, the satisfaction tends to be complete, not partial.'},4:{text:'Your sacrifice runs through in-laws and money tied to marriage. Deep research or hidden study tends to pay off well for you.',detail:'The cost here is money or resources given toward your marriage, especially involving in-laws. This placement is also good for a knack with hidden subjects or astrology, if you take that path seriously.'},5:{text:'Your sacrifice runs through your bond with a guru or father figure. The hardship is close to a pilgrimage.',detail:'This means demanding, deliberate effort for a mentor or father, sometimes with lots of travel. What it clears in return, like old debts, illness or trouble at work, tends to match what you gave.'},6:{text:'Your sacrifice runs through your career. Marriage depends on sorting out work first.',detail:'Steady work matters more here than religious ritual. Put the effort into your career and stability tends to follow for the partnership, more reliably than the reverse.'},7:{text:'Your sacrifice runs through your social circle and older siblings. It tends to spark a real change in you.',detail:'Acquaintances and extended family draw on your resources. Giving to them tends to trigger big change rather than just draining you.'},8:{text:'Your sacrifice is time alone: retreat and distance from home. Giving more brings more back as wisdom.',detail:'Time away, alone, and a habit of giving rather than only keeping are what this asks. What you let go of tends to come back as understanding, not loss.'},9:{text:'Your sacrifice is ongoing. It\u2019s a long commitment to your career and public role that rarely eases off.',detail:'This placement asks you to keep giving yourself to work and standing. Ignoring the balance tends to show up in your health and in strained family life. So the sacrifice needs a limit, not just acceptance.'},10:{text:'Your wishes come true here when you support your family with money: siblings, parents, and your father\u2019s side.',detail:'Providing for the people linked to your father\u2019s side of the family is how this Jupiter\u2019s wishes actually come true for you.'},11:{text:'Your goals abroad or in spiritual life only come true after you sacrifice for colleagues, siblings or neighbours.',detail:'The bigger goal might be travel, spiritual growth or ambition. It opens up once you first give to people close by: coworkers, siblings, or the people next door.'}},f={0:{text:'This Mars is built to protect home and mother. Stepping back from that duty tends to show up in your own health first.',detail:'Your energy naturally goes toward caring for home and mother. Pulling away here tends to line up with strain on your own health more than with anything outside you.'},1:{text:'This Mars is built to protect your knowledge and judgement. Take care with learning and romance, and don\u2019t overdo food or drink.',detail:'This asks you to use and value what you know, and to pay attention in social or romantic settings. Neglect here tends to show up as overdoing food or drink, not as a big failure.'},2:{text:'This Mars is built to protect coworkers and the people you deal with daily. Your own health needs the same attention.',detail:'Your duty here is to support colleagues, workers, and the people you deal with every day. Pay real attention to your own health too, not only other people\u2019s.'},3:{text:'This Mars is built to protect fairness with a spouse or clients. Neglecting that tends to cost you your peace of mind.',detail:'This asks for fairness and care toward a spouse or clients. Neglect is linked to losing your inner peace and to strain on anything shared, like property you own together.'},4:{text:'This Mars is built for discretion. You are naturally at ease with confidential, specialist knowledge.',detail:'This asks for discretion with sensitive, confidential or specialist knowledge, such as legal, financial or hidden subjects. Work built on confidentiality suits you naturally. It isn\u2019t a burden.'},5:{text:'This Mars is built to protect respect for family tradition, your father and mentors. Ignoring that tends to create friction.',detail:'This asks you to respect family tradition, your father and your mentors. Ignoring them is linked to obstacles and friction that a little respect would have avoided.'},6:{text:'This Mars is built to protect your career and any wealth you inherit. Spend it carefully before it gets spent for you.',detail:'This asks you to protect your career and manage inherited wealth wisely. Neglect is linked to friction in marriage, so the discipline pays off in more than one way.'},7:{text:'This Mars is built to treat your wider social circle fairly, giving as much as you get.',detail:'This asks for fair dealing with your network and extended family. Using these ties for your own gain tends to unsettle other parts of life, not just the relationship.'},8:{text:'This Mars is built for care with spending, and for keeping your spiritual practice and intimate life private.',detail:'This asks for care with investments and spending. It also asks you to keep spiritual practice and intimate matters out of public view.'},9:{text:'This Mars is built for physical discipline and honesty with yourself. Cutting corners here tends to blur your sense of direction.',detail:'This asks for physical discipline and honesty with yourself. Fooling yourself is linked to a foggier sense of career direction, more than to any single failure.'},10:{text:'This Mars is built for careful speech and steady saving. Aim for moderation, not restriction.',detail:'This asks for careful speech, saving habits, and moderation with food and substances. Neglect here tends to wear away the social support you\u2019d otherwise have.'},11:{text:'This Mars is built for fair dealing with siblings and neighbours, and for using your words responsibly.',detail:'This asks for fair dealing with siblings and neighbours and responsible use of your words. Getting it wrong tends to build into isolation and loss rather than fixing itself.'}},y={0:{text:'Pride can lead you to quietly keep in-laws at a distance, or to wave off hidden knowledge that would actually help you.',detail:'This Mars\u2019s independence can lead you to keep in-laws at arm\u2019s length. You may dismiss hidden or inherited knowledge. You may even turn down an inheritance rather than deal with what comes with it.'},1:{text:'Your drive to follow your own path can pull you away from a father or guru figure, sometimes at the cost of formal education.',detail:'Independence and strong personal values can create distance from your father, a guru, or inherited beliefs. It can also mean leaving formal higher education to learn your own way.'},2:{text:'Pride in your skill can lead you to leave jobs or push back on authority rather than work inside someone else\u2019s system.',detail:'This Mars tends to push you toward working for yourself. Sometimes that happens by pushing back on authority or leaving roles that don\u2019t match how capable you feel.'},3:{text:'Putting home and your spouse\u2019s peace first can mean quietly drifting from your wider social circle.',detail:'Keeping peace at home can cost you ties with extended family or friends, especially around shared property.'},4:{text:'Putting children or a spiritual commitment first can mean passing up a chance abroad or an investment, with little regret.',detail:'Learning, children, or a serious spiritual path can mean letting go of inherited property or a chance abroad. It isn\u2019t only a loss. It\u2019s a real trade-off this Mars tends to make willingly.'},5:{text:'Your drive to excel and compete can push your body past what it can sustain.',detail:'A strong urge to win can mean training or working harder than your body can comfortably handle. Watch for it before it becomes the thing that holds you back.'},6:{text:'Putting your spouse first can mean drifting from your birth family, or spending down savings on the relationship.',detail:'Full commitment to a partner can cost you closeness with the family you grew up in. Sometimes it also costs savings spent on the relationship or a move together.'},7:{text:'Guarding something confidential can quietly strain a bond with a sibling, especially if it\u2019s later shared too openly.',detail:'Guarding an inheritance or private matters closely can create tension with a sibling. It often goes badly if the private information is later shared in public instead of handled quietly.'},8:{text:'A real commitment to higher knowledge or a guru path can mean stepping back from comfort at home.',detail:'Taking dharma (your path of duty), study, or a mentor seriously can mean less time and attention for home comforts. This Mars tends to make that trade on purpose, not by accident.'},9:{text:'Full commitment to your career can mean less time with your children. It can come with a disciplined, almost monk-like way of living.',detail:'Career and public duty take up a lot here. That often costs time with children or purely intellectual interests. Sometimes it comes with a strict, focused personal discipline.'},10:{text:'Putting belonging first when you\u2019re young can strain your health. Easing off close ties with relatives on your mother\u2019s side tends to help.',detail:'A strong pull toward fitting in early on can cost you some health if you don\u2019t balance it. Ties with aunts or uncles on your mother\u2019s side often work better with a little distance than with constant closeness.'},11:{text:'Private choices about spending or investing can quietly strain a marriage or business partnership.',detail:'Money or investment decisions you make alone can put real pressure on a shared relationship. Bring them into the open before the pressure builds.'}},p={0:{text:'The gap between what you expect and what happens tends to show up at home: property, cars, or people in your household.',detail:'With Rahu (the Moon\u2019s north node, linked to craving) here, home, mother, property or a car can turn out differently than you expected. This can happen more than once, usually before your early thirties. It\u2019s a pattern to notice, not a warning to fear.'},1:{text:'The gap between what you expect and what happens tends to show up in romance or education.',detail:'A relationship or a course of study linked to this placement can turn out differently than you hoped. Spotting the pattern early tends to soften it.'},2:{text:'The gap between what you expect and what happens tends to show up around health, or a rival who acts like a friend.',detail:'A diagnosis or health reading may need a second look. Someone who seems supportive in a competitive setting isn\u2019t always what they appear to be. Neither is cause for alarm. Just check twice.'},3:{text:'The gap tends to show up with a spouse or business partner. It isn\u2019t always betrayal, just a broken expectation or a promise not kept.',detail:'This isn\u2019t only about cheating. It\u2019s any gap between what a partner said and what they actually did. Naming the gap plainly tends to help more than assuming the worst.'},4:{text:'The gap tends to show up around in-laws, inheritance, or a careless approach to hidden practices.',detail:'Insurance, estate matters, or an occult practice taken up too lightly can turn out more complicated than you expected. A little more care at the start tends to prevent most of it.'},5:{text:'The gap tends to show up with a father figure, a mentor, or something you run into while travelling.',detail:'Your expectations are most likely to miss with your father or a teacher. The same goes for an offer you meet on the road or on pilgrimage.'},6:{text:'The gap tends to show up in your career. The credit you expect doesn\u2019t always arrive when you hoped.',detail:'Your public reputation can come more slowly, or in a different shape, than you expected. This is a timing gap more than a judgement on your work.'},7:{text:'The gap tends to show up through work or social networks: a group or cause that isn\u2019t quite what it claimed to be.',detail:'Look closely at any group you join here, including anything to do with donations. Check it properly before you fully commit to it.'},8:{text:'The gap tends to show up in risky investments or offers from abroad.',detail:'Anything that promises quick or unusually big returns, especially from far away, deserves more checking than it first seems to need.'},9:{text:'The gap tends to be with yourself. You may misjudge your own talent or direction, especially around fame or career.',detail:'This is less about being fooled by someone else. It\u2019s more about a view of yourself that needs updating, especially about what you\u2019re really suited for.'},10:{text:'The gap tends to show up around banks, jewellers, or family money.',detail:'Double-check a bank or a family money matter here rather than taking it at face value.'},11:{text:'The gap tends to show up with siblings, neighbours, or people you meet online.',detail:'A relationship online, or with someone nearby, can turn out differently than it first seemed. As with the other placements here, it\u2019s a pattern to notice, not a reason to pull away.'}}},831,[]);
